GitHub"},"message":"SUPPORT-646: test coverage (JUnit, Jest, Cypress incl. SEC-1 stored-XSS guard) (#14)\n\n* test: pin shipped default OSGi config resource (G-J1)\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n\n* test: cover StatuspageIoBanner DOM/security, locales, and JS validator divergence (G-Je1-10)\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n\n* test: fix G-C3 back-office banner reveal to assert the origin-guard negative\n\nThe existing reveal test posted a showFrame message from the Cypress app\nwindow, but StatuspageIoBanner.js enforces\nevent.origin === ''https://<pageId>.statuspage.io'' before acting, so that\npath can never fire — the old expect(right).to.equal(''60px'') was an\nunreachable, non-exercising (flaky) assertion. Replaced with the honest\nnegative: the cross-origin message is ignored and the iframe stays at its\ninitial -9999px. The matching-origin reveal path is unit-tested in Jest\n(G-Je6) where MessageEvent.origin is controllable.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n\n* test: add SEC-1 stored-XSS regression guard for per-node widget pageId\n\nThe per-node widget pageId has no server-side write validation (CND mandatory\nbut unconstrained, no save listener), so the JSP render-path char-allowlist\n[a-z0-9-], length 1-63 is the SOLE guard against stored XSS via the unescaped\ninline var pageId=''${pageId}'' / iframe host. This spec persists genuinely\nunsafe pageIds (quote/script-tag breakout, host swap via . / @ / //, uppercase,\n>63 chars) and proves none render: no Jahia Status iframe, statusEmbedTest hook\nundefined, injected alert never fires, raw payload absent from the served DOM —\ncontrasted with a valid pageId that DOES inject correctly. Fails loudly if the\nallowlist ever loosens. Stage 7 handoff: add write-side validation (CND\nconstraint / save listener / output escaping) via a shared pageId regex so the\ndefense is not render-only (also resolves the D7 divergent-validators finding).\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n\n* test: fix SEC-1 cleanup so malicious-pageId assertions are non-vacuous\n\nThe removeWidget helper deleted the widget node via cy.request with basic\nauth, which Jahia''s API security filter denies (GqlAccessDeniedException).\nThe node was therefore never removed; because every case reused one node\nname, only the first addChild succeeded and the rest failed silently with\nItemExistsException (cy.apollo swallows GraphQL errors). Six of seven\nnegative cases asserted against a stale node instead of their own payload,\nand the positive control never got a valid widget, so it failed.\n\nFix: delete via cy.apollo (authenticated session, passes the security\nfilter) like spec 02, give each case a unique node name, and publish the\nparent after each add to flush the footer-1 area output cache so the\nfreshly-created node actually renders. All 8 cases now pass and every\nnegative assertion genuinely exercises the JSP render-path allowlist.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n\n* fix: validate widget pageId at write time via CND value constraint\n\nThe per-node jnt:statuspageIoWidget/pageId property was CND-declared mandatory\nbut had no value constraint and no save-time JCR validation, so any string\npersisted. The sole guard against stored XSS was the JSP render-path allowlist\nin statuspageIoWidget.jsp -- a single render-path point of failure.\n\nAdd a JCR value constraint ''[a-z0-9-]{1,63}'' on pageId, kept IDENTICAL to that\nJSP allowlist, so JCR rejects an unsafe value at setValue/save time with a\nConstraintViolationException (the addStatuspageIoWidget mutation now returns an\nerror and no node is persisted). The JSP allowlist is retained as the matching\nrender-side layer -> defense in depth (write + render), not render-only.\n\nThe SEC-1 spec (04-statuspageIoWidgetXss.cy.ts) is extended: each malicious\npageId now asserts the write is rejected (constraint-violation error) AND that\nnothing renders; the valid pageId positive control still persists and renders.\n\nD7 residual (documented in the CND comment, not fixed here): the global\nOSGi-config path uses a stricter DNS regex and the JS util is looser (allows\nuppercase); a single shared constant across CND/Java/JSP/JS is not achievable\nand is left as a maintainer follow-up.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n\n* chore(deps): add @testing-library/dom devDependency\n\n@testing-library/react@16 declares @testing-library/dom (^10) as a peer\ndependency, but it was absent from both package.json and yarn.lock. Classic\nyarn v1 (used by the module build via frontend-maven-plugin) does not\nauto-install peer deps, so the pre-existing StatuspageIoConfigPanel.test.jsx\nJest suite failed to load (''Cannot find module @testing-library/dom'').\n\nAdd @testing-library/dom@^10.0.0 to devDependencies and regenerate yarn.lock\nwith the project-pinned classic yarn v1.22.21 (resolves to 10.4.1 + transitive\ndeps). All 4 Jest suites now load and pass (56 tests).\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n\n* docs: align version to pom (1.0.3-SNAPSHOT) and fix AGENTS.md permission name\n\n- package.json version 1.0.2 -> 1.0.3-SNAPSHOT to match pom.xml (source of\n  truth); resolves the D3 version drift (pom/package.json/AGENTS.md disagreed).\n- AGENTS.md version 1.0.1 -> 1.0.3-SNAPSHOT.\n- AGENTS.md: mutation requires ''statuspageAdmin'' (not ''admin'') -- the real\n  enforced permission (README was already correct; D2).\n- AGENTS.md: document the new pageId CND value constraint on jnt:statuspageIoWidget.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n\n---------\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>","tree":{"sha":"8ddb2228168bc14fc153a541bfe57d604d1efff9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/jahia-statuspage-io/git/trees/8ddb2228168bc14fc153a541bfe57d604d1efff9"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/jahia-statuspage-io/git/commits/d