ct correctly. Fails loudly if the\nallowlist ever loosens. Stage 7 handoff: add write-side validation (CND\nconstraint / save listener / output escaping) via a shared pageId regex so the\ndefense is not render-only (also resolves the D7 divergent-validators finding).\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n\n* test: fix SEC-1 cleanup so malicious-pageId assertions are non-vacuous\n\nThe removeWidget helper deleted the widget node via cy.request with basic\nauth, which Jahia''s API security filter denies (GqlAccessDeniedException).\nThe node was therefore never removed; because every case reused one node\nname, only the first addChild succeeded and the rest failed silently with\nItemExistsException (cy.apollo swallows GraphQL errors). Six of seven\nnegative cases asserted against a stale node instead of their own payload,\nand the positive control never got a valid widget, so it failed.\n\nFix: delete via cy.apollo (authenticated session, passes the security\nfilter) like spec 02, give each case a unique node name, and publish the\nparent after each add to flush the footer-1 area output cache so the\nfreshly-created node actually renders. All 8 cases now pass and every\nnegative assertion genuinely exercises the JSP render-path allowlist.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n\n* fix: validate widget pageId at write time via CND value constraint\n\nThe per-node jnt:statuspageIoWidget/pageId property was CND-declared mandatory\nbut had no value constraint and no save-time JCR validation, so any string\npersisted. The sole guard against stored XSS was the JSP render-path allowlist\nin statuspageIoWidget.jsp -- a single render-path point of failure.\n\nAdd a JCR value constraint ''[a-z0-9-]{1,63}'' on pageId, kept IDENTICAL to that\nJSP allowlist, so JCR rejects an unsafe value at setValue/save time with a\nConstraintViolationException (the addStatuspageIoWidget mutation now returns an\nerror and no node is persisted). The JSP allowlist is retained as the matching\nrender-side layer -> defense in depth (write + render), not render-only.\n\nThe SEC-1 spec (04-statuspageIoWidgetXss.cy.ts) is extended: each malicious\npageId now asserts the write is rejected (constraint-violation error) AND that\nnothing renders; the valid pageId positive control still persists and renders.\n\nD7 residual (documented in the CND comment, not fixed here): the global\nOSGi-config path uses a stricter DNS regex and the JS util is looser (allows\nuppercase); a single shared constant across CND/Java/JSP/JS is not achievable\nand is left as a maintainer follow-up.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n\n* chore(deps): add @testing-library/dom devDependency\n\n@testing-library/react@16 declares @testing-library/dom (^10) as a peer\ndependency, but it was absent from both package.json and yarn.lock. Classic\nyarn v1 (used by the module build via frontend-maven-plugin) does not\nauto-install peer deps, so the pre-existing StatuspageIoConfigPanel.test.jsx\nJest suite failed to load (''Cannot find module @testing-library/dom'').\n\nAdd @testing-library/dom@^10.0.0 to devDependencies and regenerate yarn.lock\nwith the project-pinned classic yarn v1.22.21 (resolves to 10.4.1 + transitive\ndeps). All 4 Jest suites now load and pass (56 tests).\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n\n* docs: align version to pom (1.0.3-SNAPSHOT) and fix AGENTS.md permission name\n\n- package.json version 1.0.2 -> 1.0.3-SNAPSHOT to match pom.xml (source of\n  truth); resolves the D3 version drift (pom/package.json/AGENTS.md disagreed).\n- AGENTS.md version 1.0.1 -> 1.0.3-SNAPSHOT.\n- AGENTS.md: mutation requires ''statuspageAdmin'' (not ''admin'') -- the real\n  enforced permission (README was already correct; D2).\n- AGENTS.md: document the new pageId CND value constraint on jnt:statuspageIoWidget.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n\n---------\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqVzaGCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAQcAQAEkjrk9uYWzazPd/Ew/ech0L\n1/ut0c7U4OK8nxnoAO97ycHFDkjSxBhAPshWaVzg8Xe0VdvzhR3fXrEcbohdhIsN\nrz2rrTWDsprMmUKuk0hRuKAKAtDHNKk8yEbLjuL9dlVNBhEkDqcNEm9+ezPmKEuB\ni8FpGQwJ1igoAhsEhS+fAHPnqikGz6Otn8mPjuxi68TebAb1UWz0RYUiG4P3NxbN\n1R+mqEuFM10M6agN8DUQxjAOMCJHOjZOi0XqOrVBSXxCAMMxjQPOT81Jg88MacUv\n+ggVj6DE+4Y/dCGslOZvqmVZZgRWSoHwdVRT9ws9hONaOjQ4uhf6JT//rWQTH9en\nkLyxVW5sh4w/CEEcoWHthlT9SlkEtIZ00VOKo9erQYRhi7jehXmvZVIXTtfesn5P\ne+sR/gRM7WljzCYWU0roFnqzVjLQUNZzRWNhBj4sV4XSc51YUfryPVpAjO9OjwII\n0Jv4H62a+OabIC/hGcAKaSMx+kDT9un6lzerw4aJl5bZld5FBeP0PZrM8XqWiDIF\nsg9SZ2O5YCgKDfuVJpD0oTXo/1ihwwYOabTlrPtqO3rZunk9s5pGBAIXh4UPJu92\nCLsEBKZWwxWVyaDUSawLNCEGvIGOqdRZRoEGeVSlXw1jfwqO0rq/R6miOAQBqWXP\nzx527qA0I9WnTxXsRXla\n=fe+I\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-07-15T07:28:07Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/jahia-statuspage-io/commit/dc7f538f58e0683b8817c9d6f9d704bd9f651897","node_id":"C_kwDORxx6xNoAKGRjN2Y1MzhmNThlMDY4M2I4ODE3YzlkNmY5ZDcwNGJkOWY2NTE4OTc","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/jahia-statuspage-io/commit/42ed0b2f2df445d6d2e18684ad9761c1f21ebfef","sha":"42ed0b2f2df445d6d2e18684ad9761c1f21ebfef","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/jahia-statuspage-io/commits/42ed0b2f2df445d6d2e18684ad9761c1f21ebfef"}],"sha":"dc7f538f58e0683b8817c9d6f9d704bd9f651897","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/jahia-statuspage-io/commits/dc7f538f58e0683b8817c9d6f9d704bd9f651897"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16238554?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/fbourasse","id":16238554,"login":"fbourasse","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjM4NTU0","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/jahia-statuspage-io/commits/42ed0b2f2df445d6d2e18684ad9761c1f21ebfef/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-08T16:30:36Z","email":"fbourasse@jahia.com","name":"Florent BOURASSÉ"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-08T16:30:36Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix: patch form-data, tar, @babel/core and assertj-core (#13)\n\nResolves all open Dependabot alerts:\n- form-data <2.5.6 & <4.0.6 (HIGH) -> fresh Classic install resolves to 2.5.6 and 4.0.6\n- tar <=7.5.15 (MEDIUM, dev+runtime) -> resolution ^7.5.16, resolves to 7.5.19\n- @babel/core <=7.29.0 (LOW) -> resolution ^7.29.6, resolves to 7.29.7\n- org.assertj:assertj-core <=3.27.6 (HIGH) -> 3.27.7 in pom.xml\n\nThe multi-major form-data (2.x and 4.x trees) is fixed via a fresh Yarn\nClassic lockfile regen (each major resolves to its own patched tail),\nnot a global pin. Converts tests/ lockfile from Yarn Berry to Classic to\nmatch the @jahia/cypress harness (which generates a Classic env).\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>","tree":{"sha":"91fea7f3c5d4c038a8bfda941f6ba5c83a94455a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/jahia-statuspage-io/git/trees/91fea7f3c5d4c038a8bfda941f6ba5c83a94455a"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/jahia-statuspage-io/git/commits/42ed0b2f2df445d6d2e18684ad9761c1f21ebfef","verification":{"payload":"tree 91fea7f3c5d4c038a8bfda941f6ba5c83a94455a\nparent 131a84c44c67d9cf466965b40800aeb773e340e0\nauthor Florent BOURASSÉ <fbourasse@jahia.com> 1783528236 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1783528236 +0200\n\nfix: patch form-data, tar, @babel/core and assertj-core (#13)\n\nResolves all open Dependabot alerts:\n- form-data <2.5.6 & <4.0.6 (HIGH) -> fresh Classic install resolves to 2.5.6 and 4.0.6\n- tar <=7.5.15 (MEDIUM, dev+runtime) -> resolution ^7.5.16, resolves to 7.5.19\n- @babel/core <=7.29.0 (LOW) -> resolution ^7.29.6, resolves to 7.29.7\n- org.assertj:assertj-core <=3.27.6 (HIGH) -> 3.27.7 in pom.xml\n\nThe multi-major form-data (2.x and 4.x trees) is fixed via a fresh Yarn\nClassic lockfile regen (each major resolves to its own patched tail),\nnot a global pin. Converts tests/ lockfile from Yarn Berry to Classic to\nmatch the @jahia/cypress harness (which generates a Classic env).\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqTnssCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA8CEQAEDLRjQwBGT8zI0/9p6V+0BP\n9AeTJj3SfWg946KTjfofg