40e0","sha":"131a84c44c67d9cf466965b40800aeb773e340e0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/jahia-statuspage-io/commits/131a84c44c67d9cf466965b40800aeb773e340e0"}],"sha":"42ed0b2f2df445d6d2e18684ad9761c1f21ebfef","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/jahia-statuspage-io/commits/42ed0b2f2df445d6d2e18684ad9761c1f21ebfef"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16238554?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/fbourasse","id":16238554,"login":"fbourasse","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjM4NTU0","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/jahia-statuspage-io/commits/131a84c44c67d9cf466965b40800aeb773e340e0/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-06-21T07:30:30Z","email":"fbourasse@jahia.com","name":"Florent BOURASSÉ"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-06-21T07:30:30Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"refactor: unify GraphQL operations under a statuspageIo namespace container (#12)\n\nThe query field statuspageIo (config) and the mutation updateStatuspageIoConfig were\nseparate flat root fields. Unify them under one hierarchical namespace container, per the\nJahia GraphQL convention.\n\n- Query:    statuspageIo { pageId }          -> statuspageIo { config { pageId } }\n- Mutation: updateStatuspageIoConfig(pageId) -> statuspageIo { updateConfig(pageId) }\n\nNew holder types StatuspageIoQuery/Mutation carry the operations as instance @GraphQLField\nmethods (GqlStatuspageIoConfig stays a separate file); the *Extension classes keep a single\nstatuspageIo accessor field. @GraphQLRequiresPermission(\"statuspageAdmin\") stays on the leaf.\nFrontend gql.js + jsx + init.js banner bootstrap + jest test, and Cypress fixtures/specs\nupdated in lockstep. Core JCR widget fixtures untouched.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>","tree":{"sha":"632a8e4a06038b25745b94b8582fb4c32fec7893","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/jahia-statuspage-io/git/trees/632a8e4a06038b25745b94b8582fb4c32fec7893"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/jahia-statuspage-io/git/commits/131a84c44c67d9cf466965b40800aeb773e340e0","verification":{"payload":"tree 632a8e4a06038b25745b94b8582fb4c32fec7893\nparent 0d19381cd1a3df2217026bc6b669959e5e647e44\nauthor Florent BOURASSÉ <fbourasse@jahia.com> 1782027030 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1782027030 +0200\n\nrefactor: unify GraphQL operations under a statuspageIo namespace container (#12)\n\nThe query field statuspageIo (config) and the mutation updateStatuspageIoConfig were\nseparate flat root fields. Unify them under one hierarchical namespace container, per the\nJahia GraphQL convention.\n\n- Query:    statuspageIo { pageId }          -> statuspageIo { config { pageId } }\n- Mutation: updateStatuspageIoConfig(pageId) -> statuspageIo { updateConfig(pageId) }\n\nNew holder types StatuspageIoQuery/Mutation carry the operations as instance @GraphQLField\nmethods (GqlStatuspageIoConfig stays a separate file); the *Extension classes keep a single\nstatuspageIo accessor field. @GraphQLRequiresPermission(\"statuspageAdmin\") stays on the leaf.\nFrontend gql.js + jsx + init.js banner bootstrap + jest test, and Cypress fixtures/specs\nupdated in lockstep. Core JCR widget fixtures untouched.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqN5MWCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAATF0QAE4gQBhOwCrv6GHgf5Qnatwi\nAoMCn+fPgQRnH/G1gRcL7HS9Kil+yc2v8vV/OSfHJWVhdeeqr5HWxQWVD0gULPVB\n2a7DROK72I8IJOZgjdGVxVjuAC/l/nB5D9RjVqssHowYcROJE5Bhvuoq39mYrUqS\nPhbiFzKDswbBEvMVyFl/B4TyrPecoxfjLMk5y+lyFNEHPdo7F+SB7wVXIAky8TWm\nwGo0gvvue1vwDPPMDqoCfiNATD+tk9zOQUpca+TF777glpxJEDmr8trTMxawc1Kx\nv5BfJTau1RrdcyJA7XqmhIYqQ3QDLZjMTXb0f4jBRngW4TEZzpr9PH1uZQABnNXc\nAa3U8HwNa+gyUYu3Q6si/gNs0vPSukIv5bH7yLWtN4q9jDCyqQn/6n2FTyEZwwuw\noCFA10LSD3cJQcfoZNWaQNEhAg049s7dype8PTH8EzwRryZue3nHKc6KoVzuBSEv\n6EOkhFBZHHZVYEBzcU29tFdaqNqIBtZgRxDXPIjQsJRcACaDzEvPkeRjl2j8S/YZ\nw/4hzh6/F6Wkip3nAx7kd2l4kl5jR6DGIOKKohAIWAt5zIvSjOTOHDgJSdgHkAQb\nNB0YLaKY4neALFxvarQXxiXy4NIj74WPGKZ9EFn05GdGBEE8GF2jfZfWDJtRuRV0\nP/EkTacWBYAQ/Kqi91fe\n=zwDI\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-06-21T07:30:30Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/jahia-statuspage-io/commit/131a84c44c67d9cf466965b40800aeb773e340e0","node_id":"C_kwDORxx6xNoAKDEzMWE4NGM0NGM2N2Q5Y2Y0NjY5NjViNDA4MDBhZWI3NzNlMzQwZTA","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/jahia-statuspage-io/commit/0d19381cd1a3df2217026bc6b669959e5e647e44","sha":"0d19381cd1a3df2217026bc6b669959e5e647e44","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/jahia-statuspage-io/commits/0d19381cd1a3df2217026bc6b669959e5e647e44"}],"sha":"131a84c44c67d9cf466965b40800aeb773e340e0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/jahia-statuspage-io/commits/131a84c44c67d9cf466965b40800aeb773e340e0"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16238554?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/fbourasse","id":16238554,"login":"fbourasse","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjM4NTU0","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/jahia-statuspage-io/commits/0d19381cd1a3df2217026bc6b669959e5e647e44/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-06-20T17:31:41Z","email":"fbourasse@jahia.com","name":"Florent BOURASSÉ"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-06-20T17:31:41Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Harden jahia-statuspage-io: thread-safety, AAA a11y, banner safety, tests (#8)\n\n* fix: harden StatuspageIo Java backend — thread safety, DI, unchecked exceptions, docs\n\nCRIT-1: Replace plain `config`/`configHash` fields with a single `volatile ConfigSnapshot`\nreference so GraphQL-thread reads always see a consistent config+hash pair.\n\nCRIT-2: `@Modified` now updates the snapshot directly instead of re-invoking `@Activate`\nor relying on a stored BundleContext.\n\nHIGH-5: Remove stored `bundleContext` field and the always-true `Bundle.ACTIVE` guard\nfrom `@Activate` (the SCR container guarantees the bundle is active at that point).\n\nHIGH-1: Convert `StatuspageIoMutationExtension` from static BundleUtils lookup to\n`@Inject @GraphQLOsgiService` field injection, matching the pattern in GqlStatuspageIoConfig.\n\nHIGH-2: Remove public `getConfigService()` accessor from `GqlStatuspageIoConfig`; it\nwas unused outside tests and leaked internal state.\n\nHIGH-3: Change `configurationAdmin.getConfiguration(PID, null)` to `getConfiguration(PID, \"?\")`\nso the configuration is location-independent and not pinned to the bundle''s location.\n\nHIGH-4: Remove `throws IOException` from `StatuspageIoConfigService.updatePageId` interface\nand implementation; ConfigurationAdmin IOExceptions are now wrapped in the new unchecked\n`StatuspageIoConfigException`. Mutation caller updated accordingly.\n\nSECURITY: JSP `pageIdSafe` guard verified — the character-by-character allow-list\n(`[a-z0-9-]`) prevents any JS-special character from reaching the `<script>` block,\nso no XSS path exists through the widget node property.\n\nDOC: README corrected from `admin` to `statuspageAdmin` (the actual shipped permission).\nJavadoc added to `StatuspageIoConfigService` interface methods (nullability, format,\nempty-string semantics).\n\nTESTS: Expanded `StatuspageIoConfigServiceImplTest` with activate/modified/unchecked-exception\ncoverage; added `StatuspageIoMutationExtensionTest`; added non-null contract test to\n`GqlStatuspageIoConfigTest`. All stubs updated to use `\"?\"` location arg.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n\n* harden jahia-statuspage-io: thread-safety, a11y AAA, banner safety, tests\n\nBackend: immutable volatile config snapshot (data race); @Modified updates directly;\nremoved stored bundleContext; getConfiguration(\"?\"); unchecked StatuspageIoConfigException\n(no IOException through the interface); removed leaked getConfigService(); README permission\naligned to statuspageAdmin; verified the widget JSP escapes pageId.\n(Kept the mutation on BundleUtils.getOsgiService — @GraphQLOsgiService injection does not apply\nto a mutation type-extension''s static @GraphQLField method; switching broke it at runtime.)\n\nFrontend: banner prototype-pollution-safe postMessage dispatch + reduced-motion + focus-to-main\n+ empty-pageId guard + AAA visually-hidden status region (status.json); config panel label\nassociation, persistent live region, AAA contrast, scoped focus, useEffect focus; fr.json;\nremoved console.debug; jest setup + tests.\n\nSonarQube gate OK; lint 0/0; 28 Java tests; Cypress 13/13.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n\n---------\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>","tree":{"sha":"7fb8ec097ebc0ae8954d5ba14858d909d94ce58d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/jahia-statuspage-io/git/trees/7fb8ec097ebc0ae8954d5ba14858d909d94ce58d"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/jahia-statuspage-io/git/commits/0d19381cd1a3df2217026bc6b669959e5e647e44","verification":{"payload":"tree 7fb8ec097ebc0ae8954d5ba14858d909d94ce58d\nparent a53fd463a592aa6ec6270589a6efadd7d68b8d83\nauthor Florent BOURASSÉ <fbourasse@jahia.com> 1781976701 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1781976701 +0200\n\nHarden jahia-statuspage-io: thread-safety, AAA a11y, banner safety, tests (#8)\n\n* fix: harden StatuspageIo Java backend — thread safety, DI, unchecked exceptions, docs\n\nCRIT-1: Replace plain `config`/`configHash` fields with a single `volatile ConfigSnapshot`\nreference so GraphQL-thread reads always see a consistent config+hash pair.\n\nCRIT-2: `@Modified` now updates the snapshot directly instead of re-invoking `@Activate`\nor relying on a stored BundleContext.\n\nHIGH-5: Remove stored `bundleContext` field and the always-true `Bundle.ACTIVE` guard\nfrom `@Activate` (the SCR container guarantees the bundle is active at that point).\n\nHIGH-1: Convert `StatuspageIoMutationExtension` from static BundleUtils lookup to\n`@Inject @GraphQLOsgiService` field injection, matching the pattern in GqlStatuspageIoConfig.\n\nHIGH-2: Remove public `getConfigService()` accessor from `GqlStatuspageIoConfig`; it\nwas unused outside tests and leaked internal state.\n\nHIGH-3: Change `configurationAdmin.getConfiguration(PID, null)` to `getConfiguration(PID, \"?\")`\nso the configuration is location-independent and not pinned to the bundle''s location.\n\nHIGH-4: Remove `throws IOException` from `StatuspageIoConfigService.updatePageId` interface\nand implementation; ConfigurationAdmin IOExceptions are now wrapped in the new unchecked\n`StatuspageIoConfigException`. Mutation caller updated accordingly.\n\nSECURITY: JSP `pageIdSafe` guard verified — the character-by-character allow-list\n(`[a-z0-9-]`) prevents any JS-special character from reaching the `<script>` block,\nso no XSS path exists through the widget node property.\n\nDOC: README corrected from `admin` to `statuspageAdmin` (the actual shipped permission).\nJavadoc added to `StatuspageIoConfigService` interface methods (nullability, format,\nempty-string semantics).\n\nTESTS: Expanded `StatuspageIoConfigServiceImplTest` with activate/modified/unchecked-exception\ncoverage; added `StatuspageIoMutationExtensionTest`; added non-null contract test to\n`GqlStatuspageIoConfigTest`. All stubs updated to use `\"?\"` location arg.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n\n* harden jahia-statuspage-io: thread-safety, a11y AAA, banner safety, tests\n\nBackend: immutable volatile config snapshot (data race); @Modified updates directly;\nremoved stored bundleContext; getConfiguration(\"?\"); unchecked StatuspageIoConfigException\n(no IOException through the interface); removed leaked getConfigService(); README permission\naligned to statuspageAdmin; verified the widget JSP escapes pageId.\n(Kept the mutation on BundleUtils.getOsgiService — @GraphQLOsgiService injection does not apply\nto a mutation type-extension''s static @GraphQLField method; switching broke it at runtime.)\n\nFrontend: banner prototype-pollution-safe postMessage dispatch + reduced-motion + focus-to-main\n+ empty-pageId guard + AAA visually-hidden status region (status.json); config panel label\nassociation, persistent live region, AAA contrast, scoped focus, useEffect focus; fr.json;\nremoved console.debug; jest setup + tests.\n\nSonarQube gate OK; lint 0/0; 28 Java tests; Cypress 13/13.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n\n---------\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqNs59CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAI10QAI6UiNMm6zuXjHpNYQAsNCTR\n4LQGI2V1D0P6U5vgE/ECfGRIVOd5A7UeCbp3vWX9cGENMF2fJqc5Shqu5rfL2GPw\nVBTgBhN39qiaAI62ffeScGQVnGe9Myt6doB1tiMYHSQuis+qe9blfKI2/+PCNsjK\nCJ0GDZVXoUs4JVstPP/pB45rddRUH2b3Q8deYYAM6ao27UadqSl2IcX220EtyDyT\n25epRt/gmnN9zLWWtK+xrAsp2ffLnqVOaGZnS3HmMZzkia+5tI97ooVLH9APINh4\nS4GqYO5x+ZGawi3mdwh+T2zPoBfNJOPv1C8luafEufLLGl2M/QkSp/5sODeupNNq\nQ7oWddGV6MQ+SEs60GN1kvAq0ULXPClz/2tR/GxGoLipFn6gbTFvnpWUgQ8acCfg\naXcB+s7+s//ANSbayFpZXAUPJ5z2mt31pDgz29XuXY3yY7n3wAmWd3QUYxCFFx6v\nJUHidbW7Q2F1svV/nZkP7r0Kcr2fGDqS9i//f9c13xY5FrCGKJfoNiTx1bOpbxLZ\nRodArZThGK9LDvCpX5+QaUoJKTfa/LffJhAX3+Xh4wrrA3M8gGzlK1/2sFnVbYHE\nNf+zsIDBQrcciHTKToThu4lh0upn423Xms4wvOzIEWlHt48/lySaGc/DUnbQBdNb\nW+3Srdy05TnLegMFg7sV\n=M/co\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-06-20T17:31:42Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/jahia-statuspage-io/commit/0d19381cd1a3df2217026bc6b669959e5e647e44","node_id":"C_kwDORxx6xNoAKDBkMTkzODFjZDFhM2RmMjIxNzAyNmJjNmI2Njk5NTllNWU2NDdlNDQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/jahia-statuspage-io/commit/a53fd463a592aa6ec6270589a6efadd7d68b8d83","sha":"a53fd463a592aa6ec6270589a6efadd7d68b8d83","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/jahia-statuspage-io/commits/a53fd463a592aa6ec6270589a6efadd7d68b8d83"}],"sha":"0d19381cd1a3df2217026bc6b669959e5e647e44","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/jahia-statuspage-io/commits/0d19381cd1a3df2217026bc6b669959e5e647e44"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16238554?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/fbourasse","id":16238554,"login":"fbourasse","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjM4NTU0","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/jahia-statuspage-io/commits/a53fd463a592aa6ec6270589a6efadd7d68b8d83/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-06-10T19:07:11Z","email":"fbourasse@jahia.com","name":"Florent BOURASSÉ"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-06-10T19:07:11Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"test: add fine-grained permission regression tests + assignable admin role (#7)\n\nAdd regression coverage for the fine-grained `statuspageAdmin` permission and\nship an assignable server-role so the gate can be granted without full admin.\n\n- src/main/import/roles.xml: new `jahia-statuspage-io-administrator` role\n  granting `administrationAccess statuspageAdmin` (privileged, server-role on\n  rep:root) so a non-admin user can administer the module end-to-end.\n- tests/cypress/e2e/03-statuspageIo-Permissions.cy.ts: 4 tests proving the gate\n  across the stack using a user granted ONLY the module role (never `admin`):\n    * GraphQL deny: `updateStatuspageIoConfig` -> ''Permission denied''\n    * GraphQL allow: `updateStatuspageIoConfig(pageId:''teststatuspage'')` -> true, no errors\n    * Admin UI hidden for denied user; shown for granted user\n  The public `statuspageIo` query is intentionally ungated (banner on public\n  pages), so the gated MUTATION is the operation under test.\n- pom.xml: bump module version 1.0.2 -> 1.0.3-SNAPSHOT (import content changed).\n\nThe resolver has no inner hardcoded `admin` check (only the annotation), so no\nJava relaxation was required.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>","tree":{"sha":"27e5d30d5720cfd6be92258c44cfce1f0cf787e8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/jahia-statuspage-io/git/trees/27e5d30d5720cfd6be92258c44cfce1f0cf787e8"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/jahia-statuspage-io/git/commits/a53fd463a592aa6ec6270589a6efadd7d68b8d83","verification":{"payload":"tree 27e5d30d5720cfd6be92258c44cfce1f0cf787e8\nparent 3247407c0f1b99f822469a892bd83ab5f8e35ef2\nauthor Florent BOURASSÉ <fbourasse@jahia.com> 1781118431 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1781118431 +0200\n\ntest: add fine-grained permission regression tests + assignable admin role (#7)\n\nAdd regression coverage for the fine-grained `statuspageAdmin` permission and\nship an assignable server-role so the gate can be granted without full admin.\n\n- src/main/import/roles.xml: new `jahia-statuspage-io-administrator` role\n  granting `administrationAccess statuspageAdmin` (privileged, server-role on\n  rep:root) so a non-admin user can administer the module end-to-end.\n- tests/cypress/e2e/03-statuspageIo-Permissions.cy.ts: 4 tests proving the gate\n  across the stack using a user granted ONLY the module role (never `admin`):\n    * GraphQL deny: `updateStatuspageIoConfig` -> ''Permission denied''\n    * GraphQL allow: `updateStatuspageIoConfig(pageId:''teststatuspage'')` -> true, no errors\n    * Admin UI hidden for denied user; shown for granted user\n  The public `statuspageIo` query is intentionally ungated (banner on public\n  pages), so the gated MUTATION is the operation under test.\n- pom.xml: bump module version 1.0.2 -> 1.0.3-SNAPSHOT (import content changed).\n\nThe resolver has no inner hardcoded `admin` check (only the annotation), so no\nJava relaxation was required.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqKbXfCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAASrIQADU9Eu/mUJcNwXjv+kSJVVNY\nNf9zSrOpQW0GRQJaF3FzCDv5hJeecnno6AgZrN+tQ9h7gotT+JhZ6E9lr0PG