ng, init, push, remove, pull, and status\n\nEnable with GNAP_ENABLED=true in .env. Follows the same fire-and-forget\npattern as the existing GitHub sync engine.\n\nCloses #374\nSupersedes #389","tree":{"sha":"059c225432fcc474f31b472232543793c3a61e6a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/watson-gpositive/custom-mission-control/git/trees/059c225432fcc474f31b472232543793c3a61e6a"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/watson-gpositive/custom-mission-control/git/commits/85b4184aa9c849fd4b41000b34b853d83c80d892","verification":{"payload":"tree 059c225432fcc474f31b472232543793c3a61e6a\nparent d87307a4f8764248f818add539b5c30db7701d68\nauthor nyk <93952610+0xNyk@users.noreply.github.com> 1773637659 +0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1773637659 +0700\n\nfeat: GNAP sync engine for git-native task persistence (#396)\n\nImplements Phase 1 of GNAP (Git-Native Agent Protocol) integration:\n- SQLite stays primary, GNAP repo is an optional sync target\n- Push task create/update/delete to .gnap/tasks/{id}.json with git commits\n- Status/priority mapping between MC and GNAP formats\n- Management API at /api/gnap (status, init, manual sync)\n- GNAP badge in task board header with click-to-sync\n- 15 unit tests covering mapping, init, push, remove, pull, and status\n\nEnable with GNAP_ENABLED=true in .env. Follows the same fire-and-forget\npattern as the existing GitHub sync engine.\n\nCloses #374\nSupersedes #389","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJpt5AbCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAz50QABU/Vgx7kyErJ/XE3zqVN449\ndlODMStFyqCzY1Eky8pQKh9CITDUapPa4yiK/H63y/M8OB67lh2mearjy8Cv/R/x\n+N/jueNf0Adny6qV33xV6V/mvujsAxntXkYLdYw/vwf9rLfPnIoiTJ2gvGdxy1Vl\n6+VqTJd4T32fcqiB09eE3qrqz37E+NyEqmyw6Yo0CAfV6tKwyZwfyb7ewKyYatla\nRM3zzwzg3CHNoz9WdynEN4E0Yfbc/uQO2TcLzIK0W7oU1ZY2YkObFlFpeJmlwC3E\n6PjBvQyU7I1Oo+cw/9XO5EJVDshYuE96w0UGLAx684r/sNX0E+hU1QYgzfrggVaX\nRWyTHmuqMSse3U3k1KR3gkZTgaVFiaqS/CCUwcS6udNwi8Z6+k30MUNKyYpGb3nX\nuR1vtw2GGWa7R9tQleI7AlI0/kj9rjRLKZ+25TcuQDOn7LPr2