isabled when no valid agent is\nselected.\n\nFixes #321\n\n* test: add gateway health history e2e + utility unit tests\n\n- Add tests/gateway-health-history.spec.ts: Playwright e2e tests for\n  GET /api/gateways/health/history and POST /api/gateways/health\n  covering auth guards, response shape validation, chronological\n  ordering, and gateway name resolution.\n\n- Add src/app/api/gateways/health/health-utils.test.ts: 30 vitest\n  unit tests for the pure utility functions in the health probe route:\n  ipv4InCidr, isBlockedUrl (SSRF protection), buildGatewayProbeUrl,\n  parseGatewayVersion, and hasOpenClaw32ToolsProfileRisk.\n\nAll 30 unit tests pass. Covers the health history feature introduced\nin feat(gateways): add health history logging and timeline (#300).","tree":{"sha":"7ad7d3c81e1fb6d75b590731235e9516e374d2f2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/watson-gpositive/custom-mission-control/git/trees/7ad7d3c81e1fb6d75b590731235e9516e374d2f2"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/watson-gpositive/custom-mission-control/git/commits/2fe7785433d5204d740e617bcef594205c2cf235","verification":{"payload":"tree 7ad7d3c81e1fb6d75b590731235e9516e374d2f2\nparent 5d7b05b4f6d47416e4e08b6e2805e1e26d352e95\nauthor HonzysClawdbot <janclawdbotstratil@gmail.com> 1773481142 +0100\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1773481142 +0700\n\ntest: add gateway health history e2e + utility unit tests\n\n* fix: show all agents in command select, disable those without active session\n\nPreviously the agent select in the OrchestrationBar only listed agents\nwith a session_key set (agents.filter(a => a.session_key)), causing the\ndropdown to appear completely empty when agents exist but none have an\nactive session. This was confusing — users thought no agents were\nregistered.\n\nFix: show all registered agents in the dropdown. Agents without an\nactive session_key are shown as disabled with a ''— no session'' suffix\nand a tooltip explaining why they can''t be messaged. The ''No agents\nregistered'' placeholder is shown only when the agents array is truly\nempty.\n\nThe send button remains correctly disabled when no valid agent is\nselected.\n\nFixes #321\n\n* test: add gateway health history e2e + utility unit tests\n\n- Add tests/gateway-health-history.spec.ts: Playwright e2e tests for\n  GET /api/gateways/health/history and POST /api/gateways/health\n  covering auth guards, response shape validation, chronological\n  ordering, and gateway name resolution.\n\n- Add src/app/api/gateways/health/health-utils.test.ts: 30 vitest\n  unit tests for the pure utility functions in the health probe route:\n  ipv4InCidr, isBlockedUrl (SSRF protection), buildGatewayProbeUrl,\n  parseGatewayVersion, and hasOpenClaw32ToolsProfileRisk.\n\nAll 30 unit tests pass. Covers the health history feature introduced\nin feat(gateways): add health history logging and timeline (#300).","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJptSy2CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAzkwQAJryzU3HjetZY5niFCvlKfNi\nkSK7FjQAKAuxtHVig3ynuiuccGBLMc4qrDMWy8sBoEHd3BOFPv+Fga5XNN04YThZ\nEStMsknHPUkcm4h9dPjA2NtnllAhNnMpgd7zU/bY5LX1WwLKNezdL/KLZN3fqwvn\n4afFsQX8s9Uv/FDF3zinEi5KCM+7zcsqKyNOZhM/GOyN6BC+QwY4+efkT4H2LGtA\n6iGzMnMjeeQlP3reai4VEw0bPVCHJVg/pgMqxpusYAVs+f/Qx+eznSsqSLajWbao\n9lXiKuRpP1sCWIyroSKp9mYU5Efa2mMqu6qH+Br2RNOb1g8zq1eZaZL0cgR+LLX+\nR3HWrxUBIMfrXla6LYDEp5J1aRJdcBNJTxufnyoHhTF05kw1XKeXJA31OxCJujXU\nj14lMDbxAQcpG5FQd7+lb4BhAubY5BedlFZoQs5NXV7p65SjcQIadH5Br93DYqAQ\nbUlkQ6euaGguJFvRnsuH+roua6m2TeZcoYszDsyvnajecEUUBc9OL215pUpjJJIn\ncr6DsKRZ6ks/PJkislaBc+bgN22KBSjPjYsdhJEX5M3I5aUuUSt9izhP/yEklJXG\nOpByNfRAsQgAYF8KytxUtijjjUf1Sn0bRq2KGne0Yc8xd2i3qD2jW5nbkQNE/U8Z\nPg6o/r8ayXS4LM5JWps4\n=No92\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-03-26T20:38:47Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/watson-gpositive/custom-mission-control/commit/2fe7785433d5204d740e617bcef594205c2cf235","node_id":"C_kwDORxyPE9oAKDJmZTc3ODU0MzNkNTIwNGQ3NDBlNjE3YmNlZjU5NDIwNWMyY2YyMzU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/watson-gpositive/custom-mission-control/commit/5d7b05b4f6d47416e4e08b6e2805e1e26d352e95","sha":"5d7b05b4f6d47416e4e08b6e2805e1e26d352e95","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/watson-gpositive/custom-mission-control/commits/5d7b05b4f6d47416e4e08b6e2805e1e26d352e95"}],"sha":"2fe7785433d5204d740e617bcef594205c2cf235","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/watson-gpositive/custom-mission-control/commits/2fe7785433d5204d740e617bcef594205c2cf235"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17442606?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tomwattsca/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tomwattsca/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tomwattsca/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tomwattsca/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/tomwattsca","id":17442606,"login":"tomwattsca","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDQyNjA2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tomwattsca/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tomwattsca/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tomwattsca/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tomwattsca/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tomwattsca/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/tomwattsca","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/watson-gpositive/custom-mission-control/commits/5d7b05b4f6d47416e4e08b6e2805e1e26d352e95/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-03-14T09:38:55Z","email":"tom@topshelfmedia.ca","name":"Tom Watts"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-03-14T09:38:55Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(tasks): use --expect-final for agent dispatch and Aegis review\n\nThe two-step agent → agent.wait pattern used in dispatchAssignedTasks and\nrunAegisReviews only returns lifecycle metadata (runId, status, timestamps).\nThe agent''s actual response text is only available via --expect-final on the\ninitial agent call, which blocks until completion and returns the full payload\nincluding result.payloads[0].text.\n\nWithout this fix:\n- Task resolution is stored as the raw wait JSON instead of the agent''s response\n- Aegis cannot parse a VERDICT from the resolution, so it always defaults to rejected\n- Tasks are permanently stuck in a reject/retry loop and never complete\n\nFix: replace the two-call pattern with a single --expect-final call in both\ndispatchAssignedTasks and runAegisReviews. Also improve sessionId extraction\nto use the agentMeta path from the final payload.\n\nCo-authored-by: Tom Watts <tom@techteamup.com>","tree":{"sha":"a20e30e86d480f21411f1e79bf35b4d29c535279","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/watson-gpositive/custom-mission-control/git/trees/a20e30e86d480f21411f1e79bf35b4d29c535279"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/watson-gpositive/custom-mission-control/git/commits/5d7b05b4f6d47416e4e08b6e2805e1e26d352e95","verification":{"payload":"tree a20e30e86d480f21411f1e79bf35b4d29c535279\nparent 4fa1cbd3a5bc230a8126f002cf5608c646255292\nauthor Tom Watts <tom@topshelfmedia.ca> 1773481135 +0000\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1773481135 +0700\n\nfix(tasks): use --expect-final for agent dispatch and Aegis review\n\nThe two-step agent → agent.wait pattern used in dispatchAssignedTasks and\nrunAegisReviews only returns lifecycle metadata (runId, status, timestamps).\nThe agent''s actual response text is only available via --expect-final on the\ninitial agent call, which blocks until completion and returns the full payload\nincluding result.payloads[0].text.\n\nWithout this fix:\n- Task resolution is stored as the raw wait JSON instead of the agent''s response\n- Aegis cannot parse a VERDICT from the resolution, so it always defaults to rejected\n- Tasks are permanently stuck in a reject/retry loop and never complete\n\nFix: replace the two-call pattern with a single --expect-final call in both\ndispatchAssignedTasks and runAegisReviews. Also improve sessionId extraction\nto use the agentMeta path from the final payload.\n\nCo-authored-by: Tom Watts <tom@techteamup.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJptSyvCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAACGkQAFkcM87W2EiwVH72LLCxLMs6\nZcGqlhjhXJqwvn49HfNh0kR8CqvwbGuC0qEwB0qOXNB6zps0wo2gyv395Ni9RUVM\nFDp+OtWm6vEZSdIg2QZMJAsn8Q2dg9DS0jdWhO0kL8VENuw0yJm6qLkFagkyQpvN\nTfL/LwoqjtE7uJ5EfnRDqAmkuPv6YPNjDdzflMBK97iPJBgYjDPKjVlS/JDY3WRP\nFjxdzLHf0Gh1OwRKUoOTS/ifPIrLyAmQRatUHtDRrWHpGETWhSNCYNX8jk/6aHIS\n0euIXMM6o5hK66xhqWulRKweI4ngNgXIJxqZyRRVE0N35ytwh6qb/fWMzaWLITPL\nJvEkL8nVTmwi2MaZHuajK4D5NL4GBTVt6Ummuq1MXzVtdb4J8GKNHRLgv33v1gGh\nK3SUpk/aUZCjUehCiq65GfDfO68XmyeBhNe4651HQa8pvlPn8GlanMUZdrSaBNhn\nMn/xMfVux6eJe42RhcB2y4uI3KyjV07+WnGwJWWNacqvykrTCS17IEV7O63tAxCQ\n7s4t7+ZT0yfIO4wKN94wbITCBC0R76khtNzcpW/NC2iclefdp+C+I6QaVr+FeYFq\nE3ZcO9lEaDAwTzzQBEE+GZ6x6HQYIqnjD7VSs1w0XyDhYdUa5FWRcjwHFP31j3dG\nRiDwbxiDUXAJvgMcboFz