on-control/git/trees/89656d95e2c45dcb854900d54b55b4cdbbaed39c"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/watson-gpositive/custom-mission-control/git/commits/4fa1cbd3a5bc230a8126f002cf5608c646255292","verification":{"payload":"tree 89656d95e2c45dcb854900d54b55b4cdbbaed39c\nparent 176e862431f36ad0b8d0cf3970765100e5473dd8\nauthor HonzysClawdbot <janclawdbotstratil@gmail.com> 1773481133 +0100\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1773481133 +0700\n\nfix: show all agents in command select, disable those without active session\n\nPreviously the agent select in the OrchestrationBar only listed agents\nwith a session_key set (agents.filter(a => a.session_key)), causing the\ndropdown to appear completely empty when agents exist but none have an\nactive session. This was confusing — users thought no agents were\nregistered.\n\nFix: show all registered agents in the dropdown. Agents without an\nactive session_key are shown as disabled with a ''— no session'' suffix\nand a tooltip explaining why they can''t be messaged. The ''No agents\nregistered'' placeholder is shown only when the agents array is truly\nempty.\n\nThe send button remains correctly disabled when no valid agent is\nselected.\n\nFixes #321","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJptSytCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAxocQALFtDovlFv9+don3vdr9sUY1\nkFLotwS0nOHzyF8Vz4jCftk2/3UVe8dr9cHbVPYzdLLRbNsYExIbG09mHODNoH5Y\n+8vo9DssEBv/20JGZKyGycfwZ7loPiWpFej5m9AP4NigE+xq0eYv5MCnENSzQ/bR\nsiE+mJQlXxdjamq2Asq1nWZjMNXaOCCXdXYgMoXqvauWh118ls+NUf7yTjPyLteN\n4T7zLYoc/4rd6jazSaiByEnuh12yyJLFoFW3MlnClGF/QEdsFoJLZuWIqDjLk+/m\nRCrWINgYw+2phe9aAof+3JwR9hD0ikyRY4S2Pbn2BIzfWUiKprrDhXLyxoUeHMBM\nA4a9NDpTHcdTpWJB0MWgiu4jw0aa5rpFOs24f/t5gp/6nYSdxymWofxR40CIPkbK\nLvLHlR1OmMdhVpBs2wgE0RvkX7ZjGyrV/VggEeyMbCwA5UTkck8GC1HA62lT38ze\ngxXmYe0e/zSvyrwxugdc4n1135ia9Hh7vpBK+YOiye3al11tXziJdMHHMXIaG0YY\nsKwXwpjMcKEts2xMw96A9f/ArLo+5aMPb/QGuiKPJJa/CCUrDhl+NLnMfTtWrVPH\ns4+L0cHff1Do2WWnUij/pSvUnCUvrHBvK5ZDwhCVdEpSmJyFRWNNxU3Ard2hZj3g\nW