"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/watson-gpositive/custom-mission-control/commit/8eef4139ec091801a8464542136fd2ca7d2db56a","node_id":"C_kwDORxyPE9oAKDhlZWY0MTM5ZWMwOTE4MDFhODQ2NDU0MjEzNmZkMmNhN2QyZGI1NmE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/watson-gpositive/custom-mission-control/commit/8706147f84a39959b1fe1c3121e310a6aebebb03","sha":"8706147f84a39959b1fe1c3121e310a6aebebb03","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/watson-gpositive/custom-mission-control/commits/8706147f84a39959b1fe1c3121e310a6aebebb03"}],"sha":"8eef4139ec091801a8464542136fd2ca7d2db56a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/watson-gpositive/custom-mission-control/commits/8eef4139ec091801a8464542136fd2ca7d2db56a"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/264638470?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HonzysClawdbot/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HonzysClawdbot/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HonzysClawdbot/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HonzysClawdbot/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/HonzysClawdbot","id":264638470,"login":"HonzysClawdbot","node_id":"U_kgDOD8YQBg","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HonzysClawdbot/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HonzysClawdbot/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HonzysClawdbot/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HonzysClawdbot/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HonzysClawdbot/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/HonzysClawdbot","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/watson-gpositive/custom-mission-control/commits/8706147f84a39959b1fe1c3121e310a6aebebb03/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-03-14T08:38:13Z","email":"janclawdbotstratil@gmail.com","name":"HonzysClawdbot"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-03-14T08:38:13Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(gateway): resolve Docker connectivity — 404 endpoints, EROFS write, missing OPENCLAW_HOME (#343)\n\n* docs: add screenshot drift prevention guide and CI workflow\n\n- Add docs/SCREENSHOT-GUIDE.md with step-by-step instructions for\n  capturing, optimising, and committing fresh README screenshots\n- Add .github/workflows/screenshot-drift.yml that detects UI file\n  changes in PRs, applies a ''screenshot-drift'' label, and posts a\n  checklist comment reminding contributors to verify screenshots\n\nAddresses: README screenshots may drift as the UI evolves quickly\n(setup wizard, health history timeline, and onboarding were added\nafter the last screenshot refresh on 2026-03-11)\n\n* fix(gateway): resolve Docker connectivity — 404 endpoints, EROFS write, missing OPENCLAW_HOME\n\nFixes #332, #333\n\nRoot causes\n-----------\n1. nodes/route.ts called non-existent HTTP REST endpoints on the gateway\n   (/api/presence, /api/devices, /api/rpc). The OpenClaw gateway only\n   exposes HTTP at /health; all other operations use WebSocket RPC.\n\n2. gateway-runtime.ts attempted fs.writeFileSync on openclaw.json which\n   fails with EROFS when the container or mount is read-only (docker-compose\n   uses read_only: true by default).\n\n3. install.sh never wrote the detected OPENCLAW_HOME or Docker host gateway\n   IP into .env, leaving OPENCLAW_HOME empty after a fresh install.\n\nFixes\n-----\n- nodes/route.ts: replace HTTP calls to /api/presence and /api/devices\n  with gateway /health reachability check + callOpenClawGateway() RPC\n  (node.list / device.pair.list). When the openclaw CLI is unavailable\n  inside Docker, the RPC falls back gracefully and returns connected=true\n  with an empty list rather than a misleading ''Gateway offline'' error.\n  POST device actions likewise use callOpenClawGateway instead of /api/rpc.\n\n- gateway-runtime.ts: catch EROFS / EACCES / EPERM on config write and\n  emit a warn-level log with a hint, instead of an error. This eliminates\n  the ''Failed to register MC in gateway config EROFS: read-only file\n  system'' log spam on Docker installs where openclaw.json is read-only.\n\n- install.sh: after generating .env, write the detected OPENCLAW_HOME.\n  In --docker mode also detect the Docker host IP (host-gateway or bridge\n  default) and set OPENCLAW_GATEWAY_HOST so the container can reach a\n  gateway running on the host out of the box.\n\n- docker-compose.yml: add extra_hosts host-gateway so the container can\n  resolve the Docker host IP; add a commented volume snippet for mounting\n  the OpenClaw state directory read-only.","tree":{"sha":"9375857d0cd42e3ac1d3ba75a05d153bb8058074","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/watson-gpositive/custom-mission-control/git/trees/9375857d0cd42e3ac1d3ba75a05d153bb8058074"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/watson-gpositive/custom-mission-control/git/commits/8706147f84a39959b1fe1c3121e310a6aebebb03","verification":{"payload":"tree 9375857d0cd42e3ac1d3ba75a05d153bb8058074\nparent 2b4438b63a73e589a0ff9ff47c480e0d6cc84f6b\nauthor HonzysClawdbot <janclawdbotstratil@gmail.com> 1773477493 +0100\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1773477493 +0700\n\nfix(gateway): resolve Docker connectivity — 404 endpoints, EROFS write, missing OPENCLAW_HOME (#343)\n\n* docs: add screenshot drift prevention guide and CI workflow\n\n- Add docs/SCREENSHOT-GUIDE.md with step-by-step instructions for\n  capturing, optimising, and committing fresh README screenshots\n- Add .github/workflows/screenshot-drift.yml that detects UI file\n  changes in PRs, applies a ''screenshot-drift'' label, and posts a\n  checklist comment reminding contributors to verify screenshots\n\nAddresses: README screenshots may drift as the UI evolves quickly\n(setup wizard, health history timeline, and onboarding were added\nafter the last screenshot refresh on 2026-03-11)\n\n* fix(gateway): resolve Docker connectivity — 404 endpoints, EROFS write, missing OPENCLAW_HOME\n\nFixes #332, #333\n\nRoot causes\n-----------\n1. nodes/route.ts called non-existent HTTP REST endpoints on the gateway\n   (/api/presence, /api/devices, /api/rpc). The OpenClaw gateway only\n   exposes HTTP at /health; all other operations use WebSocket RPC.\n\n2. gateway-runtime.ts attempted fs.writeFileSync on openclaw.json which\n   fails with EROFS when the container or mount is read-only (docker-compose\n   uses read_only: true by default).\n\n3. install.sh never wrote the detected OPENCLAW_HOME or Docker host gateway\n   IP into .env, leaving OPENCLAW_HOME empty after a fresh install.\n\nFixes\n-----\n- nodes/route.ts: replace HTTP calls to /api/presence and /api/devices\n  with gateway /health reachability check + callOpenClawGateway() RPC\n  (node.list / device.pair.list). When the openclaw CLI is unavailable\n  inside Docker, the RPC falls back gracefully and returns connected=true\n  with an empty list rather than a misleading ''Gateway offline'' error.\n  POST device actions likewise use callOpenClawGateway instead of /api/rpc.\n\n- gateway-runtime.ts: catch EROFS / EACCES / EPERM on config write and\n  emit a warn-level log with a hint, instead of an error. This eliminates\n  the ''Failed to register MC in gateway config EROFS: read-only file\n  system'' log spam on Docker installs where openclaw.json is read-only.\n\n- install.sh: after generating .env, write the detected OPENCLAW_HOME.\n  In --docker mode also detect the Docker host IP (host-gateway or bridge\n  default) and set OPENCLAW_GATEWAY_HOST so the container can reach a\n  gateway running on the host out of the box.\n\n- docker-compose.yml: add extra_hosts host-gateway so the container can\n  resolve the Docker host IP; add a commented volume snippet for mounting\n  the OpenClaw state directory read-only.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJptR51CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAUb8QAJEWqeZKeu7ZXEao5qm6uFlT\n+a9wUaG5GHkYvc1KyFFSTdcU0E7/hPuXuJuBmGAFDjRWCF+4YrrSr1ieWYax6nQq\nT2T50t9ZaBZ3RlD6+TimN228qn7qoCDy4gcoHZZPpMx14+91rzHBQ8N0I86CCG/Z\nXU087RZK7y9exq+oBNE7J1gnM+I+uOsyMfFEGSui2r2v4JjHd20W/eZo1/NyaQpk\nQ/72cGFTcPwUbHdkImDGfhvqO6YR/mqXRj4fS8cbCbi0o9kIDsVljjjgbgBrbZmF\nuEgX2fXXEugx2wIbKiK0o1g+5FsXZXlwdumQvfVdOwUxekeAY9H94FCYqNghJK4f\nIjy0RFXwmLXT7NqYDKYTPM8PA5JPH20zdp8reSyJ9POazMIs+97JiHoUAqIDFuvE\n0KFUT41zmF2o7PQheH1rW7OvpJn0vPAKYsxOawpyXmW0dNQSGD5aQWXqsnpyPMj9\nXYJyJr3o6d+xC1NrVjBSt/hHxMfa260Xozda9R0m6+nUS11oZICpIfphjKTjV7tD\nOxFDh1EnnY4+6bFuS0mCykOe+uuiI1dJPhZICpmyYoohNhadRCarMXcssNrOy/UD\nNQ7MBXKcE+HuQ6buv1eReYOFoZbBSMP4tKcXZ07OeDXnYrSDayIeM97JDuObZ6iD\n27Ejsh2saiHeCA/oeJwF\n=vEWl\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-03-26T20:38:47Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/watson-gpositive/custom-mission-control/commit/8706147f84a39959b1fe1c3121e310a6aebebb03","node_id":"C_kwDORxyPE9oAKDg3MDYxNDdmODRhMzk5NTliMWZlMWMzMTIxZTMxMGE2YWViZWJiMDM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/watson-gpositive/custom-mission-control/commit/2b4438b63a73e589a0ff9ff47c480e0d6cc84f6b","sha":"2b4438b63a73e589a0ff9ff47c480e0d6cc84f6b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/watson-gpositive/custom-mission-control/commits/2b4438b63a73e589a0ff9ff47c480e0d6cc84f6b"}],"sha":"8706147f84a39959b1fe1c3121e310a6aebebb03","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/watson-gpositive/custom-mission-control/commits/8706147f84a39959b1fe1c3121e310a6aebebb03"}],"requestUrl":"https://api.github.com/repos/watson-gpositive/custom-mission-control/commits?per_page=100&page=1&sha=4020847053842ca49e2a5b01c5723cdfca370904&since=2025-03-31T23%3A59%3A59.000Z&until=2026-10-08T16%3A21%3A39.241Z"}');
