":{"login":"PanoramicRum","providerType":"User"},"email":"richy@nimiq.com","name":"Richy"},"observedAt":"2026-10-08T22:23:16.201Z","repositoryId":1193063396,"sha":"6da44239b8400b02d782546ad8058d2a1a366db4"},{"author":{"account":{"login":"PanoramicRum","providerType":"User"},"email":"richy@nimiq.com","name":"Richy"},"authoredDate":"2026-05-05T01:28:11Z","committedDate":"2026-05-05T01:28:11Z","committer":{"account":{"login":"PanoramicRum","providerType":"User"},"email":"richy@nimiq.com","name":"Richy"},"observedAt":"2026-10-08T22:23:16.201Z","repositoryId":1193063396,"sha":"fdcf2c33ca335e813cece5b2d0ed9b5402107357"}],"observedAt":"2026-10-08T22:23:16.201Z","raw":[{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6556452?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/PanoramicRum","id":6556452,"login":"PanoramicRum","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY1NTY0NTI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/urule-ai/urule/commits/5b517017074d2c7de61094762ef1c4418e1e7c88/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-06-09T20:14:16Z","email":"ricardobarcar@gmail.com","name":"PanoramicRum"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-06-09T20:14:16Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(registry): membership-gate org-scoped reads (#4) (#128)\n\n`GET /orgs/:orgId` and `GET /orgs/:orgId/workspaces` were ungated: any\nauthenticated user could read another tenant''s org metadata or enumerate\nits workspace list just by changing `:orgId` (a read-IDOR — the last\nopen read gap in the registry under #4).\n\nBoth now run `requireMembership(orgParamResolver(), { objectType: ''org'' })`.\n`orgParamResolver()` (new, in authz.ts, mirrors `workspaceParamResolver`)\nreturns the `:orgId` path param directly — the org IS the addressed\nresource, so no DB lookup. The gate checks the `member` relation on\n`org:<id>`; per the OpenFGA model (packages/authz/src/model.ts) org\n`member` = direct ∪ admin ∪ owner, so the org creator (seeded as owner)\nand admins can still read. Org `member` has no `parent` userset, so a\nmember of a workspace *inside* the org is NOT an org member — no upward\ninheritance, no cross-tenant bypass.\n\n`GET /orgs` and `POST /orgs` stay `requireRole(''admin'')`; there are no\nother org-addressed routes (audited every method on the path).\n\n+10 guard tests (org-scoped-read-guard.test.ts): 403 non-member,\n401 anon, 403 workspace-member-but-not-org-member, 200 org member,\n200 admin bypass — across both routes. Tests fail if the preHandler is\nremoved (not a placebo); the mock authz client is direct-match, so the\nno-upward-inheritance case is genuinely exercised.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"6ba5c49cef1529076760d7a36c9ad302171a6fa6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/urule-ai/urule/git/trees/6ba5c49cef1529076760d7a36c9ad302171a6fa6"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/urule-ai/urule/git/commits/5b517017074d2c7de61094762ef1c4418e1e7c88","verification":{"payload":"tree 6ba5c49cef1529076760d7a36c9ad302171a6fa6\nparent 736d86c5a9fc6cb48c2ab9c232c43805f477d717\nauthor PanoramicRum <ricardobarcar@gmail.com> 1781036056 -0600\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1781036056 -0600\n\nfix(registry): membership-gate org-scoped reads (#4) (#128)\n\n`GET /orgs/:orgId` and `GET /orgs/:orgId/workspaces` were ungated: any\nauthenticated user could read another tenant''s org metadata or enumerate\nits workspace list just by changing `:orgId` (a read-IDOR — the last\nopen read gap in the registry under #4).\n\nBoth now run `requireMembership(orgParamResolver(), { objectType: ''org'' })`.\n`orgParamResolver()` (new, in authz.ts, mirrors `workspaceParamResolver`)\nreturns the `:orgId` path param directly — the org IS the addressed\nresource, so no DB lookup. The gate checks the `member` relation on\n`org:<id>`; per the OpenFGA model (packages/authz/src/model.ts) org\n`member` = direct ∪ admin ∪ owner, so the org creator (seeded as owner)\nand admins can still read. Org `member` has no `parent` userset, so a\nmember of a workspace *inside* the org is NOT an org member — no upward\ninheritance, no cross-tenant bypass.\n\n`GET /orgs` and `POST /orgs` stay `requireRole(''admin'')`; there are no\nother org-addressed routes (audited every method on the path).\n\n+10 guard tests (org-scoped-read-guard.test.ts): 403 non-member,\n401 anon, 403 workspace-member-but-not-org-member, 200 org member,\n200 admin bypass — across both routes. Tests fail if the preHandler is\nremoved (not a placebo); the mock authz client is direct-match, so the\nno-upward-inheritance case is genuinely exercised.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqKHQYCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAcHUQAI+f5NkSuczqOl7vQf/cWuh2\nFuDWg3beLdj6Z3JPVlrv8HhubDrzVMAtx4YtdhIOd+wMt3BS3Z3fHw+n7d8u7izQ\nC38TSOcrAoZ3eWAjuJCOh+zgDdXYmZnfJ5ZQ9mYbNUfMbaihsBK2nsz05uEfsFf9\njkjUoY4fblFvxGMl/76LwqJuGAjf6GGnEHIF0t56DX8KXZrbgKJPjemZSyfFv8BW\nLd5Or1/NMHiOxO2O6TUPP1pOkTPRv4YhOIA3PIgSCe3xn6FJbre+pa0A2ULRQ9Ca\n3Y4skvZvh7bu+8lKdCec4w8EIal8OHL3yUMobkt2+uwrw6DgDZOHZoCLr5qyscls\nCWpESDqPlYMbHSAzWibHq9cs/7BVxAFE+1xZSSGljMeh/7GThSsyACC5igrW+Y0P\nwudV1wixlHoZ+HXmjWEJEPEuwkg+OjAjmGu9YGrVXQJ7TzD9WAWDx8y1Bbqks1gq\nx+YxCtaw7Ul4CgZbEPvqMmmOjhKzwuPmIefvzSuTIRi92mvzwffY3qV0JPYjhxBB\nCmrSInD3J5bWqbVted3ViSOkJWld4mrT3BFtLKLfwDrKhFPX8kshXu2mktQX7vVf\nAE3pmL4ObpRQZ7UB9jIje4U2BH715sdD3GFWW1iaon1swQchW7YdPl4+OPMxdMkT\nnDdkyBcwkmVgfPjKx+JQ\n=oaM5\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-06-09T20:14:17Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/urule-ai/urule/commit/5b517017074d2c7de61094762ef1c4418e1e7c88","node_id":"C_kwDORxyz5NoAKDViNTE3MDE3MDc0ZDJjN2RlNjEwOTQ3NjJlZjFjNDQxOGUxZTdjODg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/urule-ai/urule/commit/736d86c5a9fc6cb48c2ab9c232c43805f477d717","sha":"736d86c5a9fc6cb48c2ab9c232c43805f477d717","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/urule-ai/urule/commits/736d86c5a9fc6cb48c2ab9c232c43805f477d717"}],"sha":"5b517017074d2c7de61094762ef1c4418e1e7c88","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/urule-ai/urule/commits/5b517017074d2c7de61094762ef1c4418e1e7c88"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6556452?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/PanoramicRum","id":6556452,"login":"PanoramicRum","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY1NTY0NTI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/urule-ai/urule/commits/736d86c5a9fc6cb48c2ab9c232c43805f477d717/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-06-07T19:06:25Z","email":"ricardobarcar@gmail.com","name":"PanoramicRum"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-06-07T19:06:25Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(registry): membership-gate per-id resource reads (#4) (#127)\n\n* fix(registry): membership-gate per-id resource reads (#4)\n\nKnowing a ULID let any authenticated user read another workspace''s resource by\nid (read-IDOR). Resolve each resource''s workspace and require membership on the\nper-id GET routes: agents (/:id + /metrics /health /conversations /logs),\nconversations (/:id + /messages /branches), providers (/:id masked), and runtimes\n(/:id, via a new runtimeWorkspaceResolver). GET /providers/:id/key keeps its own\ninline admin gate (the service-caller path). +29 guard tests (every gated route:\nnon-member 403 + anon 401; member/admin 200 on the representative detail routes).\n\nNote: the langgraph-adapter calls GET /agents/:id and GET /conversations/:id/messages with no auth header (only correlation-id). Safe today — the phase6 stack runs SKIP_AUTH=true so the registry treats it as the mock admin user (bypass). Under real auth the adapter already 401s on these (and already can''t reach the admin-gated /providers/:id/key), so this introduces no new breakage; giving internal callers a service identity is the pre-existing prerequisite for enabling real auth.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(registry): also gate GET /agents/:agentId/memories (#4 review follow-up)\n\nThe per-id read-IDOR pass (029e17c4) gated every agent detail read except\nGET /api/v1/agents/:agentId/memories — the POST and DELETE on the same\nresource were gated with requireAgentMembership, but the companion GET was\nmissed, so any authenticated user could read another workspace''s agent\nmemories by knowing the agent ULID. Add the same preHandler, and add the\nroute to the guard test''s ALL_GATED list (403 non-member + 401 anon).\n\nCaught by an independent fresh-context adversarial review of 029e17c4.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"19fc40a03f97e5c0219fcc5f8d903dd34d3ec3bd","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/urule-ai/urule/git/trees/19fc40a03f97e5c0219fcc5f8d903dd34d3ec3bd"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/urule-ai/urule/git/commits/736d86c5a9fc6cb48c2ab9c232c43805f477d717","verification":{"payload":"tree 19fc40a03f97e5c0219fcc5f8d903dd34d3ec3bd\nparent 34d0eb22bc01748d791f6ccbad2131cced3d79cd\nauthor PanoramicRum <ricardobarcar@gmail.com> 1780859185 -0600\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1780859185 -0600\n\nfix(registry): membership-gate per-id resource reads (#4) (#127)\n\n* fix(registry): membership-gate per-id resource reads (#4)\n\nKnowing a ULID let any authenticated user read another workspace''s resource by\nid (read-IDOR). Resolve each resource''s workspace and require membership on the\nper-id GET routes: agents (/:id + /metrics /health /conversations /logs),\nconversations (/:id + /messages /branches), providers (/:id masked), and runtimes\n(/:id, via a new runtimeWorkspaceResolver). GET /providers/:id/key keeps its own\ninline admin gate (the service-caller path). +29 guard tests (every gated route:\nnon-member 403 + anon 401; member/admin 200 on the representative detail routes).\n\nNote: the langgraph-adapter calls GET /agents/:id and GET /conversations/:id/messages with no auth header (only correlation-id). Safe today — the phase6 stack runs SKIP_AUTH=true so the registry treats it as the mock admin user (bypass). Under real auth the adapter already 401s on these (and already can''t reach the admin-gated /providers/:id/key), so this introduces no new breakage; giving internal callers a service identity is the pre-existing prerequisite for enabling real auth.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(registry): also gate GET /agents/:agentId/memories (#4 review follow-up)\n\nThe per-id read-IDOR pass (029e17c4) gated every agent detail read except\nGET /api/v1/agents/:agentId/memories — the POST and DELETE on the same\nresource were gated with requireAgentMembership, but the companion GET was\nmissed, so any authenticated user could read another workspace''s agent\nmemories by knowing the agent ULID. Add the same preHandler, and add the\nroute to the guard test''s ALL_GATED list (403 non-member + 401 anon).\n\nCaught by an independent fresh-context adversarial review of 029e17c4.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqJcExCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA12UQAFtNEBLwMsJwLDvyIln2c+ba\nC7XkI9VGqi9u7C2oTPe+wNJ7phE40zpI5pv5F5xJTuOEzLjwGzZeU1c4qYmegpS4\nt7