nthe admin list (now a shared decorateConversations helper), and a non-member\ncan''t use it to enumerate another workspace. +5 guard tests (non-member 403,\nanon 401, member 200, admin bypass, decorated shape).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(office-ui): scope chat + meetings lists to the workspace conversations route (#4)\n\nMove the chat list and meetings list off the admin-only GET /conversations onto\nGET /workspaces/:wsId/conversations via useWorkspaceId (mirrors the #95 agent-list\nmigration): workspaceId in the query key, enabled: !!workspaceId guard. Existing\n[\"conversations\"]/[\"meetings\"] invalidations still prefix-match the new keys.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"f86fdd89dd40b8e142263eedc9bb38e47d66647a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/urule-ai/urule/git/trees/f86fdd89dd40b8e142263eedc9bb38e47d66647a"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/urule-ai/urule/git/commits/db556dbd87edae56c2faabc021ec0603549ea55c","verification":{"payload":"tree f86fdd89dd40b8e142263eedc9bb38e47d66647a\nparent 4eb8c51af75dda5bec4fd60392d8c915a7d46e7b\nauthor PanoramicRum <ricardobarcar@gmail.com> 1780699389 -0600\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1780699389 -0600\n\nfix(security): scope office-ui conversations lists to the workspace (#4) (#124)\n\n* feat(registry): add membership-gated GET /workspaces/:wsId/conversations (#4)\n\noffice-ui''s chat + meetings lists were calling the admin-only cross-workspace\nGET /api/v1/conversations, so non-admin members got 403s. Add a workspace-scoped\nlist gated by requireMembership(:wsId) (the established #4 resolve→membership\npattern) — it returns the same agents/message_count/last_message decoration as\nthe admin list (now a shared decorateConversations helper), and a non-member\ncan''t use it to enumerate another workspace. +5 guard tests (non-member 403,\nanon 401, member 200, admin bypass, decorated shape).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(office-ui): scope chat + meetings lists to the workspace conversations route (#4)\n\nMove the chat list and meetings list off the admin-only GET /conversations onto\nGET /workspaces/:wsId/conversations via useWorkspaceId (mirrors the #95 agent-list\nmigration): workspaceId in the query key, enabled: !!workspaceId guard. Existing\n[\"conversations\"]/[\"meetings\"] invalidations still prefix-match the new keys.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqI1D9CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAFEYQAF08c3+CTyUx5SDL9fkPOe3r\nhyDJthvoghhOnPXaz1DNV9RR+LurZXQcquoQbK6T4xc8eyt6BFo5JXImilb4dqvS\n8G4AutbYprBTslKT9UydOMivXkWTRm2QoPFnZZy7bIyKm7bo6WTM6XNURQwAmDxM\nxVzyte9vfz6QYGAIsFqMofLbGXFPTwLlp9kiikg8TZEt2j4csAYT6mQ3mJ90I6AB\nb5tj209BTux9gaN6Nrpt+MAH4SuKez7x3h+v3iMYogAoYOWYR332KAoI26vCZ1Zv\n+GygaE2G4ROoCoDqQDYpsv1b8dye8/JnnWGADUxOYlxOa7Cezyl9Zm/63UW/mtbh\nxWI3EmRw42cMdpY6yDDH2BBu9FiJiFR6+jRD08nVHdVQbGoUAk8CplyXTFsQRb6E\ny6+Y3TdBIoFrrdRW/LtCsKS13/cfndABpePoImaQ3XACNWN1JpwUMrUAUljKNvt3\n7ok4s0enqwe6vWQbKY/yre8471fAzMv2Nh9RVv+BIM+hHWRcp91LG2UjPi6Il5bu\nId54oivwesHI4Goe/Kp8U+YRRZrnAYRHMMCWKKkDhoReZPrA2lD6hRgKX293uDAq\negoXtgQSQg4po11Cgtno8BN7RHnBvztgX0eTRVc8YkVBTQVHbY0Abmsyg6oDptVK\nTTJydHnWOIE1HKVn9xRD\n=k3WF\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-06-05T22:43:09Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/urule-ai/urule/commit/db556dbd87edae56c2faabc021ec0603549ea55c","node_id":"C_kwDORxyz5NoAKGRiNTU2ZGJkODdlZGFlNTZjMmZhYWJjMDIxZWMwNjAzNTQ5ZWE1NWM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/urule-ai/urule/commit/4eb8c51af75dda5bec4fd60392d8c915a7d46e7b","sha":"4eb8c51af75dda5bec4fd60392d8c915a7d46e7b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/urule-ai/urule/commits/4eb8c51af75dda5bec4fd60392d8c915a7d46e7b"}],"sha":"db556dbd87edae56c2faabc021ec0603549ea55c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/urule-ai/urule/commits/db556dbd87edae56c2faabc021ec0603549ea55c"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6556452?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/PanoramicRum","id":6556452,"login":"PanoramicRum","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY1NTY0NTI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/urule-ai/urule/commits/4eb8c51af75dda5bec4fd60392d8c915a7d46e7b/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-06-05T15:00:17Z","email":"ricardobarcar@gmail.com","name":"PanoramicRum"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-06-05T15:00:17Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(security): verify widget manifest signatures before iframe load (#39) (#123)\n\n* feat(office-ui): verify widget manifest signatures before iframe load (#39)\n\nHost-side enforcement of packagehub Ed25519 publisher signatures for external\n(iframe) marketplace widgets — closes the latent #39 / Q-M-13 hole where a\ntampered manifest could point entryUrl at attacker infrastructure. Native\nin-bundle widgets are unaffected; fail-closed for legacy/unverified entries.\n\n- gate install, boot-hydration, and render on packagehub''s /verify endpoint\n- bind the verified version to the installed manifest via widgetInstallTarget so\n  a yanked-latest can''t verify one version while registering another''s entryUrl\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* refactor(spec): align WidgetManifest with the runtime widget-sdk shape (#39)\n\nThe spec''s embedded widget config used a dead `entrypoint` field with zero\nconsumers; packagehub publishes manifests with z.object({}).loose() so it was\nnever enforced. Replace it with the real runtime shape (entryType / entryUrl /\ncomponentPath / mountPoints / ...) that widget-sdk and office-ui already use, so\nthe signed field name is unambiguous across repos. Adds a widget-pack example +\npositive/negative validator tests.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* test(office-ui): make widget verify/gate binding genuinely regression-proof (#39)\n\nAddresses an independent-review finding: the prior widgetInstallTarget unit\ntest pinned the helper''s contract but not the call site, so a future revert that\nverified the page-level (newest non-yanked) version again would pass silently.\nExtract the install decision into a pure, dependency-injected\ninstallWidgetFromPackage() and test it directly: verify is always called with the\nmanifest''s source version; an external widget that fails (or throws during)\nverification is never installed or registered; native widgets skip verification.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"abec04442760478caac55881d56b7d2c0bc9cfdc","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/urule-ai/urule/git/trees/abec04442760478caac55881d56b7d2c0bc9cfdc"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/urule-ai/urule/git/commits/4eb8c51af75dda5bec4fd60392d8c915a7d46e7b","verification":{"payload":"tree abec04442760478caac55881d56b7d2c0bc9cfdc\nparent 1a1aac25eab4b52462eb76828f532b96e40d741f\nauthor PanoramicRum <ricardobarcar@gmail.com> 1780671617 -0600\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1780671617 -0600\n\nfeat(security): verify widget manifest signatures before iframe load (#39) (#123)\n\n* feat(office-ui): verify widget manifest signatures before iframe load (#39)\n\nHost-side enforcement of packagehub Ed25519 publisher signatures for external\n(iframe) marketplace widgets — closes the latent #39 / Q-M-13 hole where a\ntampered manifest could point entryUrl at attacker infrastructure. Native\nin-bundle widgets are unaffected; fail-closed for legacy/unverified entries.\n\n- gate install, boot-hydration, and render on packagehub''s /verify endpoint\n- bind the verified version to the installed manifest via widgetInstallTarget so\n  a yanked-latest can''t verify one version while registering another''s entryUrl\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* refactor(spec): align WidgetManifest with the runtime widget-sdk shape (#39)\n\nThe spec''s embedded widget config used a dead `entrypoint` field with zero\nconsumers; packagehub publishes manifests with z.object({}).loose() so it was\nnever enforced. Replace it with the real runtime shape (entryType / entryUrl /\ncomponentPath / mountPoints / ...) that widget-sdk and office-ui already use, so\nthe signed field name is unambiguous across repos. Adds a widget-pack example +\npositive/negative validator tests.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* test(office-ui): make widget verify/gate binding genuinely regression-proof (#39)\n\nAddresses an independent-review finding: the prior widgetInstallTarget unit\ntest pinned the helper''s contract but not the call site, so a future revert that\nverified the page-level (newest non-yanked) version again would pass silently.\nExtract the install decision into a pure, dependency-injected\ninstallWidgetFromPackage() and test it directly: verify is always called with the\nmanifest''s source version; an external widget that fails (or throws during)\nverification is never installed or registered; native widgets skip verification.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqIuSBCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA16IQAGUoRVJQOH1pnkiFhLjiRrBQ\nKg0T96bhpdcjtQ3qqC6M6ClwtCdpKw63Ag3Tep5Gd3j9co7wzfDBt7Twj7ibhLfg\n2ALA1H2FphqTphT5FbOnXwgWhwFqVNjqF/AltC0FcxNGOFEhF4oQoWDrj05jwPBw\nC/7l7sfaPlr9zgxNDFb8To6JkoG63pzkqm0518Z74UIC+ADoKqkYPr41hvJiaIIi\nnrywxDV5DwNPSdGwm9l97ic5kXNPbWnxM0GL1aA3E93M5NYJLmrG5mmMCShXGPgV\nPNM4mu82wJoGgAgupKa/Rn1C8A+NzD1cz7QI60oYeGaXjVeX+m2VW+POyC9E1KCb\nTlylpo8wFis+CiryktnTAkwAKkgcED2gLz5gzw1R7NZg13488tkH6rgRU0GTIIBx\nc8BjkepJPhJq+kxmaNjuz/w3RGBVyvaTDlIIY7obTZ0thEJwqeRf6snWJFt05M3C\ngZDqQr4SmRl0+Mdmu9wTCmgQ1az3gR7CjfYGVaGOYJyK1trDKYL2