cRum/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/PanoramicRum","id":6556452,"login":"PanoramicRum","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY1NTY0NTI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/urule-ai/urule/commits/1a1aac25eab4b52462eb76828f532b96e40d741f/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-06-04T18:13:43Z","email":"ricardobarcar@gmail.com","name":"PanoramicRum"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-06-04T18:13:43Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(security): scope office-ui agent lists to the workspace (#95) (#122)\n\nAfter #25 made `GET /api/v1/agents` admin-only, the office-ui''s 9 agent-list\nqueries 403 for non-admin users (they only work in the dev compose, which runs\nSKIP_AUTH=true). Move them onto the documented workspace-scoped path.\n\n- New `useWorkspaceId()` hook resolves the current workspace via\n  `GET /api/v1/workspaces/current` (member-accessible — NOT the admin-only\n  cross-workspace `/workspaces` list).\n- All 9 agent-list queries now call `GET /api/v1/workspaces/:wsId/agents` with\n  `enabled: !!workspaceId` and `workspaceId` in the query key: agents,\n  agents/new, agents/[id], chat, chat/[conversationId], meetings, meetings/[id],\n  projects, office.\n- Server: the workspace-scoped list now decorates each agent with its\n  `model_provider` (shared `decorateAgentsWithProviders` helper, also used by the\n  admin list) so the response shape is identical — several UI sites read\n  `agent.model_provider.provider` and would crash on a bare row. (The per-row\n  provider lookup is an N+1, #32 — unchanged behavior; batch when #32 lands.)\n\nTests: +1 registry test locking the scoped route''s provider decoration (118\ngreen). office-ui + registry typecheck green.\n\nNote: #95 part 1 (admin-gating the cross-workspace list routes) was already\ncomplete — workspaces/orgs/providers/agents/conversations are gated and there is\nno bare `GET /api/v1/runtimes`. This PR is part 2 (the office-ui migration).\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"c238c2cbcee90fb68451132744d940db552b5312","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/urule-ai/urule/git/trees/c238c2cbcee90fb68451132744d940db552b5312"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/urule-ai/urule/git/commits/1a1aac25eab4b52462eb76828f532b96e40d741f","verification":{"payload":"tree c238c2cbcee90fb68451132744d940db552b5312\nparent 2831e476ebb3a78d879536aa9326a64792a8a87c\nauthor PanoramicRum <ricardobarcar@gmail.com> 1780596823 -0600\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1780596823 -0600\n\nfeat(security): scope office-ui agent lists to the workspace (#95) (#122)\n\nAfter #25 made `GET /api/v1/agents` admin-only, the office-ui''s 9 agent-list\nqueries 403 for non-admin users (they only work in the dev compose, which runs\nSKIP_AUTH=true). Move them onto the documented workspace-scoped path.\n\n- New `useWorkspaceId()` hook resolves the current workspace via\n  `GET /api/v1/workspaces/current` (member-accessible — NOT the admin-only\n  cross-workspace `/workspaces` list).\n- All 9 agent-list queries now call `GET /api/v1/workspaces/:wsId/agents` with\n  `enabled: !!workspaceId` and `workspaceId` in the query key: agents,\n  agents/new, agents/[id], chat, chat/[conversationId], meetings, meetings/[id],\n  projects, office.\n- Server: the workspace-scoped list now decorates each agent with its\n  `model_provider` (shared `decorateAgentsWithProviders` helper, also used by the\n  admin list) so the response shape is identical — several UI sites read\n  `agent.model_provider.provider` and would crash on a bare row. (The per-row\n  provider lookup is an N+1, #32 — unchanged behavior; batch when #32 lands.)\n\nTests: +1 registry test locking the scoped route''s provider decoration (118\ngreen). office-ui + registry typecheck green.\n\nNote: #95 part 1 (admin-gating the cross-workspace list routes) was already\ncomplete — workspaces/orgs/providers/agents/conversations are gated and there is\nno bare `GET /api/v1/runtimes`. This PR is part 2 (the office-ui migration).\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqIcBXCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAHa8QAFBlE/J0N4xUDJrJw7syi7pj\nJMhr2XPwoFkyhIcWLPxDmOdhHQ3VVdYBSN6uWLWN8gTzWq0y0fg7NHEuEr5UzENv\nD8wmzhodRBWeYXfaodo5inmWdo7DWqvBGN2jb9yorcilVksJdfiQfurU1d2+iUb5\nB0U20JzT3LKFx0BWQtdH3mUYkKlVLiuhjvtjIeNkIGKEB8CZlGlY9fCM3CxBmfjC\nav6burCHIMc/4jdad9/S1QgNBN4cKpYeHcDOPGT1NfBrbYi/PEoo/R+gbGZSzMCj\n8B1ZhmlkFTQzY5ZJSZTqt2BBe6hm8a/AwnZp+IgJWCj1f5i+LNumhnHzpBBPfVGJ\nvKvdxy158VRcwTJJvYvtGKefs6XnV1KwC/vLfbnmeataynipWNkmkQlS3RleraMo\nu8eJX1eryFwHQOoNSqEJUSfRwqd6b0Yy2Pgp1ql/DQiFM5HgZKFzIb4Y7X1p69mK\nOn2+V50Ar+PFFmZpQuwSaZQHYKyuvoli09fTKAiEQgwL1xdsZHuQvc6wyomHEdih\nKIpvNgk3wUyIa1OVwlh7Fvi4M31CHNnugv3pjJhK71krZDff/VKNd4HS0gF1EwZf\nz2D6eTxKf0i7ZiPlKag7g3bZZv34iJkKgfJnH42x3zbRpx1rNezXc4EijUrvr2m0\nMD+RlUDixcAhhVKz/AoH\n=wLPY\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-06-04T18:13:44Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/urule-ai/urule/commit/1a1aac25eab4b52462eb76828f532b96e40d741f","node_id":"C_kwDORxyz5NoAKDFhMWFhYzI1ZWFiNGI1MjQ2MmViNzY4MjhmNTMyYjk2ZTQwZDc0MWY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/urule-ai/urule/commit/2831e476ebb3a78d879536aa9326a64792a8a87c","sha":"2831e476ebb3a78d879536aa9326a64792a8a87c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/urule-ai/urule/commits/2831e476ebb3a78d879536aa9326a64792a8a87c"}],"sha":"1a1aac25eab4b52462eb76828f532b96e40d741f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/urule-ai/urule/commits/1a1aac25eab4b52462eb76828f532b96e40d741f"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6556452?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/PanoramicRum","id":6556452,"login":"PanoramicRum","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY1NTY0NTI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/urule-ai/urule/commits/2831e476ebb3a78d879536aa9326a64792a8a87c/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-06-04T17:49:43Z","email":"ricardobarcar@gmail.com","name":"PanoramicRum"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-06-04T17:49:43Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(security): harden Stripe webhook tail — Zod-parse body (#48) + idempotency constraint (#33) (#121)\n\nTwo small follow-ons on the path Phase Q (#119) just touched.\n\n#48 — the `Stripe-Signature` HMAC proves the body came from Stripe, but not\nthat it has the shape the handler reads. Replace the `request.body as\nStripeEvent` cast with a Zod `stripeEventSchema.safeParse()` (after signature\nverification): a malformed / partial payload is now a clean 400 MALFORMED_EVENT\ninstead of a runtime throw (500) deep in the handler. `mode` / `payment_status`\nare parsed as loose strings on purpose so an unrecognised-but-valid Stripe value\nfalls through to the safe no-mint path rather than 400 (which Stripe retries\nforever). Unknown top-level Stripe fields are stripped, not rejected.\n\n#33 — the webhook keyed idempotency on (packageId, externalRef) via a\nSELECT-then-INSERT, which races under Stripe''s at-least-once delivery (two\nconcurrent deliveries both find no row, both insert → duplicate entitlements).\nAdd a unique index on (package_id, external_ref) and switch the INSERT to\n`ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING` + read-back, so a lost race resolves to the existing\nrow (200 idempotent) instead of a duplicate or a 500. `external_ref` is NULL for\nmanual grants — Postgres treats NULLs as distinct, so manual grants are\nunaffected. The migration de-dupes any pre-existing duplicate rows\ndeterministically (earliest per key, ULID tie-break) before creating the index\nso it can''t fail on legacy data.\n\nTests: +3 (malformed body → 400, non-string metadata → 400, lost-race delivery →\n200 idempotent via the constraint). Full packagehub suite green (122).\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"fe0c3eb707c46b936c9da28335ba6d542c44fa5a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/urule-ai/urule/git/trees/fe0c3eb707c46b936c9da28335ba6d542c44fa5a"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/urule-ai/urule/git/commits/2831e476ebb3a78d879536aa9326a64792a8a87c","verification":{"payload":"tree fe0c3eb707c46b936c9da28335ba6d542c44fa5a\nparent 225869c02d52ab39875feb3f61099090797da202\nauthor PanoramicRum <ricardobarcar@gmail.com> 1780595383 -0600\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1780595383 -0600\n\nfeat(security): harden Stripe webhook tail — Zod-parse body (#48) + idempotency constraint (#33) (#121)\n\nTwo small follow-ons on the path Phase Q (#119) just touched.\n\n#48 — the `Stripe-Signature` HMAC proves the body came from Stripe, but not\nthat it has the shape the handler reads. Replace the `request.body as\nStripeEvent` cast with a Zod `stripeEventSchema.safeParse()` (after signature\nverification): a malformed / partial payload is now a clean 400 MALFORMED_EVENT\ninstead of a runtime throw (500) deep in the handler. `mode` / `payment_status`\nare parsed as loose strings on purpose so an unrecognised-but-valid Stripe value\nfalls through to the safe no-mint path rather than 400 (which Stripe retries\nforever). Unknown top-level Stripe fields are stripped, not rejected.\n\n#33 — the webhook keyed idempotency on (packageId, externalRef) via a\nSELECT-then-INSERT, which races under Stripe''s at-least-once delivery (two\nconcurrent deliveries both find no row, both insert → duplicate entitlements).\nAdd a unique index on (package_id, external_ref) and switch the INSERT to\n`ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING` + read-back, so a lost race resolves to the existing\nrow (200 idempotent) instead of a duplicate or a 500. `external_ref` is NULL for\nmanual grants — Postgres treats NULLs as distinct, so manual grants are\nunaffected. The migration de-dupes any pre-existing duplicate rows\ndeterministically (earliest per key, ULID tie-break) before creating the index\nso it can''t fail on legacy data.\n\nTests: +3 (malformed body → 400, non-string metadata → 400, lost-race delivery →\n200 idempotent via the constraint). Full packagehub suite green (122).\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqIbq3CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAs6QQAK1Mw8gpAMZRdwlFADbkEjsN\nGXHLZZ339FKNtn0VdPRGD71BH+CN0z2J8exkmExVhImuh0SkDGbkJUV4WfDApBzW\nQ9l5Vj7YEW+4XBe5wFUzolYGIF4ChQmIV/NVperih7Xdm1z+b0bXwv94ujlOb/Xs\n4JP/ounOK6LU57kSIwcJ2TxhDpEIn669Fvvz2/b6CPSKj/1wmDORLQqWZAMqF1pD\nszQXs9EAwfV8qQZp/D8hFFrEHYwJ7TXy2ejoi9q1ZX1hFN620QnGrHQAaf6YpMGM\nOWqNwviDrjV6TT7pLRyhdvQlZm6ObO6rsAtnSorebDmtmAaGtLWx7p5iLoJPlPGc\nJUTeS2cHxLSI0Zghj9UqqStquRpMDrcIoTwjf3JF6MsGTctT3oYSGlF0ViANk9Uv\ne3LPLFwfARWgUvevIEa74FwRmVeS8Tmnjta7veQZBbcqBtLChbffCL3ddoQ5+npW\nssB2iqAI+uybMlTuiCksWkVKX3U4L7eftEMoNpovDO44ijHVOkjQuKxGRCjh5Bth\n7atOgoWdjJQNWzSR5Bkg3T0hUihjQJ+rxW/YWJBGnashwtVgzjHYO0aSLi9vvHOU\nt4CGjG4nFlESPS6MKSzgRkRTbu+5x9OmoFSpHZM/D/V6H0axL4n31SYhQCR2GTzR\nkeqXxNppYahA77BHyZLV\n=ocRe\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-06-04T17:49:43Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/urule-ai/urule/commit/2831e476ebb3a78d879536aa9326a64792a8a87c","node_id":"C_kwDORxyz5NoAKDI4MzFlNDc2ZWJiM2E3OGQ4Nzk1MzZhYTkzMjZhNjQ3OTJhOGE4N2M","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/urule-ai/urule/commit/225869c02d52ab39875feb3f61099090797da202","sha":"225869c02d52ab39875feb3f61099090797da202","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/urule-ai/urule/commits/225869c02d52ab39875feb3f61099090797da202"}],"sha":"2831e476ebb3a78d879536aa9326a64792a8a87c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/urule-ai/urule/commits/2831e476ebb3a78d879536aa9326a64792a8a87c"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6556452?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/PanoramicRum","id":6556452,"login":"PanoramicRum","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY1NTY0NTI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/urule-ai/urule/commits/225869c02d52ab39875feb3f61099090797da202/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-06-04T17:49:29Z","email":"ricardobarcar@gmail.com","name":"PanoramicRum"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-06-04T17:49:29Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(security): provider baseUrl egress allow-list (#6 / C-06) (#120)\n\nPhase R of the urule security cleanup. Closes #6 (C-06) — a workspace\nmember could PATCH/POST a provider `baseUrl` to an attacker host and\nsilently exfiltrate the API key + every chat payload the orchestrator\nadapter sends there (CWE-918 SSRF, CWE-522, CWE-862).\n\nAuthz on the mutation routes was already in place (requireProviderMembership,\nPR #104); this adds the missing server-side egress validation:\n\n- `getBaseUrlIssue()` allow-lists the recognised hosted endpoint per\n  provider kind (api.openai.com / api.anthropic.com /\n  generativelanguage.googleapis.com / *.openai.azure.com / openrouter.ai).\n  Any other host is a self-hosted / custom endpoint and now requires the\n  `admin` role — issue #6''s Ollama/vLLM model. A non-admin member can no\n  longer redirect provider egress off the hosted allow-list.\n- Hard SSRF stops applied to everyone (incl. admins): non-http(s) schemes\n  (blocks file:/gopher:), embedded credentials, plaintext downgrade of a\n  recognised hosted endpoint, and link-local / cloud-metadata addresses\n  (169.254.0.0/16, metadata.google.internal, fe80::/10).\n- Wired into both POST create and PATCH. PATCH only re-validates when the\n  request actually changes baseUrl, so unrelated updates to legacy rows\n  with a pre-existing custom baseUrl aren''t rejected retroactively.\n- baseUrl changes are now logged + audited explicitly (drift monitoring).\n\nAlso folds in #30: a `declare module ''fastify''` augmentation in\n@urule/auth-middleware types `request.uruleUser` (UruleUser | null),\ndropping the `(request as any).uruleUser` casts in providers.routes.ts.\n\nTests: 15 new — 10 pure-policy on `getBaseUrlIssue` (allow-list, look-alike\nhost, admin self-hosted Ollama/vLLM, metadata hard-stop incl. IPv6\nlink-local, scheme/credential/downgrade/malformed) and 5 route-level for\nthe admin-gate + metadata block on POST/PATCH, including a real non-admin\nmembership-tuple path. Full registry suite green (116), auth-middleware\ngreen (13), monorepo typecheck green.\n\nDeferred (issue #6 fix items 3–4, noted for follow-up): per-workspace\n`allow_self_hosted` flag + email notification, a dedicated baseUrl-change\nevent topic, and a key-rotation sentinel on baseUrl change.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"fcf5dd8ed95dde438ffacad884207d7d3c313643","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/urule-ai/urule/git/trees/fcf5dd8ed95dde438ffacad884207d7d3c313643"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/urule-ai/urule/git/commits/225869c02d52ab39875feb3f61099090797da202","verification":{"payload":"tree fcf5dd8ed95dde438ffacad884207d7d3c313643\nparent ad889977d9020d9f72beae0c7fa2943e587d27a3\nauthor PanoramicRum <ricardobarcar@gmail.com> 1780595369 -0600\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1780595369 -0600\n\nfeat(security): provider baseUrl egress allow-list (#6 / C-06) (#120)\n\nPhase R of the urule security cleanup. Closes #6 (C-06) — a workspace\nmember could PATCH/POST a provider `baseUrl` to an attacker host and\nsilently exfiltrate the API key + every chat payload the orchestrator\nadapter sends there (CWE-918 SSRF, CWE-522, CWE-862).\n\nAuthz on the mutation routes was already in place (requireProviderMembership,\nPR #104); this adds the missing server-side egress validation:\n\n- `getBaseUrlIssue()` allow-lists the recognised hosted endpoint per\n  provider kind (api.openai.com / api.anthropic.com /\n  generativelanguage.googleapis.com / *.openai.azure.com / openrouter.ai).\n  Any other host is a self-hosted / custom endpoint and now requires the\n  `admin` role — issue #6''s Ollama/vLLM model. A non-admin member can no\n  longer redirect provider egress off the hosted allow-list.\n- Hard SSRF stops applied to everyone (incl. admins): non-http(s) schemes\n  (blocks file:/gopher:), embedded credentials, plaintext downgrade of a\n  recognised hosted endpoint, and link-local / cloud-metadata addresses\n  (169.254.0.0/16, metadata.google.internal, fe80::/10).\n- Wired into both POST create and PATCH. PATCH only re-validates when the\n  request actually changes baseUrl, so unrelated updates to legacy rows\n  with a pre-existing custom baseUrl aren''t rejected retroactively.\n- baseUrl changes are now logged + audited explicitly (drift monitoring).\n\nAlso folds in #30: a `declare module ''fastify''` augmentation in\n@urule/auth-middleware types `request.uruleUser` (UruleUser | null),\ndropping the `(request as any).uruleUser` casts in providers.routes.ts.\n\nTests: 15 new — 10 pure-policy on `getBaseUrlIssue` (allow-list, look-alike\nhost, admin self-hosted Ollama/vLLM, metadata hard-stop incl. IPv6\nlink-local, scheme/credential/downgrade/malformed) and 5 route-level for\nthe admin-gate + metadata block on POST/PATCH, including a real non-admin\nmembership-tuple path. Full registry suite green (116), auth-middleware\ngreen (13), monorepo typecheck green.\n\nDeferred (issue #6 fix items 3–4, noted for follow-up): per-workspace\n`allow_self_hosted` flag + email notification, a dedicated baseUrl-change\nevent topic, and a key-rotation sentinel on baseUrl change.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqIbqpCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAJ8MQAA20Ig5NjLzlyVHgTz3p8EI5\n5Fb/VtQP2xMdy8ErzIRaiyuyPyrPjG9PCRDw9yrT31kQtcdcSDld3zTv7ajK9vZP\n4gL5QhN1wzuaQsEL29Reb5XCr3GG6pHJDcLasBA0qvnollN9/1dhqJMNhP3RYgLm\niwSGJqR6jfaccyzcLJZeWfCy8ZWGuHDJ4eD+XwKtKII32kk03oh66t2fTvJLcIpQ\nsVM/baqZADj0YN5GCPy9zX9c3zjBLFPa4rewu7hYPEDmhSsUP35ENMPGcukZcQvG\nAtW9laGL4IgohjOiqLls4o9bCGHYe6vKJi