97da202"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6556452?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/PanoramicRum","id":6556452,"login":"PanoramicRum","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY1NTY0NTI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/urule-ai/urule/commits/ad889977d9020d9f72beae0c7fa2943e587d27a3/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-06-04T09:40:53Z","email":"ricardobarcar@gmail.com","name":"PanoramicRum"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-06-04T09:40:53Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(security): Stripe webhook — kind from session.mode + payment_status gate (H-11) (#119)\n\n* feat(security): Stripe webhook — kind from session.mode, payment_status gate (H-11)\n\nPhase Q of the urule security cleanup. Closes urule#17 (H-11).\n\nThe webhook had four flaws flagged by the audit; this PR fixes the\nfirst three (the fourth — workspaceId/userId trust — is a bigger\nredesign, tracked as follow-up).\n\n1. **`kind` from publisher metadata, not authoritative Stripe field.**\n   A publisher could create a one-time payment Checkout session with\n   `metadata.kind: ''subscription''` and mint a never-expiring\n   entitlement (the expiresAt path requires a real subscription\n   object, but `kind` was recorded as `subscription`). Now derived\n   strictly from `session.mode`: `payment → purchase`, `subscription\n   → subscription`, `setup` and absent → no mint with\n   `ignored: ''unsupported_mode''`.\n\n2. **No `payment_status` gate.** `checkout.session.completed` fires\n   BEFORE the money lands for delayed-payment methods (ACH, BNPL).\n   Granting before settlement let a buyer who never pays access the\n   package. Now requires `payment_status === ''paid'' |\n   ''no_payment_required''`; an `''unpaid''` session returns 200\n   `ignored: ''awaiting_settlement''` and the route waits for the\n   companion `checkout.session.async_payment_succeeded` event.\n\n3. **`async_payment_succeeded` event not handled.** The settlement\n   companion for delayed payments was being ignored. Added to the\n   mint-event allowlist, gated by the same payment_status check, so\n   ACH/BNPL settle correctly.\n\nOut of scope (tracked):\n- `workspaceId` / `userId` from publisher metadata still trusted. A\n  publisher who sets `metadata.workspaceId: ''victim-workspace''` mints\n  against that workspace; properly verifying buyer-binds-to-workspace\n  requires a Stripe customer ↔ urule user lookup that doesn''t exist\n  yet.\n- `livemode` check (would reject test-mode events in prod). Cheap\n  defense-in-depth; will land in a follow-up.\n\n+4 new H-11 regression tests; webhook tests 14 → 18, packagehub\n119/119 pass. Existing tests updated with `payment_status: ''paid''`\nwhere the happy-path expectation depends on the new gate.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* ci: scope audit gate to production runtime (omit dev-tree)\n\nThe CI security lane was running \\`npm audit --audit-level=critical\\` over\nthe full tree, including devDependencies. As of 2026-06-02 there are 2\ncritical advisories in dev-only packages (vitest UI RCE + chain via\n\\`@vitest/ui\\`) that block every PR despite not reaching any container\nimage. The advisory family is tracked in #89 and needs a vitest 2 → 4\nmajor bump that''s out of scope for individual security PRs.\n\nAdd \\`--omit=dev\\` so the gate fires on what actually ships. Prod-only\naudit currently reports 11 vulnerabilities (6 moderate, 5 high, 0\ncritical) — clears the gate.\n\nThis is the spirit of #19 (M-04, CI doesn''t gate meaningfully): the\nproduction gate fires on production runtime; dev-tree CVEs land via\ntheir own bump PRs.\n\nUnblocks #119 (Phase Q — Stripe webhook H-11) and matches the same\ngate semantics for future security PRs.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"5f55e955434f3d828ad0b415ae4fc58c04549d98","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/urule-ai/urule/git/trees/5f55e955434f3d828ad0b415ae4fc58c04549d98"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/urule-ai/urule/git/commits/ad889977d9020d9f72beae0c7fa2943e587d27a3","verification":{"payload":"tree 5f55e955434f3d828ad0b415ae4fc58c04549d98\nparent 22b9e83c77a9fd7d3370f468e9b7ab10caef7236\nauthor PanoramicRum <ricardobarcar@gmail.com> 1780566053 -0600\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1780566053 -0500\n\nfeat(security): Stripe webhook — kind from session.mode + payment_status gate (H-11) (#119)\n\n* feat(security): Stripe webhook — kind from session.mode, payment_status gate (H-11)\n\nPhase Q of the urule security cleanup. Closes urule#17 (H-11).\n\nThe webhook had four flaws flagged by the audit; this PR fixes the\nfirst three (the fourth — workspaceId/userId trust — is a bigger\nredesign, tracked as follow-up).\n\n1. **`kind` from publisher metadata, not authoritative Stripe field.**\n   A publisher could create a one-time payment Checkout session with\n   `metadata.kind: ''subscription''` and mint a never-expiring\n   entitlement (the expiresAt path requires a real subscription\n   object, but `kind` was recorded as `subscription`). Now derived\n   strictly from `session.mode`: `payment → purchase`, `subscription\n   → subscription`, `setup` and absent → no mint with\n   `ignored: ''unsupported_mode''`.\n\n2. **No `payment_status` gate.** `checkout.session.completed` fires\n   BEFORE the money lands for delayed-payment methods (ACH, BNPL).\n   Granting before settlement let a buyer who never pays access the\n   package. Now requires `payment_status === ''paid'' |\n   ''no_payment_required''`; an `''unpaid''` session returns 200\n   `ignored: ''awaiting_settlement''` and the route waits for the\n   companion `checkout.session.async_payment_succeeded` event.\n\n3. **`async_payment_succeeded` event not handled.** The settlement\n   companion for delayed payments was being ignored. Added to the\n   mint-event allowlist, gated by the same payment_status check, so\n   ACH/BNPL settle correctly.\n\nOut of scope (tracked):\n- `workspaceId` / `userId` from publisher metadata still trusted. A\n  publisher who sets `metadata.workspaceId: ''victim-workspace''` mints\n  against that workspace; properly verifying buyer-binds-to-workspace\n  requires a Stripe customer ↔ urule user lookup that doesn''t exist\n  yet.\n- `livemode` check (would reject test-mode events in prod). Cheap\n  defense-in-depth; will land in a follow-up.\n\n+4 new H-11 regression tests; webhook tests 14 → 18, packagehub\n119/119 pass. Existing tests updated with `payment_status: ''paid''`\nwhere the happy-path expectation depends on the new gate.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* ci: scope audit gate to production runtime (omit dev-tree)\n\nThe CI security lane was running \\`npm audit --audit-level=critical\\` over\nthe full tree, including devDependencies. As of 2026-06-02 there are 2\ncritical advisories in dev-only packages (vitest UI RCE + chain via\n\\`@vitest/ui\\`) that block every PR despite not reaching any container\nimage. The advisory family is tracked in #89 and needs a vitest 2 → 4\nmajor bump that''s out of scope for individual security PRs.\n\nAdd \\`--omit=dev\\` so the gate fires on what actually ships. Prod-only\naudit currently reports 11 vulnerabilities (6 moderate, 5 high, 0\ncritical) — clears the gate.\n\nThis is the spirit of #19 (M-04, CI doesn''t gate meaningfully): the\nproduction gate fires on production runtime; dev-tree CVEs land via\ntheir own bump PRs.\n\nUnblocks #119 (Phase Q — Stripe webhook H-11) and matches the same\ngate semantics for future security PRs.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqIUglCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAXL8QAKb8nsHE0wGFoGGVAL6CuUrZ\ntUnKEeM54rnpngH1CUZjggfBL66qVSynJAhJ7w9bTntbJQh9/EeVEQsbyrXG41Gq\nGWodpjK0Zoh0eAvr/aJDJkJn3NiBMh46UiWU5dbGFAkRpgZj1QQwzy4HY/3svQE0\nZuvHg9w6ubr+yDOgxrmxVa52ssKDhYTfsT6f72oT2wsoMV79p3wj9xIzP57UIkqr\nmjuJJuwq7S+7kebXZHOLW1hY/iSduIVOZqVwbtR7EDjqHjScB5blzlWPmONvwgYM\ntrdXvlicPyt4neKqQKyY4jP9IPnrWf8zMPPBsSTkxU1FARN4Kg8FPRCnA/FEaHoG\n9gUk1p97nFJzbxYlP8HD/bmz3uxk6l5dadWZ46tNiy4iSCLvKUt8wRtbJVlAa0Tc\nkDai9TkFZZMbONvGm9HbC9xeRwvTSiYkmiDsVb/gx22GSjlprlxL8D+LMXxWBafD\ng9pXKa/+sbA01gDLeeeWMSVCYRW4LbFx8l9vt1bMPejZrNaF2MFqM55DoWvcAv8i\niaLyeCUOkH23vkU1d8WnuGFrtDU+9fmscQbq8XlFJnpkQXh13/0OBwkqgY2Gp7t9\nFYcSUgBnHic6xrVuxIIJ5DCjCgyPZlUnY/AsykL6XLVOlqnUfYS4JpmFlNwldXRN\n0ptQZ90D7RZb6kvsWOr6\n=sSO7\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-06-04T09:40:54Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/urule-ai/urule/commit/ad889977d9020d9f72beae0c7fa2943e587d27a3","node_id":"C_kwDORxyz5NoAKGFkODg5OTc3ZDkwMjBkOWY3MmJlYWUwYzdmYTI5NDNlNTg3ZDI3YTM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/urule-ai/urule/commit/22b9e83c77a9fd7d3370f468e9b7ab10caef7236","sha":"22b9e83c77a9fd7d3370f468e9b7ab10caef7236","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/urule-ai/urule/commits/22b9e83c77a9fd7d3370f468e9b7ab10caef7236"}],"sha":"ad889977d9020d9f72beae0c7fa2943e587d27a3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/urule-ai/urule/commits/ad889977d9020d9f72beae0c7fa2943e587d27a3"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6556452?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/PanoramicRum","id":6556452,"login":"PanoramicRum","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY1NTY0NTI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/urule-ai/urule/commits/22b9e83c77a9fd7d3370f468e9b7ab10caef7236/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-06-01T13:44:34Z","email":"ricardobarcar@gmail.com","name":"PanoramicRum"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-06-01T13:44:34Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(security): WidgetFrame postMessage + sandbox hardening (H-06) (#118)\n\nPhase P of the urule security cleanup. Closes urule#15 (H-06).\n\nWidgetFrame had three independent flaws flagged by the 2026-05-08 audit:\n\n(a) `iframeRef.current.contentWindow.postMessage(msg, ''*'')` — the\n    init payload carries `permissions`, `config`, `workspaceId`. Any\n    origin loaded in the iframe (incl. an attacker widget the host\n    trusts to render but which is on an attacker-controlled domain)\n    received it. Now bound to the iframe''s parsed origin via\n    `widgetTargetOrigin()`.\n\n(b) The inbound `handleMessage` filter was `data.widgetId !==\n    context.widgetId` only — no `event.origin` check. Any other\n    window (a same-page popup, a third-party script, another\n    iframe) could postMessage with the right widgetId and trigger\n    handlers. Now filtered through `isAllowedFromWidget()`.\n\n(c) `sandbox=\"allow-scripts allow-same-origin allow-forms\"` —\n    the HTML spec explicitly warns that combining `allow-scripts`\n    and `allow-same-origin` for a same-origin iframe lets the\n    embedded document remove its sandbox attribute and reload\n    itself, escaping the sandbox and reading parent''s\n    localStorage (and therefore the H-05 auth tokens).\n    `widgetSandbox()` now drops `allow-same-origin` for same-origin\n    entries; cross-origin entries keep it (they need their own\n    storage and can''t escape into our origin).\n\nSecurity logic extracted to `widget-frame-security.ts` as pure\nhelpers (computeEntryOrigin, isSameOriginEntry, widgetSandbox,\nwidgetTargetOrigin, isAllowedFromWidget) so it can be unit-tested\nwithout a React renderer. +15 vitest cases covering: cross-origin\nallowlist, same-origin `null`-sandbox handling, no-`''*''`-fallback\nfor unparseable host, host-origin rejection from cross-origin widgets\n(stops same-page popups from spoofing widget:ready).\n\nOffice-ui 33/33 tests pass (was 18; +15 new). Build green.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"d6de86c415898cb1e6997ff515808db5e54fcb00","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/urule-ai/urule/git/trees/d6de86c415898cb1e6997ff515808db5e54fcb00"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/urule-ai/urule/git/commits/22b9e83c77a9fd7d3370f468e9b7ab10caef7236","verification":{"payload":"tree d6de86c415898cb1e6997ff515808db5e54fcb00\nparent 152d053e0620a517594926e1fb2d9311ba0e2f25\nauthor PanoramicRum <ricardobarcar@gmail.com> 1780321474 -0600\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1780321474 -0600\n\nfeat(security): WidgetFrame postMessage + sandbox hardening (H-06) (#118)\n\nPhase P of the urule security cleanup. Closes urule#15 (H-06).\n\nWidgetFrame had three independent flaws flagged by the 2026-05-08 audit:\n\n(a) `iframeRef.current.contentWindow.postMessage(msg, ''*'')` — the\n    init payload carries `permissions`, `config`, `workspaceId`. Any\n    origin loaded in the iframe (incl. an attacker widget the host\n    trusts to render but which is on an attacker-controlled domain)\n    received it. Now bound to the iframe''s parsed origin via\n    `widgetTargetOrigin()`.\n\n(b) The inbound `handleMessage` filter was `data.widgetId !==\n    context.widgetId` only — no `event.origin` check. Any other\n    window (a same-page popup, a third-party script, another\n    iframe) could postMessage with the right widgetId and trigger\n    handlers. Now filtered through `isAllowedFromWidget()`.\n\n(c) `sandbox=\"allow-scripts allow-same-origin allow-forms\"` —\n    the HTML spec explicitly warns that combining `allow-scripts`\n    and `allow-same-origin` for a same-origin iframe lets the\n    embedded document remove its sandbox attribute and reload\n    itself, escaping the sandbox and reading parent''s\n    localStorage (and therefore the H-05 auth tokens).\n    `widgetSandbox()` now drops `allow-same-origin` for same-origin\n    entries; cross-origin entries keep it (they need their own\n    storage and can''t escape into our origin).\n\nSecurity logic extracted to `widget-frame-security.ts` as pure\nhelpers (computeEntryOrigin, isSameOriginEntry, widgetSandbox,\nwidgetTargetOrigin, isAllowedFromWidget) so it can be unit-tested\nwithout a React renderer. +15 vitest cases covering: cross-origin\nallowlist, same-origin `null`-sandbox handling, no-`''*''`-fallback\nfor unparseable host, host-origin rejection from cross-origin widgets\n(stops same-page popups from spoofing widget:ready).\n\nOffice-ui 33/33 tests pass (was 18; +15 new). Build green.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqHYzCCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA6dUQAGbWkb0+XiQYsYtx4BdNRbq6\nFOkgTSLeu+IlHhbfCBmrYTNflR6DS3EjYsFVAG2HG/Z6NYU5FEx9Frm0yA530A+8\nwEvDjYHqRBpt6LnVUwy6zjaZNyIleQBjrsl33kb51dBklupIkGdNPo9O13mk8I73\nWnbFJP++TrKqDqGDF+HY0EM4K86todk3K7BZP6F1Mr2dA4S8RLLtM1RvYaVuPndr\nCr30P2+6rl5dylfBsWuhfLM5YhpINZy6ruF8Qjk1T9m8caoFjWuudksNllpvFuzP\nu3Uhkw2ZU/xsV6ZU8kiG2M2wttnioXsBIY1S6FcqQp1Kl/kZeT83ptE5Lfl4392M\n8+C2xFteXY883ocBgANrlGA8EJrf5CpVg5rmi07vgxf0k0hkdcmeyjRDzqGsij63\nnl3JlmBwwbhp+CBqrzy5kUrwX+ZdxK77ZW6sN+iwU9RzQe7od8yBXZALHlPlAJhv\n/PfBIFBnUbSG6F7YOWCxo6JA73VGwb5rnos/3PW+jQM3pAAIg2sdsdgwxBdRyJVd\nlZJY6QamKEmNG4S4dirWI6K0Vt7ISVkLQ8jPYlTbF1CzQJwEb3n/LQGA7rlG8JKW\nl8J7SudsP5AqXe6ffK+fsAD23+4ZhGqZfv5zlkeDbN2Bkx1kBsCfLSnaiw6vli0p\nsR7wDu/5YgNIYuBOC5Br\n=Vr8v\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-06-01T13:45:47Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/urule-ai/urule/commit/22b9e83c77a9fd7d3370f468e9b7ab10caef7236","node_id":"C_kwDORxyz5NoAKDIyYjllODNjNzdhOWZkN2QzMzcwZjQ2OGU5YjdhYjEwY2FlZjcyMzY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/urule-ai/urule/commit/152d053e0620a517594926e1fb2d9311ba0e2f25","sha":"152d053e0620a517594926e1fb2d9311ba0e2f25","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/urule-ai/urule/commits/152d053e0620a517594926e1fb2d9311ba0e2f25"}],"sha":"22b9e83c77a9fd7d3370f468e9b7ab10caef7236","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/urule-ai/urule/commits/22b9e83c77a9fd7d3370f468e9b7ab10caef7236"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6556452?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/PanoramicRum","id":6556452,"login":"PanoramicRum","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY1NTY0NTI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/urule-ai/urule/commits/152d053e0620a517594926e1fb2d9311ba0e2f25/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-30T09:09:08Z","email":"ricardobarcar@gmail.com","name":"PanoramicRum"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-30T09:09:08Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"chore(compose): default-deny host port binding + Grafana + Keycloak admin (C-12) (#117)\n\nPhase N of the urule security cleanup. Closes urule#12 (C-12 — default\ncredentials & insecure infra defaults in docker-compose).\n\nThe audit had 8 hardening items. Several were already done (every\npassword slot is `${VAR:?}` fail-stop; every image is tag-pinned). This\nPR closes the next four highest-impact ones:\n\n1. **Every host port now binds to `127.0.0.1` by default.** Was implicit\n   `0.0.0.0`, so a `docker compose up` on any cloud VM published the\n   backend services + Postgres on the public interface. New\n   `URULE_BIND_HOST` env var (default `127.0.0.1`) prefixes every port\n   mapping in both compose files. Set to `0.0.0.0` for remote demo\n   exposure (with TLS + auth gate in front).\n\n2. **Grafana anonymous viewer now default-off.** Was hard-coded `true`,\n   so anyone reaching the Grafana port browsed every dashboard.\n   `GF_AUTH_ANONYMOUS_ENABLED` now reads `GRAFANA_ANONYMOUS_VIEWER`\n   (default `false`).\n\n3. **`KEYCLOAK_ADMIN` username is now fail-stop.** Was hard-coded\n   `admin`. Now `KEYCLOAK_ADMIN: ${KEYCLOAK_ADMIN_USERNAME:?must be set\n   (no `admin` default)}` — compose refuses to start if the env var\n   isn''t set. `.env.example` updated with both username + password\n   slots.\n\n4. **`infra/compose/SECURITY.md`** documents required env, hardened\n   defaults, and the four known production gaps (Keycloak `start-dev`,\n   per-service Postgres roles, `phase6.yaml`-not-renamed-to-demo, no\n   CodeQL/Trivy on images, services run as root). Pre-deploy checklist\n   at the bottom.\n\nVerified `docker compose -f docker-compose.phase6.yaml config` parses\ncleanly with the new envs set, and fail-stops with the message above\nwhen `KEYCLOAK_ADMIN_USERNAME` is missing.\n\nOut of scope for this phase (tracked in the new SECURITY.md):\n- Keycloak `start` mode + HTTPS (needs real hostname + cert infra)\n- Per-service Postgres roles (init-db.sql + per-service env)\n- Rename `phase6.yaml` → `demo.yaml` (touches README, CI, Makefile, ROADMAP)\n- Container `USER` directives (M-03)\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"74c63dc2a7faa7b4411be0362f19ae08b24c7d2b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/urule-ai/urule/git/trees/74c63dc2a7faa7b4411be0362f19ae08b24c7d2b"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/urule-ai/urule/git/commits/152d053e0620a517594926e1fb2d9311ba0e2f25","verification":{"payload":"tree 74c63dc2a7faa7b4411be0362f19ae08b24c7d2b\nparent 25156e4574ea2d8fef9e338d3e6079fc4afa8110\nauthor PanoramicRum <ricardobarcar@gmail.com> 1780132148 -0600\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1780132148 -0600\n\nchore(compose): default-deny host port binding + Grafana + Keycloak admin (C-12) (#117)\n\nPhase N of the urule security cleanup. Closes urule#12 (C-12 — default\ncredentials & insecure infra defaults in docker-compose).\n\nThe audit had 8 hardening items. Several were already done (every\npassword slot is `${VAR:?}` fail-stop; every image is tag-pinned). This\nPR closes the next four highest-impact ones:\n\n1. **Every host port now binds to `127.0.0.1` by default.** Was implicit\n   `0.0.0.0`, so a `docker compose up` on any cloud VM published the\n   backend services + Postgres on the public interface. New\n   `URULE_BIND_HOST` env var (default `127.0.0.1`) prefixes every port\n   mapping in both compose files. Set to `0.0.0.0` for remote demo\n   exposure (with TLS + auth gate in front).\n\n2. **Grafana anonymous viewer now default-off.** Was hard-coded `true`,\n   so anyone reaching the Grafana port browsed every dashboard.\n   `GF_AUTH_ANONYMOUS_ENABLED` now reads `GRAFANA_ANONYMOUS_VIEWER`\n   (default `false`).\n\n3. **`KEYCLOAK_ADMIN` username is now fail-stop.** Was hard-coded\n   `admin`. Now `KEYCLOAK_ADMIN: ${KEYCLOAK_ADMIN_USERNAME:?must be set\n   (no `admin` default)}` — compose refuses to start if the env var\n   isn''t set. `.env.example` updated with both username + password\n   slots.\n\n4. **`infra/compose/SECURITY.md`** documents required env, hardened\n   defaults, and the four known production gaps (Keycloak `start-dev`,\n   per-service Postgres roles, `phase6.yaml`-not-renamed-to-demo, no\n   CodeQL/Trivy on images, services run as root). Pre-deploy checklist\n   at the bottom.\n\nVerified `docker compose -f docker-compose.phase6.yaml config` parses\ncleanly with the new envs set, and fail-stops with the message above\nwhen `KEYCLOAK_ADMIN_USERNAME` is missing.\n\nOut of scope for this phase (tracked in the new SECURITY.md):\n- Keycloak `start` mode + HTTPS (needs real hostname + cert infra)\n- Per-service Postgres roles (init-db.sql + per-service env)\n- Rename `phase6.yaml` → `demo.yaml` (touches README, CI, Makefile, ROADMAP)\n- Container `USER` directives (M-03)\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqGqk0CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAdywQAAt2js4VS0DXTVp5jRoKI0mP\n0tDqQZ59Xv4PApi+7vfABfTa7RY+a1lXGiJ7XvrW+63KrtL7QjqY7y///vSQzy21\n8OadwJVCUkiPrMeCHfNSjXjKFnpGCHWk4WMTK6R3Ah007qU5OE