56e4574ea2d8fef9e338d3e6079fc4afa8110"}],"sha":"152d053e0620a517594926e1fb2d9311ba0e2f25","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/urule-ai/urule/commits/152d053e0620a517594926e1fb2d9311ba0e2f25"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6556452?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/PanoramicRum","id":6556452,"login":"PanoramicRum","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY1NTY0NTI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/urule-ai/urule/commits/25156e4574ea2d8fef9e338d3e6079fc4afa8110/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-30T08:39:32Z","email":"ricardobarcar@gmail.com","name":"PanoramicRum"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-30T08:39:32Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(security): harden package-install source dispatch (C-10 fix) (#116)\n\nPhase M of the urule security cleanup. Closes urule#10 (C-10 — SSRF +\narbitrary file read via the package installer).\n\nThree vulnerabilities the original code carried, all reachable by any\nauthenticated workspace member via POST /api/v1/packages/install:\n\n(a) `startsWith(''https://github.com'')` was bypassable —\n    `https://github.com.attacker.com/repo.git` matched the prefix and\n    simple-git was told to clone the attacker host. Replaced by\n    `isGitHubUrl()`, which `new URL`-parses the source and requires\n    `hostname === ''github.com''` exactly + a sane `/owner/repo` path\n    (rejects subdomains, embedded credentials, mistyped TLDs).\n\n(b) `loader.loadFromPath(source)` accepted any local path\n    (`/etc/passwd/...` style). Now default-deny: a deployer must\n    explicitly set `URULE_PACKAGES_LOCAL_INSTALL_ROOT`, and the\n    supplied source must resolve inside that root with no `..`\n    traversal escape. `resolve()` collapses `..` before the prefix\n    check, blocking the obvious bypasses.\n\n(c) `simple-git clone` had no timeout and no ref validation. Adds a\n    5-minute clone timeout via simple-git''s `timeout` option, and a\n    `isSafeGitRef()` regex (`/^[A-Za-z0-9._/-]+$/`, no leading `-`,\n    max 200 chars) that blocks argument-injection (`-upload-pack=evil`)\n    and shell-metacharacter payloads (`main; rm -rf /`,\n    `main$(whoami)`, etc.) before they ever reach git.\n\nAlso fixes a Zod / TS drift on the install schema — `source` was\ndeclared `z.object({}).loose()` (accepts any object) but the\n`PackageInstallRequest` interface declared `string`. Now\n`z.string().min(1).max(2048).optional()`.\n\n+37 new C-10 regression tests in `manifest-loader-c10.test.ts`\n(URL allowlist boundaries, ref injection vectors, local-path\ntraversal). Existing `package-manager.test.ts` updated: the\n\"loads local-path source\" test now verifies default-deny without\nthe env var and the happy path with it; the GitHub URL test is\nunchanged. Packages 110/110.\n\nCloses #10.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"ff995cc978534bd6093cceea33e305d5d0beaa99","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/urule-ai/urule/git/trees/ff995cc978534bd6093cceea33e305d5d0beaa99"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/urule-ai/urule/git/commits/25156e4574ea2d8fef9e338d3e6079fc4afa8110","verification":{"payload":"tree ff995cc978534bd6093cceea33e305d5d0beaa99\nparent 41d6b043f0b2ba05179a92848c3781d270ce77aa\nauthor PanoramicRum <ricardobarcar@gmail.com> 1780130372 -0600\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1780130372 -0600\n\nfeat(security): harden package-install source dispatch (C-10 fix) (#116)\n\nPhase M of the urule security cleanup. Closes urule#10 (C-10 — SSRF +\narbitrary file read via the package installer).\n\nThree vulnerabilities the original code carried, all reachable by any\nauthenticated workspace member via POST /api/v1/packages/install:\n\n(a) `startsWith(''https://github.com'')` was bypassable —\n    `https://github.com.attacker.com/repo.git` matched the prefix and\n    simple-git was told to clone the attacker host. Replaced by\n    `isGitHubUrl()`, which `new URL`-parses the source and requires\n    `hostname === ''github.com''` exactly + a sane `/owner/repo` path\n    (rejects subdomains, embedded credentials, mistyped TLDs).\n\n(b) `loader.loadFromPath(source)` accepted any local path\n    (`/etc/passwd/...` style). Now default-deny: a deployer must\n    explicitly set `URULE_PACKAGES_LOCAL_INSTALL_ROOT`, and the\n    supplied source must resolve inside that root with no `..`\n    traversal escape. `resolve()` collapses `..` before the prefix\n    check, blocking the obvious bypasses.\n\n(c) `simple-git clone` had no timeout and no ref validation. Adds a\n    5-minute clone timeout via simple-git''s `timeout` option, and a\n    `isSafeGitRef()` regex (`/^[A-Za-z0-9._/-]+$/`, no leading `-`,\n    max 200 chars) that blocks argument-injection (`-upload-pack=evil`)\n    and shell-metacharacter payloads (`main; rm -rf /`,\n    `main$(whoami)`, etc.) before they ever reach git.\n\nAlso fixes a Zod / TS drift on the install schema — `source` was\ndeclared `z.object({}).loose()` (accepts any object) but the\n`PackageInstallRequest` interface declared `string`. Now\n`z.string().min(1).max(2048).optional()`.\n\n+37 new C-10 regression tests in `manifest-loader-c10.test.ts`\n(URL allowlist boundaries, ref injection vectors, local-path\ntraversal). Existing `package-manager.test.ts` updated: the\n\"loads local-path source\" test now verifies default-deny without\nthe env var and the happy path with it; the GitHub URL test is\nunchanged. Packages 110/110.\n\nCloses #10.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqGqJECRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAkx4QAJvyfpeIvKXgYM7las+Ty7WB\nMyzPtcOUOMVbnyvEtHqwLcosBw56UZ47B3+kSP2dt+olg3xTS+Q1qHAoabp14zc/\n6pKw76+5N1S9YbssIp1qYZ+WKyfDtYMERLCG4ZNAIbM0rBlvzYtptf9cbUipC5TK\nOpND8fDyZt3qLHGCJrhnJVG6xyxPz/zRg+M4iEpmCCOkOSs4treTLVFPpn+DZqZ9\nzib81Ho8lijLswYAFhtTfJeEtUQR3/8AMvvwvJnX+wsWB9H5OE+xwAaw+agdMSEV\ng2qDkhFnfuEI8uqt1kLPQhZhcE4lRFFU2MIDhVgUm7hDtxzovsCLOixtgFMZuMYX\nIyAr9JYHum1osFiuGa6cQGB53DQKyGEevOjeRTrISs8bWz/hPtoXardFluQJggEl\nWvUcLPvSYDWfv+pVuntCszSWG6ztXdD7JCR/ZkHCvkqy2BsqkQSC18lot64KmOOw\n4YCITSGTWHN9vmfb+Ax4aHz/bVEmDrL+BTpyp+h0bjWQLxm4qqUU64leOxjMf29c\npHWGxptYvp9YSnXrw5VdnYQGZEB8rEo/6M+3stdy7eDYm/Txz77az3JKAWbL5Ptr\nyVLcEqnLkBibeu+pQY3M4mw/hUu+2KhymjZK9onrc4wMt2peuO7EwvAsjv74H7Am\ncoMF3dNb2Ve55ElW/G8E\n=EVgA\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-05-30T08:39:32Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/urule-ai/urule/commit/25156e4574ea2d8fef9e338d3e6079fc4afa8110","node_id":"C_kwDORxyz5NoAKDI1MTU2ZTQ1NzRlYTJkOGZlZjllMzM4ZDNlNjA3OWZjNGFmYTgxMTA","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/urule-ai/urule/commit/41d6b043f0b2ba05179a92848c3781d270ce77aa","sha":"41d6b043f0b2ba05179a92848c3781d270ce77aa","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/urule-ai/urule/commits/41d6b043f0b2ba05179a92848c3781d270ce77aa"}],"sha":"25156e4574ea2d8fef9e338d3e6079fc4afa8110","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/urule-ai/urule/commits/25156e4574ea2d8fef9e338d3e6079fc4afa8110"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6556452?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/PanoramicRum","id":6556452,"login":"PanoramicRum","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY1NTY0NTI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/urule-ai/urule/commits/41d6b043f0b2ba05179a92848c3781d270ce77aa/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-29T20:03:43Z","email":"ricardobarcar@gmail.com","name":"PanoramicRum"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-29T20:03:43Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(security): admin-only gate on entitlement mint + revoke (#4 phase L — C-11) (#115)\n\nPhase L of the urule security cleanup. Closes urule#11 (C-11 —\nentitlement bypass).\n\nPreviously POST /api/v1/entitlements and DELETE /api/v1/entitlements/:id\nwere JWT-auth only — any authenticated user could:\n- mint paid entitlements for themselves (revenue loss); the Stripe\n  flow was bypassable entirely\n- revoke any paying customer''s entitlement (DoS for paying users)\n\nNow both routes carry `preHandler: requireRole(''admin'')` from\n@urule/authz-middleware. The Stripe webhook receiver writes directly\nto the DB after HMAC verification — it doesn''t call the HTTP route —\nso admin-only on the HTTP path doesn''t break the purchase flow.\n\nGET /api/v1/entitlements (the install gate consulted by the packages\nservice before installing) stays open — it''s a read-only check that\nneeds to be callable from the install pipeline.\n\nC-09 (#9 — packagehub anyone-can-publish) verified already-closed by\nPhase E (#107):\n- Method-qualified `''GET /api/v1/packages''` in publicRoutes gates\n  POST/PATCH/DELETE under the same prefix.\n- POST /packages captures publisherId from the JWT; POST\n  /packages/:name/versions enforces caller === publisher.\n- Pubkey rotation routes gated by cryptographic proof-of-possession.\n- Residual: legacy packages with both publisherId=null and\n  publisherPubkey=null allow any authenticated caller to publish\n  (intentional back-compat for pre-E seed data). Tracking as a\n  separate seed-script audit.\n\n+8 new enforcement tests (authz-entitlements.test.ts): non-admin 403,\nadmin 201/204, GET stays open. Packagehub 115/115.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"6e0a004102411b4c40d9dd1e051bd5c414033538","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/urule-ai/urule/git/trees/6e0a004102411b4c40d9dd1e051bd5c414033538"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/urule-ai/urule/git/commits/41d6b043f0b2ba05179a92848c3781d270ce77aa","verification":{"payload":"tree 6e0a004102411b4c40d9dd1e051bd5c414033538\nparent 7eefcd4f9ba03e7c76eda0e918267cb932f347a9\nauthor PanoramicRum <ricardobarcar@gmail.com> 1780085023 -0600\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1780085023 -0600\n\nfeat(security): admin-only gate on entitlement mint + revoke (#4 phase L — C-11) (#115)\n\nPhase L of the urule security cleanup. Closes urule#11 (C-11 —\nentitlement bypass).\n\nPreviously POST /api/v1/entitlements and DELETE /api/v1/entitlements/:id\nwere JWT-auth only — any authenticated user could:\n- mint paid entitlements for themselves (revenue loss); the Stripe\n  flow was bypassable entirely\n- revoke any paying customer''s entitlement (DoS for paying users)\n\nNow both routes carry `preHandler: requireRole(''admin'')` from\n@urule/authz-middleware. The Stripe webhook receiver writes directly\nto the DB after HMAC verification — it doesn''t call the HTTP route —\nso admin-only on the HTTP path doesn''t break the purchase flow.\n\nGET /api/v1/entitlements (the install gate consulted by the packages\nservice before installing) stays open — it''s a read-only check that\nneeds to be callable from the install pipeline.\n\nC-09 (#9 — packagehub anyone-can-publish) verified already-closed by\nPhase E (#107):\n- Method-qualified `''GET /api/v1/packages''` in publicRoutes gates\n  POST/PATCH/DELETE under the same prefix.\n- POST /packages captures publisherId from the JWT; POST\n  /packages/:name/versions enforces caller === publisher.\n- Pubkey rotation routes gated by cryptographic proof-of-possession.\n- Residual: legacy packages with both publisherId=null and\n  publisherPubkey=null allow any authenticated caller to publish\n  (intentional back-compat for pre-E seed data). Tracking as a\n  separate seed-script audit.\n\n+8 new enforcement tests (authz-entitlements.test.ts): non-admin 403,\nadmin 201/204, GET stays open. Packagehub 115/115.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqGfEfCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAQGQQABt26Of2plwn8E1c7GlIGay8\nK/M9hpIL8MlDcYlVOyV6X8g+e2YWgHnqJr0Pren1M6cBkMlX7Koo+8330nDaYS60\n0N0i0r41oJuhy7QTvl+vWm5zmmTdbcEfRH7ppjMF5NWKqofZMa05kXWPp9aYqekz\nGg32UHVpY2ZyjbI1Ot/5eH5zSSRLIxw0gj5Ci1Z/kVaF0JU0O30ZCPSd0l5IfRfc\nYSBKafm/8yx+0LYH05I2wRTcKf5ACDsaQkPggAKXOqGgXG9COWGqZ8hEmXgKeozu\nyRanY2F4Z9dsudEqY9X3KJQF+TOSKhMRWpzawoXIAsFgDMAkF9o28YNI7If84fl6\nApJFw3TLT2yBi6df4zMymyJrIsdLh0Hj9l1qIIDxzWUH2x9cbSJqfkVzF7KWq+Gp\ngIfB2AcOWStxOV8G+3siGaRA839R36YTQnVtKNsQr8vf/mdEoeIRJwPpQnae5a8N\nu5zkJLSwgvqN/dvIHZ7EF9lrb0kz3B+fre79SI4tWGBnVtlDMvcPZjMJQYhJ2OAC\niKSqPhTIUAn7buq9dq/g6zldALlf46aO0dzM0PpoJV6UTg6H/0ipE5b/1qDNlS7/\n4vP9wrqQ3oKwsm94cI654qDJ3N9sIC3RR01sfdRohFjYf1M/H4jtOz/chbxi5xvo\nUtkMrGJgE3ra1x2e7DSM\n=r7sE\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-05-29T20:03:43Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/urule-ai/urule/commit/41d6b043f0b2ba05179a92848c3781d270ce77aa","node_id":"C_kwDORxyz5NoAKDQxZDZiMDQzZjBiMmJhMDUxNzlhOTI4NDhjMzc4MWQyNzBjZTc3YWE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/urule-ai/urule/commit/7eefcd4f9ba03e7c76eda0e918267cb932f347a9","sha":"7eefcd4f9ba03e7c76eda0e918267cb932f347a9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/urule-ai/urule/commits/7eefcd4f9ba03e7c76eda0e918267cb932f347a9"}],"sha":"41d6b043f0b2ba05179a92848c3781d270ce77aa","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/urule-ai/urule/commits/41d6b043f0b2ba05179a92848c3781d270ce77aa"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6556452?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/PanoramicRum","id":6556452,"login":"PanoramicRum","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY1NTY0NTI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/urule-ai/urule/commits/7eefcd4f9ba03e7c76eda0e918267cb932f347a9/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-29T18:43:19Z","email":"ricardobarcar@gmail.com","name":"PanoramicRum"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-29T18:43:19Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(security): close C-08 message spoofing + admin-gate cross-workspace lists (#95) (#114)\n\nPhase K of the urule issue #4 family. Closes the last critical\naudit-family hole in registry and clears the related security\nenhancement #95.\n\nC-08 (#8) — POST /api/v1/conversations/:conversationId/messages\n  - `senderId` is now derived from request.uruleUser.id, not the\n    request body (where any authenticated workspace member could\n    forge a sender). Drops the field from the Zod schema and\n    switches to `z.strictObject` so a body containing `senderId`\n    returns 400 instead of being silently stripped — spoofing\n    attempts surface in CI / logs.\n  - `senderType` constrained to `''user'' | ''agent'' | ''system''`\n    (was free-form string).\n  - The `requireConversationMembership` preHandler (already in\n    place from Phase B) continues to bound spam to workspaces\n    the caller belongs to; deeper cost-control for the\n    fire-and-forget LLM trigger is out of scope.\n\n#95 — cross-workspace list admin-gating\n  - GET /workspaces, /orgs, /conversations: preHandler:\n    requireRole(''admin''). Workspace-scoped callers should use the\n    `:orgId/workspaces` or `:wsId/conversations` siblings.\n  - GET /providers: hybrid — `?workspaceId=` accessible to members\n    (membership-checked via `request.authz.check`), no-filter path\n    requires admin. Custom `requireAdminOrWorkspaceFilter`\n    preHandler in providers.routes.ts. Closer to least-privilege\n    than blanket admin-only since office-ui needs the filtered case.\n\nPre-existing C-06 (#6 — provider PATCH baseUrl redirect) and C-07\n(#7 — agent memories/PATCH prompt-injection) verified already-fixed\nby Phase B''s `requireProviderMembership` / `requireAgentMembership`\npreHandlers. Those issues are closeable as-is.\n\n+15 new Phase K enforcement tests; 101/101 registry tests pass.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"ee3747e8a5c249fbdf6a4629eff3217f08f5528e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/urule-ai/urule/git/trees/ee3747e8a5c249fbdf6a4629eff3217f08f5528e"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/urule-ai/urule/git/commits/7eefcd4f9ba03e7c76eda0e918267cb932f347a9","verification":{"payload":"tree ee3747e8a5c249fbdf6a4629eff3217f08f5528e\nparent d5ec3a666608aa2e44d605d16ad077b32be7aaa9\nauthor PanoramicRum <ricardobarcar@gmail.com> 1780080199 -0600\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1780080199 -0600\n\nfeat(security): close C-08 message spoofing + admin-gate cross-workspace lists (#95) (#114)\n\nPhase K of the urule issue #4 family. Closes the last critical\naudit-family hole in registry and clears the related security\nenhancement #95.\n\nC-08 (#8) — POST /api/v1/conversations/:conversationId/messages\n  - `senderId` is now derived from request.uruleUser.id, not the\n    request body (where any authenticated workspace member could\n    forge a sender). Drops the field from the Zod schema and\n    switches to `z.strictObject` so a body containing `senderId`\n    returns 400 instead of being silently stripped — spoofing\n    attempts surface in CI / logs.\n  - `senderType` constrained to `''user'' | ''agent'' | ''system''`\n    (was free-form string).\n  - The `requireConversationMembership` preHandler (already in\n    place from Phase B) continues to bound spam to workspaces\n    the caller belongs to; deeper cost-control for the\n    fire-and-forget LLM trigger is out of scope.\n\n#95 — cross-workspace list admin-gating\n  - GET /workspaces, /orgs, /conversations: preHandler:\n    requireRole(''admin''). Workspace-scoped callers should use the\n    `:orgId/workspaces` or `:wsId/conversations` siblings.\n  - GET /providers: hybrid — `?workspaceId=` accessible to members\n    (membership-checked via `request.authz.check`), no-filter path\n    requires admin. Custom `requireAdminOrWorkspaceFilter`\n    preHandler in providers.routes.ts. Closer to least-privilege\n    than blanket admin-only since office-ui needs the filtered case.\n\nPre-existing C-06 (#6 — provider PATCH baseUrl redirect) and C-07\n(#7 — agent memories/PATCH prompt-injection) verified already-fixed\nby Phase B''s `requireProviderMembership` / `requireAgentMembership`\npreHandlers. Those issues are closeable as-is.\n\n+15 new Phase K enforcement tests; 101/101 registry tests pass.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqGd5HCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAiGIQABF5REoxuz7+xEi8/wVaGDuz\n9cyq1f84EckifeVQF7xJYOPeP6kGrhxFZ/LC42e6+QKpPnOjHI845YuRVj9XtjPB\nKpme9Q5loHjAtz4rFtIIxbITO15xTj+hcQBZKUdGR/s9ytYVUvhHFdKfrXKJn16A\nYcX+u0vsnyKHisTknkdy6cIgeMsoUFrBzDErdAOx1lfjLaPa1OTSG4fTyMSaDJf+\np+S0NXxPTsXpNc8516y/JNZROahbuh5CGc6dz5zBPnDX/LPMkWa0A8sZ7DIKXi+E\nLIsv3/qaEk6ybArzl/8pBWC0Ics0LRBKv6DmvdaJgrJJZVLYw8lQ05nFygWnAk4l\nZs9stR/UqVvh8dgmd8lvbLVTSxlj+pT9rOwiU+5oPhHdtUiEvWHoc+9oHe2Ph0TF\nXqAkcYdsm/GJ0eW22gg6gyly8SUalR/t8p0X8C8JnO94i+oaPnJWuVSDOPFWrSfT\nqwOuo8vaALk+c6Ili6xggTcFxLEsDo+WMQDutC5T5CYNChH7WLS0xVqFF/kOp4tc\nV+3cMkR2x0g9g+bdJt0f/Eei2P3cVOLGFXVRtc8zEf2Ds8QtPjilx2GVrPMdkdDH\ngO9roff+JfRsyoF3nOr4O8gICXbttYeKa0ikB+6+Z/e6fu60p8NZKhFYDseRhSVu\nDUs2Jmc2vo2NMMRo6UDc\n=Odi7\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-05-29T18:43:20Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/urule-ai/urule/commit/7eefcd4f9ba03e7c76eda0e918267cb932f347a9","node_id":"C_kwDORxyz5NoAKDdlZWZjZDRmOWJhMDNlN2M3NmVkYTBlOTE4MjY3Y2I5MzJmMzQ3YTk","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/urule-ai/urule/commit/d5ec3a666608aa2e44d605d16ad077b32be7aaa9","sha":"d5ec3a666608aa2e44d605d16ad077b32be7aaa9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/urule-ai/urule/commits/d5ec3a666608aa2e44d605d16ad077b32be7aaa9"}],"sha":"7eefcd4f9ba03e7c76eda0e918267cb932f347a9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/urule-ai/urule/commits/7eefcd4f9ba03e7c76eda0e918267cb932f347a9"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6556452?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/PanoramicRum","id":6556452,"login":"PanoramicRum","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY1NTY0NTI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/urule-ai/urule/commits/d5ec3a666608aa2e44d605d16ad077b32be7aaa9/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-29T10:49:39Z","email":"ricardobarcar@gmail.com","name":"PanoramicRum"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-29T10:49:39Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(security): governance admin-only authz (#4 phase J — final) (#113)\n\n* feat(security): admin-only authz on governance (#4 phase J — final)\n\nPhase J of urule issue #4 (system-wide missing authorization), and the\nlast service in the rollout. Adds `requireRole(''admin'')` to every\ngovernance route — `/decide`, `/policy/evaluate`, `/authz/check`,\n`/authz/batch-check`. The previous posture was \"any authenticated user,\"\nwhich let any JWT-holder probe policy decisions and OpenFGA tuples\nacross the platform — information disclosure across every workspace.\n\nGovernance is off-pattern: routes are service-to-service decision\nendpoints, not user-driven, so `requireMembership(workspaceId)` doesn''t\napply. Mirrors packagehub''s special-case principle (use a non-membership\nauthz model that fits the service). Services that need to call governance\nwill use admin service-account JWTs; the SKIP_AUTH mock user already has\n`admin`, so the existing route + correlation-id + CORS tests stay green\nwithout changes.\n\n- adds `tests/authz-enforcement.test.ts` — 17 tests: 4 routes × 4 user\n  shapes (admin / non-admin / no-roles / null) + an audit-still-fires\n  regression\n- adds `@urule/authz-middleware` workspace dep\n\nOut of scope: composing governance into docker-compose.phase6.yaml\n(currently only in the test-compose file — the natural trigger is when\nthe first internal caller wires up, per registry''s TODO marker).\n\nCloses the issue #4 rollout. Phases A-J shipped.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* review fixes(governance): real audit-fires assertion + clearer null-user comment\n\nAddress findings from the Phase J PR review:\n\n- The audit-fires regression test was a placebo — only asserted 200 and\n  body shape, never verified the audit event actually emitted. Tightened\n  to spy on `app.log.info` and check at least one call carries the\n  expected `{ audit: true, topic: ''urule.audit.config.changed'', data: {\n  entityType: ''governance-decision'' } }` shape, after draining the\n  fire-and-forget microtask via `setImmediate`. Would now fail if the\n  preHandler accidentally short-circuited the handler OR if the audit\n  wiring regressed.\n- Null-user test comment rewritten to be precise about the 401-vs-403\n  divergence between production (auth-middleware short-circuits with\n  401) and the requireRole-in-isolation test (403).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"d2f790322e5c41b7b1af44e6d655d6552c8080d7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/urule-ai/urule/git/trees/d2f790322e5c41b7b1af44e6d655d6552c8080d7"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/urule-ai/urule/git/commits/d5ec3a666608aa2e44d605d16ad077b32be7aaa9","verification":{"payload":"tree d2f790322e5c41b7b1af44e6d655d6552c8080d7\nparent 5ebafd1c3e909f99509170237a7798b814d993aa\nauthor PanoramicRum <ricardobarcar@gmail.com> 1780051779 -0600\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1780051779 -0600\n\nfeat(security): governance admin-only authz (#4 phase J — final) (#113)\n\n* feat(security): admin-only authz on governance (#4 phase J — final)\n\nPhase J of urule issue #4 (system-wide missing authorization), and the\nlast service in the rollout. Adds `requireRole(''admin'')` to every\ngovernance route — `/decide`, `/policy/evaluate`, `/authz/check`,\n`/authz/batch-check`. The previous posture was \"any authenticated user,\"\nwhich let any JWT-holder probe policy decisions and OpenFGA tuples\nacross the platform — information disclosure across every workspace.\n\nGovernance is off-pattern: routes are service-to-service decision\nendpoints, not user-driven, so `requireMembership(workspaceId)` doesn''t\napply. Mirrors packagehub''s special-case principle (use a non-membership\nauthz model that fits the service). Services that need to call governance\nwill use admin service-account JWTs; the SKIP_AUTH mock user already has\n`admin`, so the existing route + correlation-id + CORS tests stay green\nwithout changes.\n\n- adds `tests/authz-enforcement.test.ts` — 17 tests: 4 routes × 4 user\n  shapes (admin / non-admin / no-roles / null) + an audit-still-fires\n  regression\n- adds `@urule/authz-middleware` workspace dep\n\nOut of scope: composing governance into docker-compose.phase6.yaml\n(currently only in the test-compose file — the natural trigger is when\nthe first internal caller wires up, per registry''s TODO marker).\n\nCloses the issue #4 rollout. Phases A-J shipped.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* review fixes(governance): real audit-fires assertion + clearer null-user comment\n\nAddress findings from the Phase J PR review:\n\n- The audit-fires regression test was a placebo — only asserted 200 and\n  body shape, never verified the audit event actually emitted. Tightened\n  to spy on `app.log.info` and check at least one call carries the\n  expected `{ audit: true, topic: ''urule.audit.config.changed'', data: {\n  entityType: ''governance-decision'' } }` shape, after draining the\n  fire-and-forget microtask via `setImmediate`. Would now fail if the\n  preHandler accidentally short-circuited the handler OR if the audit\n  wiring regressed.\n- Null-user test comment rewritten to be precise about the 401-vs-403\n  divergence between production (auth-middleware short-circuits with\n  401) and the requireRole-in-isolation test (403).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqGW9DCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAl/YQAIXJuXF0twIHEZNZ5Em0jTIy\nr+5bi5QbgD4NYOj7KLxnTtFKMwuaYmp4jJKaT+k43FHGFM7J1+rVGNfWUafuA3bX\nkfbHUNBc5O1sqV0V7OBCJjleQIwwfPxk