admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/urule-ai/urule/commit/46885551e7139f04c277ca9c8fd3a9e27247ee6e","node_id":"C_kwDORxyz5NoAKDQ2ODg1NTUxZTcxMzlmMDRjMjc3Y2E5YzhmZDNhOWUyNzI0N2VlNmU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/urule-ai/urule/commit/ef49bca63238ad7afa79150cafe6ee947df24b30","sha":"ef49bca63238ad7afa79150cafe6ee947df24b30","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/urule-ai/urule/commits/ef49bca63238ad7afa79150cafe6ee947df24b30"}],"sha":"46885551e7139f04c277ca9c8fd3a9e27247ee6e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/urule-ai/urule/commits/46885551e7139f04c277ca9c8fd3a9e27247ee6e"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6556452?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/PanoramicRum","id":6556452,"login":"PanoramicRum","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY1NTY0NTI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/urule-ai/urule/commits/ef49bca63238ad7afa79150cafe6ee947df24b30/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-18T13:29:21Z","email":"ricardobarcar@gmail.com","name":"PanoramicRum"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-18T13:29:21Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(packagehub): publisher-ownership authorization on publish routes (#4 phase E) (#107)\n\nPhase E of issue #4 (C-04). Unlike registry/state/packages, a packagehub\npackage has no workspace — it is global, keyed by name. The hole: POST /packages\nwas fully public (name-squatting) and POST .../versions let any authenticated\nuser publish a version to any package (takeover). The fix is an npm-style\npublisher-ownership model, not OpenFGA.\n\n- @urule/auth-middleware: `publicRoutes` entries may now be method-qualified\n  (`GET /api/v1/packages` — public for GET only, so a POST to the same path\n  still authenticates). Backward compatible — bare-path entries are unchanged.\n- packagehub: new nullable `packages.publisher_id` column (migration 0006).\n- POST /api/v1/packages now authenticates (moved behind the method-qualified\n  public route) and records the caller as the package''s `publisherId`.\n- POST /api/v1/packages/:name/versions: when the package has a `publisherId`,\n  only that account may publish — 403 NOT_PACKAGE_OWNER otherwise. Legacy\n  packages (null publisherId — seed / pre-ownership data) fall back to the\n  existing signature gate. The signature checks are unchanged.\n\nTests: auth-middleware method-qualified publicRoutes; packagehub\nauthz-publisher.test.ts (publisherId recorded, non-owner 403, owner 201,\nlegacy package still publishes); auth-401 updated for the new route config.\nauth-middleware 13 + packagehub 107 + repo-wide typecheck green.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"7af16eeae0ed0c167b0b6844d85407789c6d49b5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/urule-ai/urule/git/trees/7af16eeae0ed0c167b0b6844d85407789c6d49b5"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/urule-ai/urule/git/commits/ef49bca63238ad7afa79150cafe6ee947df24b30","verification":{"payload":"tree 7af16eeae0ed0c167b0b6844d85407789c6d49b5\nparent 76b0b9bd9ffa251cda44e0e54b24dbf452ea87b2\nauthor PanoramicRum <ricardobarcar@gmail.com> 1779110961 -0600\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1779110961 -0600\n\nfeat(packagehub): publisher-ownership authorization on publish routes (#4 phase E) (#107)\n\nPhase E of issue #4 (C-04). Unlike registry/state/packages, a packagehub\npackage has no workspace — it is global, keyed by name. The hole: POST /packages\nwas fully public (name-squatting) and POST .../versions let any authenticated\nuser publish a version to any package (takeover). The fix is an npm-style\npublisher-ownership model, not OpenFGA.\n\n- @urule/auth-middleware: `publicRoutes` entries may now be method-qualified\n  (`GET /api/v1/packages` — public for GET only, so a POST to the same path\n  still authenticates). Backward compatible — bare-path entries are unchanged.\n- packagehub: new nullable `packages.publisher_id` column (migration 0006).\n- POST /api/v1/packages now authenticates (moved behind the method-qualified\n  public route) and records the caller as the package''s `publisherId`.\n- POST /api/v1/packages/:name/versions: when the package has a `publisherId`,\n  only that account may publish — 403 NOT_PACKAGE_OWNER otherwise. Legacy\n  packages (null publisherId — seed / pre-ownership data) fall back to the\n  existing signature gate. The signature checks are unchanged.\n\nTests: auth-middleware method-qualified publicRoutes; packagehub\nauthz-publisher.test.ts (publisherId recorded, non-owner 403, owner 201,\nlegacy package still publishes); auth-401 updated for the new route config.\nauth-middleware 13 + packagehub 107 + repo-wide typecheck green.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqCxQxCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAXVIQAC8Qn1+bH2b7IwVMvTTmAfPH\n5TXo34FOTKOEZC7rLd4Xbv8nL68g6oUnzn0AUBzsJJLzFPgMNmxSaylK9RQ1PRBi\nI0