github.com/users/PanoramicRum/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/urule-ai/urule/commits/b1fe1537661bd52d1427681e08eb9c26f1fc5d98/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-18T06:07:48Z","email":"ricardobarcar@gmail.com","name":"PanoramicRum"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-18T06:07:48Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(state): resource-level authorization on the state service (#4 phase C) (#105)\n\nPhase C of issue #4 (C-04). The `state` service held the other critical IDOR\nsurface — case C (\"delete any room/task\") and case D (\"spoof presence as\nanother user\"). `state` keeps all data in-memory, so it writes no tuples and\nneeds no backfill: it is a pure authz consumer that resolves a room/task/widget\nto its workspace and checks workspace membership.\n\nShared bootstrap:\n- Promote the OpenFGA store/model bootstrap into `@urule/authz` as\n  `bootstrapAuthzClient` — one implementation every service reuses. Registry\n  migrated off its local `buildAuthzClient` copy.\n\nstate enforcement:\n- New `services/state/src/authz.ts` — workspace-id resolvers over the in-memory\n  managers (room/task/widget → workspaceId) plus `requireSelfOrAdmin`.\n- `requireMembership` preHandler on every state write route: rooms, presence,\n  tasks (+assign), widget-state, typing. `config.ts`/`server.ts` gain the\n  OpenFGA wiring + `authzMiddleware`.\n\nIdentity-spoofing fix (case D):\n- `POST presence`/`typing` derive the user from the JWT; `POST /tasks` derives\n  `creatorId` from the JWT — the body''s `userId`/`workspaceId`/`creatorId` are\n  now optional and ignored, so they can no longer be forged.\n- `PATCH`/`DELETE` presence & typing by `:userId` require self (admin exempt).\n\nTests: new `tests/authz-enforcement.test.ts` (403/2xx/admin-bypass/404 + the\nspoofing fixes); `collaboration-journey` + `routes` tests updated to inject\ndistinct users now that identity is server-derived. state 64 + registry 76 +\nauthz 21 + repo-wide typecheck green.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"cb026b1cc5ed4baac9b228119c29e2d240360f72","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/urule-ai/urule/git/trees/cb026b1cc5ed4baac9b228119c29e2d240360f72"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/urule-ai/urule/git/commits/b1fe1537661bd52d1427681e08eb9c26f1fc5d98","verification":{"payload":"tree cb026b1cc5ed4baac9b228119c29e2d240360f72\nparent 6091e35decd977191ebdf7990eb7d446b53051f2\nauthor PanoramicRum <ricardobarcar@gmail.com> 1779084468 -0600\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1779084468 -0600\n\nfeat(state): resource-level authorization on the state service (#4 phase C) (#105)\n\nPhase C of issue #4 (C-04). The `state` service held the other critical IDOR\nsurface — case C (\"delete any room/task\") and case D (\"spoof presence as\nanother user\"). `state` keeps all data in-memory, so it writes no tuples and\nneeds no backfill: it is a pure authz consumer that resolves a room/task/widget\nto its workspace and checks workspace membership.\n\nShared bootstrap:\n- Promote the OpenFGA store/model bootstrap into `@urule/authz` as\n  `bootstrapAuthzClient` — one implementation every service reuses. Registry\n  migrated off its local `buildAuthzClient` copy.\n\nstate enforcement:\n- New `services/state/src/authz.ts` — workspace-id resolvers over the in-memory\n  managers (room/task/widget → workspaceId) plus `requireSelfOrAdmin`.\n- `requireMembership` preHandler on every state write route: rooms, presence,\n  tasks (+assign), widget-state, typing. `config.ts`/`server.ts` gain the\n  OpenFGA wiring + `authzMiddleware`.\n\nIdentity-spoofing fix (case D):\n- `POST presence`/`typing` derive the user from the JWT; `POST /tasks` derives\n  `creatorId` from the JWT — the body''s `userId`/`workspaceId`/`creatorId` are\n  now optional and ignored, so they can no longer be forged.\n- `PATCH`/`DELETE` presence & typing by `:userId` require self (admin exempt).\n\nTests: new `tests/authz-enforcement.test.ts` (403/2xx/admin-bypass/404 + the\nspoofing fixes); `collaboration-journey` + `routes` tests updated to inject\ndistinct users now that identity is server-derived. state 64 + registry 76 +\nauthz 21 + repo-wide typecheck green.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqCqy0CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA5QwQAGHDjUYUFb1FiM/Xz5ZzjqYv\nMaGHmk2+ifHA9N3yhbv/fZQTqNiPlG+wbMVDaraMISGqefAoCmJ/0Y5TxMxbm1ca\nBVnpv06Vs5dO1Qymg29G7Y+kg4QzYcJnkiTxqddE9bnPdETJHT4EAC04uyVkYzSG\nWVdh9xvtHwIwVTUMS2M11EAW77BfFpOw4h8FedCtLPEm0dj6ePY/HUB/WXIeah72\nveyXhGq16CwEzpwHVOY0Ics4lx2oqm7Awx1ZY31k/55DlIXasYk7cS45SHY7/zCk\nmIpKYrAQWKv2AfIjqyHWLZDJbDsJ1X0WxnkbGJxYXF4kb9zk7gJMRbl6EORDVzZd\nTyVaFUX3Ta1sIonbZiUQKEE8JFMWrjGqCevqfA+YH5QLmNm8gZGZFQeD6Vp1TrJl\n4y7lZwhIzBquWGjU21FoDncwyDOHKQVHehm+bl8S0sgEt8GmnGc0+YCmCwumfGLU\nfRoaCFWWcb8v9z+H6BLwprIplqhfkUzvQgtsxgf3Fjpns+S+zrwkyrpnt3vkqOtI\nm6ayWjBNw0GqhcYaZJCWO7Sug3u1GDGAgbU5d38WwfxxsNmnPlxVBlvoyewvfo7V\nVK4qecHp5qEy1rgfQ1trlPSnXkUP6rBysn5w5g9mvnW8AD9ucOSvRH/BSjtPb8IF\njGrt/6PlO+RCkC3nJhQW\n=OeMQ\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-05-18T06:07:48Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/urule-ai/urule/commit/b1fe1537661bd52d1427681e08eb9c26f1fc5d98","node_id":"C_kwDORxyz5NoAKGIxZmUxNTM3NjYxYmQ1MmQxNDI3NjgxZTA4ZWI5YzI2ZjFmYzVkOTg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/urule-ai/urule/commit/6091e35decd977191ebdf7990eb7d446b53051f2","sha":"6091e35decd977191ebdf7990eb7d446b53051f2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/urule-ai/urule/commits/6091e35decd977191ebdf7990eb7d446b53051f2"}],"sha":"b1fe1537661bd52d1427681e08eb9c26f1fc5d98","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/urule-ai/urule/commits/b1fe1537661bd52d1427681e08eb9c26f1fc5d98"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6556452?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/PanoramicRum","id":6556452,"login":"PanoramicRum","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY1NTY0NTI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/urule-ai/urule/commits/6091e35decd977191ebdf7990eb7d446b53051f2/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-18T05:13:21Z","email":"ricardobarcar@gmail.com","name":"PanoramicRum"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-18T05:13:21Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(registry): enforce workspace membership on write routes (#4 phase B2) (#104)\n\nSecond half of issue #4 Phase B. PR B1 made the OpenFGA ownership tuples\nexist; this turns on the resource-level checks that read them — closing the\nregistry IDOR surface (C-04 cases B/C: read/delete across foreign workspaces).\n\n- @urule/authz-middleware: `requireMembership` now bypasses the OpenFGA check\n  for users carrying the `admin` realm role — a global ops/support escape hatch\n  that also keeps the SKIP_AUTH dev stack working without seeded tuples. The\n  bypass short-circuits before touching `request.authz`.\n- registry/src/authz.ts: workspace-id resolvers for the preHandlers —\n  `bodyWorkspaceResolver` (create routes; mirrors the existing `\"default\"` →\n  first-workspace fallback) and `agent/provider/conversationWorkspaceResolver`\n  (id-addressed routes; entity lookup → workspaceId, null → 404 without leaking\n  existence).\n- Every registry write route now carries a `requireMembership` preHandler:\n  POST/PATCH/DELETE on agents (+memories, +status), providers, conversations\n  (+messages, +branch), runtimes, and `PATCH /workspaces/current[/guardrails]`.\n  `POST /workspaces` gates on parent-org membership; `POST /orgs` is admin-gated\n  via `requireRole(''admin'')` (top-level, no parent resource to scope to).\n\nTests: authz-enforcement.test.ts covers non-member 403, member 2xx, admin\nbypass, and unknown-id 404; +1 admin-bypass test in the authz-middleware\npackage. Registry 76 tests + authz-middleware 15 + repo-wide typecheck green.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"414970a3732309fa77dfdcac4ffdf5e137264d68","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/urule-ai/urule/git/trees/414970a3732309fa77dfdcac4ffdf5e137264d68"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/urule-ai/urule/git/commits/6091e35decd977191ebdf7990eb7d446b53051f2","verification":{"payload":"tree 414970a3732309fa77dfdcac4ffdf5e137264d68\nparent 78d2a9f5234e53e53ffd37e19c833e7d40487437\nauthor PanoramicRum <ricardobarcar@gmail.com> 1779081201 -0600\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1779081201 -0600\n\nfeat(registry): enforce workspace membership on write routes (#4 phase B2) (#104)\n\nSecond half of issue #4 Phase B. PR B1 made the OpenFGA ownership tuples\nexist; this turns on the resource-level checks that read them — closing the\nregistry IDOR surface (C-04 cases B/C: read/delete across foreign workspaces).\n\n- @urule/authz-middleware: `requireMembership` now bypasses the OpenFGA check\n  for users carrying the `admin` realm role — a global ops/support escape hatch\n  that also keeps the SKIP_AUTH dev stack working without seeded tuples. The\n  bypass short-circuits before touching `request.authz`.\n- registry/src/authz.ts: workspace-id resolvers for the preHandlers —\n  `bodyWorkspaceResolver` (create routes; mirrors the existing `\"default\"` →\n  first-workspace fallback) and `agent/provider/conversationWorkspaceResolver`\n  (id-addressed routes; entity lookup → workspaceId, null → 404 without leaking\n  existence).\n- Every registry write route now carries a `requireMembership` preHandler:\n  POST/PATCH/DELETE on agents (+memories, +status), providers, conversations\n  (+messages, +branch), runtimes, and `PATCH /workspaces/current[/guardrails]`.\n  `POST /workspaces` gates on parent-org membership; `POST /orgs` is admin-gated\n  via `requireRole(''admin'')` (top-level, no parent resource to scope to).\n\nTests: authz-enforcement.test.ts covers non-member 403, member 2xx, admin\nbypass, and unknown-id 404; +1 admin-bypass test in the authz-middleware\npackage. Registry 76 tests + authz-middleware 15 + repo-wide typecheck green.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqCp/xCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAALoYQAKwCLJLMwuiHYJZwJacamMXS\n0XS8vh6dd+9NHQzQMkWGSK0DyB7yWsgXkXqdRBg1qqWZ7tOSFNpWMiR3yjMcAi/9\n1R7DSzLdGSzGmSUaZkhrg/k8D0lcqs8CtjY/kudXT/Xl3asAw4baYkryQP3pwj8T\nba1kcItEKLL5JOCBphyUN76nOmR+g/coXo27R2icX8NlYJiws3OiFbqOzgCHgFMC\nKQaK7BajFkOcdORzveqcJ5e9jmq6Ddth3x4LNpreYTeDj8bP+ILbak45x14Qxso0\nOD3y7GJUmLGNPB/8uuyfIGitjomRrBKX3AMGMYrna1TBfWiWlxSqQUOxCH7jQmLQ\ngb00vPxw8UdtGi5/brER25ddMReVeHY0ckSzWQjuwPLZKzE3S7c3YctQcFklr5w8\nDp2Y/3nI+I2+szUip6R+jvyl37E7lCaoUkmHVIGqvdavF4j3sU2MqxQW9+EYHClV\nQZAwWm3x8+kg5sKHGp4oDmMTsW7/1NalXmet1RZqEPG0SqeXRbY9OwHcGG+fIgB1\numouQFEfCAHaztp/VOtw4jym6LFnnpGIKV7O0Qsowwogkxtrx4TRSd00yPjUq0QO\n41MR4Sz+lrmLsddGK4zC5+JGxzUY2CX8t5LrFV+5UA0HGP6Kw4X8LwpUZikwnd+o\nRigkOxVGNDet5KIO+s3N\n=0zqA\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-05-18T05:13:22Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/urule-ai/urule/commit/6091e35decd977191ebdf7990eb7d446b53051f2","node_id":"C_kwDORxyz5NoAKDYwOTFlMzVkZWNkOTc3MTkxZWJkZjc5OTBlYjdkNDQ2YjUzMDUxZjI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/urule-ai/urule/commit/78d2a9f5234e53e53ffd37e19c833e7d40487437","sha":"78d2a9f5234e53e53ffd37e19c833e7d40487437","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/urule-ai/urule/commits/78d2a9f5234e53e53ffd37e19c833e7d40487437"}],"sha":"6091e35decd977191ebdf7990eb7d446b53051f2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/urule-ai/urule/commits/6091e35decd977191ebdf7990eb7d446b53051f2"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6556452?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/PanoramicRum","id":6556452,"login":"PanoramicRum","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY1NTY0NTI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/urule-ai/urule/commits/78d2a9f5234e53e53ffd37e19c833e7d40487437/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-17T20:37:11Z","email":"ricardobarcar@gmail.com","name":"PanoramicRum"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-17T20:37:11Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(registry): write OpenFGA ownership tuples on org/workspace create (#4 phase B1) (#103)\n\nFirst half of issue #4 Phase B for the registry service. Makes the OpenFGA\nauthorization tuples *exist* — no enforcement yet, so the product keeps working\nexactly as before. PR B2 turns on the membership checks that read these tuples.\n\n- config: OPENFGA_URL / OPENFGA_STORE_ID / OPENFGA_MODEL_ID (warn-only — dev\n  stacks without authz fall back to an in-memory mock client).\n- src/authz.ts: buildAuthzClient() — self-bootstraps the `urule` OpenFGA store\n  + writes URULE_AUTH_MODEL on first boot; falls back to the mock client if\n  OpenFGA is unreachable so registry availability is never coupled to it.\n- server.ts: register @urule/authz-middleware after auth-middleware.\n- POST /orgs writes a `user:<creator> owner org:<id>` tuple; POST /workspaces\n  writes `owner` for the creator + a `parent` link to the org so workspace\n  membership inherits org members. Tuple writes are non-fatal (warn + continue),\n  mirroring the audit-logger fire-and-forget pattern. Both routes also gain the\n  previously-missing audit.entityCreated calls.\n- src/authz-backfill.ts: idempotent backfill of owner/parent tuples for orgs &\n  workspaces created before authz existed (the seeded demo tenant). Runs on\n  registry startup and as the new `registry-authz-seed` one-shot compose service.\n- compose: registry gets OPENFGA_URL + depends_on openfga.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"525b4e91a981d375359d516aebbc1a2594b36db0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/urule-ai/urule/git/trees/525b4e91a981d375359d516aebbc1a2594b36db0"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/urule-ai/urule/git/commits/78d2a9f5234e53e53ffd37e19c833e7d40487437","verification":{"payload":"tree 525b4e91a981d375359d516aebbc1a2594b36db0\nparent 95092d84373821def66fbb3b624c3b54a495ee6e\nauthor PanoramicRum <ricardobarcar@gmail.com> 1779050231 -0600\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1779050231 -0600\n\nfeat(registry): write OpenFGA ownership tuples on org/workspace create (#4 phase B1) (#103)\n\nFirst half of issue #4 Phase B for the registry service. Makes the OpenFGA\nauthorization tuples *exist* — no enforcement yet, so the product keeps working\nexactly as before. PR B2 turns on the membership checks that read these tuples.\n\n- config: OPENFGA_URL / OPENFGA_STORE_ID / OPENFGA_MODEL_ID (warn-only — dev\n  stacks without authz fall back to an in-memory mock client).\n- src/authz.ts: buildAuthzClient() — self-bootstraps the `urule` OpenFGA store\n  + writes URULE_AUTH_MODEL on first boot; falls back to the mock client if\n  OpenFGA is unreachable so registry availability is never coupled to it.\n- server.ts: register @urule/authz-middleware after auth-middleware.\n- POST /orgs writes a `user:<creator> owner org:<id>` tuple; POST /workspaces\n  writes `owner` for the creator + a `parent` link to the org so workspace\n  membership inherits org members. Tuple writes are non-fatal (warn + continue),\n  mirroring the audit-logger fire-and-forget pattern. Both routes also gain the\n  previously-missing audit.entityCreated calls.\n- src/authz-backfill.ts: idempotent backfill of owner/parent tuples for orgs &\n  workspaces created before authz existed (the seeded demo tenant). Runs on\n  registry startup and as the new `registry-authz-seed` one-shot compose service.\n- compose: registry gets OPENFGA_URL + depends_on openfga.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqCib3CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA8UUQAJaeXUUZ6GFQ5yBYKPmV1VfZ\n51N2BqXetzXwaMu9UR3CFihBIzXT/PHdT8AtqdOeIJA0qVXuR1RIlLX5/ErgVFLz\nZfda3A7QiSWdFHNyJyAacMyYcTGIlB/lkiTSN7037Vx5C7vgSzt/hQQ5Y6Jxwf1Y\nZdZYoCN+AFsoLUmbE2zMjGFhFxXFDYyfyn9Ed7FvDLnuO4CtCeUb7rHwaOZ2YjqJ\ngnrmCxhXC2vXWHyTZAoNAHFQ8l0Qcge2Cy0EVd9FOGU7RbYTh7RjhkWzgnQaQyR0\n78z67LkB8etpRAXeqXImylvVK+65HACOnKE5UsrKaUFh8e1/qO4WsRZc