_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/urule-ai/urule/commits/a450913e653c884f386887dd809d7867b515ed79/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-13T18:30:09Z","email":"ricardobarcar@gmail.com","name":"PanoramicRum"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-13T18:30:09Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"chore(roadmap): mark Tier 1 security-audit items done (PRs #92–#100) (#101)\n\nThe 8 Tier 1 surgical fixes from §1.7 all landed across PRs #92–#100. Updated\nthe checklist with the closing PR for each, plus a pointer to the #95 sibling-\nroutes / office-ui follow-up. Tier 2 (architectural — system-wide authz, the\npackagehub/installer hardening, prompt-injection, localStorage tokens,\nWidgetFrame postMessage, Stripe webhook metadata, llm-providers retry/timeout)\nremains as the next phase — each item its own design + PR.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"9676dc1163dcb3178a338867127d5234ea588d8f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/urule-ai/urule/git/trees/9676dc1163dcb3178a338867127d5234ea588d8f"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/urule-ai/urule/git/commits/a450913e653c884f386887dd809d7867b515ed79","verification":{"payload":"tree 9676dc1163dcb3178a338867127d5234ea588d8f\nparent c7fded8fb98dda68598b8b4fb6abbab1d0eeae84\nauthor PanoramicRum <ricardobarcar@gmail.com> 1778697009 -0600\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1778697009 -0600\n\nchore(roadmap): mark Tier 1 security-audit items done (PRs #92–#100) (#101)\n\nThe 8 Tier 1 surgical fixes from §1.7 all landed across PRs #92–#100. Updated\nthe checklist with the closing PR for each, plus a pointer to the #95 sibling-\nroutes / office-ui follow-up. Tier 2 (architectural — system-wide authz, the\npackagehub/installer hardening, prompt-injection, localStorage tokens,\nWidgetFrame postMessage, Stripe webhook metadata, llm-providers retry/timeout)\nremains as the next phase — each item its own design + PR.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqBMMxCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAPGQQAJ7tRDrAc4Ekz6dKD8ISq1hU\npJux74I8zdGufPzohWW5sOBJ4KODVrmu7/dSo5ncZWz85EmVLr0doKSbQLTOnPFN\nRw8ZdbgWYtBYxG/5KkpD+qbLN+Y43yYvxl0OFdq8ltufu5M9kkOXWIHtjmYjFI27\nhklkNDIGe3nUWUqsnIP0hbR/ZZmTzOH7n7gXQpawyrerMmkyp361uhpwyl8KeDVq\nMODVq9sincxg3Q5A8WcG3hZsoXxW8Yf9YHmR/8q/n8htdTCr2XxeBA7SMd3Kt4ZC\nmv04jhFJjo+R8cwHBQacmCELmRrR53R+eTA7HTPeYB+kLwntVIzI8roHTqvV8ACu\nLGjYyeLfFhZHqcVRwHgtb1ALQjIMvuXkwoteSqPrzaFiSmMo7xgkHKBv6F7Xssnc\nwQoDPnf1aMahWLLB8dv5PzY5J+SemQes1OXwCU7S0gO7IzyRKVTID6umbq75hrJg\nVf0TXoUwCptA9Ipe9RtseXC+NK9inw0FPgedlNsOkvnnY4Mq0JZ60Aan1js4PUuB\nIFD5pfsU7PBtnliSkh67GtM+6r0HgJX0QAY2S3h/XCcLp22TAZutgXdHvy2KFNxb\n2hdkAR4UmKfOaudcwyvmvXbugKkmv6J7bsUGdex/FWBPeqX5BX+Hv9RkZ/C1wAtI\npAqYqhGrh6pF3RQskvAX\n=xI0o\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-05-13T18:30:10Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/urule-ai/urule/commit/a450913e653c884f386887dd809d7867b515ed79","node_id":"C_kwDORxyz5NoAKGE0NTA5MTNlNjUzYzg4NGYzODY4ODdkZDgwOWQ3ODY3YjUxNWVkNzk","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/urule-ai/urule/commit/c7fded8fb98dda68598b8b4fb6abbab1d0eeae84","sha":"c7fded8fb98dda68598b8b4fb6abbab1d0eeae84","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/urule-ai/urule/commits/c7fded8fb98dda68598b8b4fb6abbab1d0eeae84"}],"sha":"a450913e653c884f386887dd809d7867b515ed79","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/urule-ai/urule/commits/a450913e653c884f386887dd809d7867b515ed79"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6556452?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/PanoramicRum","id":6556452,"login":"PanoramicRum","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY1NTY0NTI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/urule-ai/urule/commits/c7fded8fb98dda68598b8b4fb6abbab1d0eeae84/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-13T08:30:39Z","email":"ricardobarcar@gmail.com","name":"PanoramicRum"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-13T08:30:39Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(infra): non-root USER in all in-repo Dockerfiles + Helm runAsNonRoot (#23) (#100)\n\n#23: every container ran as root because none of the seven in-repo Dockerfiles\nhad a `USER` directive. Now each runner stage (and the migrator stages for\nregistry / packagehub / packages) does `RUN chown -R node:node /app` + `USER\nnode` before its CMD. The `node:20-slim` base image ships a `node` user at uid\n1000; the healthcheck''s embedded `node -e \"fetch(''/healthz'')…\"` runs fine as\nthe same user.\n\nHelm: added a global `podSecurityContext: { runAsNonRoot: true, runAsUser:\n1000, fsGroup: 1000 }` default in `values.yaml`; the deployments + migrate-jobs\ntemplates emit it when set. Disable per-deploy via `--set\nglobal.podSecurityContext=null` (the values.yaml comment documents the why).\n\nOut of scope: standalones (approvals, channel-router, mcp-gateway, runtime-\nbroker, langgraph-adapter) live in separate repos and still run as root in\ntheir own Dockerfiles. Until they catch up they can''t deploy under the\nsecure-by-default Helm chart — operators override or fix the standalone\nDockerfile. Called out inline in `values.yaml`.\n\nVerified: `npm run typecheck:all` (18/18), `npm run build:all` (14/14), `docker\ncompose -f docker-compose.phase6.yaml config` valid. (Actual `docker build`\nverification happens on the docker-publish workflow when a release tag goes up.)\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"ce56668728940d0b75ee949517f51e0ebd46e9fe","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/urule-ai/urule/git/trees/ce56668728940d0b75ee949517f51e0ebd46e9fe"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/urule-ai/urule/git/commits/c7fded8fb98dda68598b8b4fb6abbab1d0eeae84","verification":{"payload":"tree ce56668728940d0b75ee949517f51e0ebd46e9fe\nparent 613e4bffeb7d4aef08103169cab31d23d777d308\nauthor PanoramicRum <ricardobarcar@gmail.com> 1778661039 -0600\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1778661039 -0600\n\nfix(infra): non-root USER in all in-repo Dockerfiles + Helm runAsNonRoot (#23) (#100)\n\n#23: every container ran as root because none of the seven in-repo Dockerfiles\nhad a `USER` directive. Now each runner stage (and the migrator stages for\nregistry / packagehub / packages) does `RUN chown -R node:node /app` + `USER\nnode` before its CMD. The `node:20-slim` base image ships a `node` user at uid\n1000; the healthcheck''s embedded `node -e \"fetch(''/healthz'')…\"` runs fine as\nthe same user.\n\nHelm: added a global `podSecurityContext: { runAsNonRoot: true, runAsUser:\n1000, fsGroup: 1000 }` default in `values.yaml`; the deployments + migrate-jobs\ntemplates emit it when set. Disable per-deploy via `--set\nglobal.podSecurityContext=null` (the values.yaml comment documents the why).\n\nOut of scope: standalones (approvals, channel-router, mcp-gateway, runtime-\nbroker, langgraph-adapter) live in separate repos and still run as root in\ntheir own Dockerfiles. Until they catch up they can''t deploy under the\nsecure-by-default Helm chart — operators override or fix the standalone\nDockerfile. Called out inline in `values.yaml`.\n\nVerified: `npm run typecheck:all` (18/18), `npm run build:all` (14/14), `docker\ncompose -f docker-compose.phase6.yaml config` valid. (Actual `docker build`\nverification happens on the docker-publish workflow when a release tag goes up.)\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqBDavCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAU78QACQ3eObjggqih0ApPGksjVGq\nCH8dgEo+Eze1O+8idv9xRucmQiQ1gzlxLsFZXkBiy4Z0S6N3gdY/BgLY/sB0YQIz\n+xBGUyX3WJQ3WySnJZhT78OSOIcOmy79AFVob/O6zmWSP65fc/qtLhMGbtsmS+rL\nkvvsjhzoFk