ps://api.github.com/repos/urule-ai/urule/commits/46a9024283d37873264aef99053bdd986a60c1fc"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6556452?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/PanoramicRum","id":6556452,"login":"PanoramicRum","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY1NTY0NTI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/urule-ai/urule/commits/179efbba9fbf3f308d91e8d4df65d240a879eb86/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-13T05:11:52Z","email":"ricardobarcar@gmail.com","name":"PanoramicRum"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-13T05:11:52Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(infra): pin :latest container images — compose + Helm (#24, #45) (#97)\n\n#24: the docker-compose infra services pulled `:latest` for Temporal (×2),\nKeycloak, OpenFGA, OPA, the OTel collector, and Jaeger — no reproducibility,\nand a broken/malicious upstream push hits you immediately. Pinned each to a\nspecific tag (temporalio/auto-setup:1.25.0, temporalio/ui:2.30.0,\nquay.io/keycloak/keycloak:26.1, openfga/openfga:v1.8.0, openpolicyagent/opa:1.0.0,\notel/opentelemetry-collector-contrib:0.116.0, jaegertracing/all-in-one:1.62.0).\npostgres / nats / prometheus / grafana were already pinned. Bump these as\nupstream releases — the requirement is \"not :latest\", not \"the newest\".\n\n#45: the Helm chart''s `global.imageTag` default was `latest`, and the\n`urule.image` helper fell back to `latest` when unset. Both now default to\n`\"0.1.0\"` (matches the chart appVersion / workspace package versions; a `v0.1.0`\ngit tag publishes `<registry>/<service>:0.1.0`). The README already documents\noverriding `global.imageTag` per deploy.\n\nVerified: `docker compose -f docker-compose.phase6.yaml config` valid; the\nchanged files parse as valid YAML; no `:latest` left under infra/.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"126dc0ab13cc6fb70ed2868132e670e35b8218bb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/urule-ai/urule/git/trees/126dc0ab13cc6fb70ed2868132e670e35b8218bb"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/urule-ai/urule/git/commits/179efbba9fbf3f308d91e8d4df65d240a879eb86","verification":{"payload":"tree 126dc0ab13cc6fb70ed2868132e670e35b8218bb\nparent f9b82e55bd98ce564d3e962350f5d21cb8060d31\nauthor PanoramicRum <ricardobarcar@gmail.com> 1778649112 -0600\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1778649112 -0600\n\nfix(infra): pin :latest container images — compose + Helm (#24, #45) (#97)\n\n#24: the docker-compose infra services pulled `:latest` for Temporal (×2),\nKeycloak, OpenFGA, OPA, the OTel collector, and Jaeger — no reproducibility,\nand a broken/malicious upstream push hits you immediately. Pinned each to a\nspecific tag (temporalio/auto-setup:1.25.0, temporalio/ui:2.30.0,\nquay.io/keycloak/keycloak:26.1, openfga/openfga:v1.8.0, openpolicyagent/opa:1.0.0,\notel/opentelemetry-collector-contrib:0.116.0, jaegertracing/all-in-one:1.62.0).\npostgres / nats / prometheus / grafana were already pinned. Bump these as\nupstream releases — the requirement is \"not :latest\", not \"the newest\".\n\n#45: the Helm chart''s `global.imageTag` default was `latest`, and the\n`urule.image` helper fell back to `latest` when unset. Both now default to\n`\"0.1.0\"` (matches the chart appVersion / workspace package versions; a `v0.1.0`\ngit tag publishes `<registry>/<service>:0.1.0`). The README already documents\noverriding `global.imageTag` per deploy.\n\nVerified: `docker compose -f docker-compose.phase6.yaml config` valid; the\nchanged files parse as valid YAML; no `:latest` left under infra/.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqBAgYCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAC0kQACwN2NaSO1bJT8CpQFTcR6us\nPpLX/TOEyhXPFsevKHvW2Cq98s7VfXu6LuEqdSCKwmi9FImlaUrhRNiCkT/LYAdr\ntqWzHCGHQYvILr/guKLSDW8iAilQ63eCGji/zgpUL14UfZ4EJfB+mzTxZmyT8B2Y\nhsnCCFP8vOP2flPQEGHjdJOyobLBvyImGqNcNZfg3wXpIJ8ygdXmtTn68L4Bx6a3\nFSJH2jmbu48M/b/B9v7fjMc6OeCGA2brQr8D6OLy/ll23WVLXIYze5pSBPTiSZlN\nJlz8qltMr1AbSljPgfGvCLVnGRYDn0eDxAj9moOB0EgSxaJGUl6ImWcl8JpGIvtS\nYpXWIR4OavenwSZyBS9l754B3rbzXz54Weqq6MY6o8zR5eofRSPYwOEWVQy2zfqQ\nf6Y8NuwKULOP701noJjmHWguN6M8g1gTFo/rCLqAe8yXd5RG/hljGio84xAD7oYp\nXcN21hjQp6IXMbfKfjliewiTGIc45d54rmBlMZsa6Dv1nPzQsNzfkl75gSbv216H\nIvhFKdVTMzKS53EiJIIpxg+DZxI7VSFBLuWUbC8Tol5pMVqz3depmuaeWQOwDfuc\n0aNN0M9ICzFdMLGNT2B92SNywlNYZuYTEijX3+QxoCbfKN4VnLIK38gKH1c7wUSp\nooZjOrANvBUFws4OngY+\n=fB9e\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-05-13T05:11:53Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/urule-ai/urule/commit/179efbba9fbf3f308d91e8d4df65d240a879eb86","node_id":"C_kwDORxyz5NoAKDE3OWVmYmJhOWZiZjNmMzA4ZDkxZThkNGRmNjVkMjQwYTg3OWViODY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/urule-ai/urule/commit/f9b82e55bd98ce564d3e962350f5d21cb8060d31","sha":"f9b82e55bd98ce564d3e962350f5d21cb8060d31","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/urule-ai/urule/commits/f9b82e55bd98ce564d3e962350f5d21cb8060d31"}],"sha":"179efbba9fbf3f308d91e8d4df65d240a879eb86","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/urule-ai/urule/commits/179efbba9fbf3f308d91e8d4df65d240a879eb86"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6556452?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/PanoramicRum","id":6556452,"login":"PanoramicRum","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY1NTY0NTI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/urule-ai/urule/commits/f9b82e55bd98ce564d3e962350f5d21cb8060d31/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-13T04:24:44Z","email":"ricardobarcar@gmail.com","name":"PanoramicRum"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-13T04:24:44Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(registry): admin-gate the cross-workspace GET /api/v1/agents (#25) (#96)\n\n`GET /api/v1/agents` is the cross-workspace \"admin-shaped\" list — it returned\nevery workspace''s agents to any authenticated caller, no admin guard (despite\nthe route''s own doc: \"Admin-shaped — most callers should use /workspaces/:wsId/\nagents\"). Now it requires the `admin` realm role; non-admin and anonymous\ncallers get 403, pointed at the workspace-scoped variant.\n\nStill works in the dev compose (registry runs SKIP_AUTH=true → mock admin).\nTracked in #95: the office-ui''s ~9 agent-list queries should switch to\n/api/v1/workspaces/:wsId/agents, and the sibling \"admin-shaped\" routes\n(/workspaces, /orgs, /runtimes, /conversations) need the same guard. TODO(#4):\nonce the authz layer can scope to the caller''s workspaces, prefer that over a\nblanket admin gate.\n\nTests (services/registry/tests/unit/agents-list-guard.test.ts): 403 for a\nnon-admin, 403 for an anonymous request, 200 + the list for an admin. Registry\nsuite: 10 files / 65 tests green.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"057382714207fe976260d091421c25d2e442c47e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/urule-ai/urule/git/trees/057382714207fe976260d091421c25d2e442c47e"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/urule-ai/urule/git/commits/f9b82e55bd98ce564d3e962350f5d21cb8060d31","verification":{"payload":"tree 057382714207fe976260d091421c25d2e442c47e\nparent e503a8f21cfac1e8330197f59279ccf42b94f848\nauthor PanoramicRum <ricardobarcar@gmail.com> 1778646284 -0600\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1778646284 -0600\n\nfix(registry): admin-gate the cross-workspace GET /api/v1/agents (#25) (#96)\n\n`GET /api/v1/agents` is the cross-workspace \"admin-shaped\" list — it returned\nevery workspace''s agents to any authenticated caller, no admin guard (despite\nthe route''s own doc: \"Admin-shaped — most callers should use /workspaces/:wsId/\nagents\"). Now it requires the `admin` realm role; non-admin and anonymous\ncallers get 403, pointed at the workspace-scoped variant.\n\nStill works in the dev compose (registry runs SKIP_AUTH=true → mock admin).\nTracked in #95: the office-ui''s ~9 agent-list queries should switch to\n/api/v1/workspaces/:wsId/agents, and the sibling \"admin-shaped\" routes\n(/workspaces, /orgs, /runtimes, /conversations) need the same guard. TODO(#4):\nonce the authz layer can scope to the caller''s workspaces, prefer that over a\nblanket admin gate.\n\nTests (services/registry/tests/unit/agents-list-guard.test.ts): 403 for a\nnon-admin, 403 for an anonymous request, 200 + the list for an admin. Registry\nsuite: 10 files / 65 tests green.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqA/0MCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAL2AQAELcZDv9gG1YOnxl77g2xZtA\noTNIQPvaaAn3XeaCFV9nYf6OvKViVIxXJA8KMkZjKyWk6geDh91IviGGcLkck3UP\nJndLJEIt+/bd4AtVasvD5ETBKjWmcpN43nQtPxUDI9u7D0obJr1BeK8U1N+Sl+Cr\nkG50MYDZOjB6c9GPXOSrWrVhXnQhIpb9zIlMHaQkQRLWxA9JGB2EkUzTVVSB9eUb\nHv0HgJuZ77raDg8bfn8zBGVm7N/AuZvyLGG+Q1LvDP34COVZ2MxRhjSRAkiWlvux\nwzrKacuNLhy4xn/b9l7eLuEIpudaY4QBw8VDcYwxz312YxifsEyujkD+uERkRgXN\nfWto10rbJQfg/d01ETUC42osJ37PmMaGa2cESqaanXQklCF8vP3qa1NfsI/BGWt4\nTFMwCwue1HNhyOi3aTpXaFtrZ9bz/rOIPCZT92Oe6CrlpnIDhfeF+/Mj37fAydik\n0lnQzXm3+CcbX4eK12z1EQWUu1gjCvN4cbZLxqhoAe4IbfCGCV70ZnPekzko+J60\ngFpnAGdkKPof2L+iJo1XZdmbq2cDK/9XSQjAdRSTywvOFaEWFlNHrJ805DWDA5Bb\n9cQzbrN2nosWiVMxAikUz7GECRR3v/XnhX483WvuMEESWcx6Q6LL5j/Zrha2kWNd\nh/GoZqzqz9Eonp+o8gg5\n=wj5v\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-05-13T04:24:45Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/urule-ai/urule/commit/f9b82e55bd98ce564d3e962350f5d21cb8060d31","node_id":"C_kwDORxyz5NoAKGY5YjgyZTU1YmQ5OGNlNTY0ZDNlOTYyMzUwZjVkMjFjYjgwNjBkMzE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/urule-ai/urule/commit/e503a8f21cfac1e8330197f59279ccf42b94f848","sha":"e503a8f21cfac1e8330197f59279ccf42b94f848","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/urule-ai/urule/commits/e503a8f21cfac1e8330197f59279ccf42b94f848"}],"sha":"f9b82e55bd98ce564d3e962350f5d21cb8060d31","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/urule-ai/urule/commits/f9b82e55bd98ce564d3e962350f5d21cb8060d31"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6556452?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/PanoramicRum","id":6556452,"login":"PanoramicRum","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY1NTY0NTI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/urule-ai/urule/commits/e503a8f21cfac1e8330197f59279ccf42b94f848/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-12T20:05:00Z","email":"ricardobarcar@gmail.com","name":"PanoramicRum"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-12T20:05:00Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(infra): require docker-compose credentials via ${VAR:?} — no insecure defaults (#12, #46) (#94)\n\nThe compose stack shipped working default credentials baked into the YAML —\n`POSTGRES_PASSWORD: urule` (and `POSTGRES_PWD`/`KC_DB_PASSWORD` reusing it),\n`KEYCLOAK_ADMIN_PASSWORD: admin`, `GF_SECURITY_ADMIN_PASSWORD: urule`, plus the\n`postgres://urule:urule@...` DSNs in every service''s `DATABASE_URL` and the\n`PGPASSWORD` in the seed jobs. Anyone deploying the compose as-is got known\ncreds.\n\nNow the credentials are required env vars (`${POSTGRES_PASSWORD:?}`,\n`${KEYCLOAK_ADMIN_PASSWORD:?}`, `${GRAFANA_ADMIN_PASSWORD:?}`) — a service\nrefuses to start when its credential is missing; no insecure value lives in the\nYAML. (Usernames / DB names stay literal — not secrets.)\n\n- `infra/compose/.env.example` (new) — the insecure dev defaults + a loud\n  \"development only / supply real secrets in production\" header.\n- `make infra-up` / `make infra-down` and the CI `docker` job copy\n  `.env.example` → `infra/compose/.env` (already gitignored) so local dev and\n  `docker compose config` keep working.\n- `docs/DEPLOYMENT.md` — updated the secrets section; also dropped the stale\n  `AUTH_FAIL_CLOSED` row (removed in #92) for a `SKIP_AUTH` row, and fixed the\n  `DATABASE_URL` default.\n- While here: corrected the inaccurate \"the dev stack ships no Keycloak\" comment\n  in phase6.yaml — the bundled Keycloak exists (infra.yaml) but isn''t wired to\n  the services (no `KEYCLOAK_REALM_URL`), which is why they `SKIP_AUTH=true`.\n\nVerified: `docker compose -f docker-compose.phase6.yaml config` succeeds with\n`.env` present and fails with a clear \"required variable POSTGRES_PASSWORD is\nmissing a value\" without it.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"2ca2339b2551eb4887e48134f86d245aeeb342bf","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/urule-ai/urule/git/trees/2ca2339b2551eb4887e48134f86d245aeeb342bf"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/urule-ai/urule/git/commits/e503a8f21cfac1e8330197f59279ccf42b94f848","verification":{"payload":"tree 2ca2339b2551eb4887e48134f86d245aeeb342bf\nparent ad9704dc37390b2acf346e1cff66d3fc11b9cb32\nauthor PanoramicRum <ricardobarcar@gmail.com> 1778616300 -0600\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1778616300 -0600\n\nfix(infra): require docker-compose credentials via ${VAR:?} — no insecure defaults (#12, #46) (#94)\n\nThe compose stack shipped working default credentials baked into the YAML —\n`POSTGRES_PASSWORD: urule` (and `POSTGRES_PWD`/`KC_DB_PASSWORD` reusing it),\n`KEYCLOAK_ADMIN_PASSWORD: admin`, `GF_SECURITY_ADMIN_PASSWORD: urule`, plus the\n`postgres://urule:urule@...` DSNs in every service''s `DATABASE_URL` and the\n`PGPASSWORD` in the seed jobs. Anyone deploying the compose as-is got known\ncreds.\n\nNow the credentials are required env vars (`${POSTGRES_PASSWORD:?}`,\n`${KEYCLOAK_ADMIN_PASSWORD:?}`, `${GRAFANA_ADMIN_PASSWORD:?}`) — a service\nrefuses to start when its credential is missing; no insecure value lives in the\nYAML. (Usernames / DB names stay literal — not secrets.)\n\n- `infra/compose/.env.example` (new) — the insecure dev defaults + a loud\n  \"development only / supply real secrets in production\" header.\n- `make infra-up` / `make infra-down` and the CI `docker` job copy\n  `.env.example` → `infra/compose/.env` (already gitignored) so local dev and\n  `docker compose config` keep working.\n- `docs/DEPLOYMENT.md` — updated the secrets section; also dropped the stale\n  `AUTH_FAIL_CLOSED` row (removed in #92) for a `SKIP_AUTH` row, and fixed the\n  `DATABASE_URL` default.\n- While here: corrected the inaccurate \"the dev stack ships no Keycloak\" comment\n  in phase6.yaml — the bundled Keycloak exists (infra.yaml) but isn''t wired to\n  the services (no `KEYCLOAK_REALM_URL`), which is why they `SKIP_AUTH=true`.\n\nVerified: `docker compose -f docker-compose.phase6.yaml config` succeeds with\n`.env` present and fails with a clear \"required variable POSTGRES_PASSWORD is\nmissing a value\" without it.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqA4fsCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAb94QAE3iQguSK2zDc/pzmjC0cqfx\nDGabKuPwu5w5DpxSdtozWlWer8JPc1ZhS2YyuxibgcISVjVjfsUG637JgNnZXfpO\nuJHenoXsK9pfKGO6bSUEp3IBHAy8PeTD8Ydidzhg5dN519ts+YvK39fiuNbLoG6p\nKqoB9DJd3J1n8xqy3xuymzriYE5JFl5n1PZPG8dfsH7ubrWzmkVJjBNKJMTWVqAG\nIZNrH10R/SFpeZxjPKAGfrXGGJIBACBhaarXSSte+ctR1VyYgOsJBUKclbSh4qer\nyRoVYj+y65sljDBBDAah1Euxx0+jimNvNa6JYcR6U/s8hbNW+IHjx6wf06jExsL7\nYeSblxMuJhqGoDSMivzKllLOP0z2sCcNPWycFH7e1OKa+l+wSGoWJIrFGsoXvHVX\n9WjhDqfjPxe3Rphi6/Lr7RSKqeJlxidPeuFCQULckVFRwbCrC6TdMYnubt90hjuJ\nAH/A1FpefAo18QkzN2UfN8jN8WVfjnXK5xHalUkDST7W+RvfegTJE9gXyzPhGQO4\noXJCA1GI76EXHb8y9yxuLLcvM4+E40Dj8vZWCHv97idlsBZdhzIP5BoabnVvwkLZ\nqb73H3MSx46AciOtKZgrtrbuI6fPLjdj1tXTeYuejFDxYHCNQDEJmoq1MNKSd7cI\nb1DAIs/yzhaN+UxvE05a\n=SGOx\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-05-12T20:05:00Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https