m/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/urule-ai/urule/commits/ad9704dc37390b2acf346e1cff66d3fc11b9cb32/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-12T19:02:11Z","email":"ricardobarcar@gmail.com","name":"PanoramicRum"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-12T19:02:11Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(registry): admin-gate GET /providers/:id/key — stop key exfiltration (#5) (#93)\n\nThe endpoint returns the UNMASKED LLM provider API key but only checked\nauthentication, so any authenticated user could `GET /api/v1/providers/<id>/key`\nand dump any provider''s key. Now it requires the `admin` realm role — non-admin\nand anonymous callers get 403.\n\nThe office-ui never calls this (it uses the masked `GET /:id`); the orchestrator\nadapters are the only legitimate callers and run with an elevated identity (in\nthe dev compose, registry runs SKIP_AUTH=true → mock admin, so chat keeps\nworking). TODO(#4): swap the admin gate for proper service-to-service auth once\nthe authz layer can scope provider access to the caller''s workspace.\n\nTests (services/registry/tests/unit/provider-key.test.ts): 403 for a non-admin\nuser, 403 for an anonymous request, 200 + unmasked key for an admin, 404 for an\nunknown provider. Registry suite: 9 files / 62 tests green.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"2592b7b67041150f6951cd2a01acae926a257fa5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/urule-ai/urule/git/trees/2592b7b67041150f6951cd2a01acae926a257fa5"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/urule-ai/urule/git/commits/ad9704dc37390b2acf346e1cff66d3fc11b9cb32","verification":{"payload":"tree 2592b7b67041150f6951cd2a01acae926a257fa5\nparent 896e761369fe3819d3861cdb30885e92468ccbdb\nauthor PanoramicRum <ricardobarcar@gmail.com> 1778612531 -0600\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1778612531 -0600\n\nfix(registry): admin-gate GET /providers/:id/key — stop key exfiltration (#5) (#93)\n\nThe endpoint returns the UNMASKED LLM provider API key but only checked\nauthentication, so any authenticated user could `GET /api/v1/providers/<id>/key`\nand dump any provider''s key. Now it requires the `admin` realm role — non-admin\nand anonymous callers get 403.\n\nThe office-ui never calls this (it uses the masked `GET /:id`); the orchestrator\nadapters are the only legitimate callers and run with an elevated identity (in\nthe dev compose, registry runs SKIP_AUTH=true → mock admin, so chat keeps\nworking). TODO(#4): swap the admin gate for proper service-to-service auth once\nthe authz layer can scope provider access to the caller''s workspace.\n\nTests (services/registry/tests/unit/provider-key.test.ts): 403 for a non-admin\nuser, 403 for an anonymous request, 200 + unmasked key for an admin, 404 for an\nunknown provider. Registry suite: 9 files / 62 tests green.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqA3kzCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAYsAQACWTKkMdd7IlrIgVIfJ5oDlv\nFMxfG+7akQAg/HDJija9l60YW6od04q8fR3NosJv26Mzx89wQfg5JK5bcWMLBlmp\nArDzm+k/LA1nYhfRkb9RNcqLuz/7ovX9U5MRZ7uDoU9BNCaNv9UVjqXegM+mHjPr\nR88K6qqbS6fd1cjApYF/SE9mnF/WZkqNG3hWHYE/gqHJcB3TzaphnhG8hufleogV\nHFEDsC0HonGDJ+GrQ4sb1/Yq6H0y8VD+fUduCTYErsDP4b8aF72eLE3ctdMFIDkT\nims3Q7hSdoubDLdsbDpgvWjAeVKa9n/gxvswuE/VZMsaIRMSPNegqfg3zEQIOR8W\nPZawlQ8W6LrO3XxiLoRXXN8l8XEIOXWyQNLBjhl15jnXS0y/hIbUJbu4MrBPg9as\nCQ3lrqA4iRtZC/GtZSKGPPx/2gwDLKVP1PHfTqc+5X/njfgJlr98/EEFp6Qof49S\njNpNTjpYD+kw3KP3t711JTGdcL18rtQNZZG1z8CPhtcmIEZ1LF3eKT4SK/m6vplJ\n7MEBtEKFnMPXobivtykP1NKHJQWZDR5PEJbiSZshXMjDxp0gCl32