ramicRum/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/PanoramicRum","id":6556452,"login":"PanoramicRum","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY1NTY0NTI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/urule-ai/urule/commits/896e761369fe3819d3861cdb30885e92468ccbdb/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-12T16:32:08Z","email":"ricardobarcar@gmail.com","name":"PanoramicRum"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-12T16:32:08Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(auth-middleware): fail closed on JWKS error; drop hardcoded ''account'' audience (#1, #13) (#92)\n\n#1 (C-01): when the JWKS endpoint was unreachable at startup, the plugin\nsilently fell back to authenticating EVERY request as the mock admin user\n(roles: [''admin'']) unless AUTH_FAIL_CLOSED=true was set. Now it fails closed\nunconditionally — 401 on every non-public route (/healthz and other\npublicRoutes still respond, for liveness probes). The only bypass is the\nexplicit SKIP_AUTH=true dev escape hatch. Removed the now-redundant\nfailClosed option / AUTH_FAIL_CLOSED env.\n\n#13 (H-01): the audience check accepted Keycloak''s built-in `account`\naudience alongside the configured one. Removed — extracted a testable\naudienceMatches(aud, expected) (no aud claim → ok; when present must include\nthe configured audience). Deployments should configure the Keycloak client\nwith an audience mapper so tokens carry `aud: urule-office`.\n\nRipple — the silent fail-open was load-bearing:\n- Tests that buildServer() or register the middleware without skipAuth and\n  without a reachable Keycloak relied on it. Added env: { SKIP_AUTH: ''true'' }\n  to the 6 services''/plugin''s vitest.config.ts; the auth-401 specs pin\n  skipAuth:false so they still exercise the real fail-closed path.\n- The dev compose ships no Keycloak, so all 9 backend services in\n  docker-compose.phase6.yaml now set SKIP_AUTH: ''true'' explicitly — the\n  dev-mode auth bypass is now intentional, not an accident of the fallback.\n\nVerified: typecheck 18/18, build:all 14/14, full test suite 14/14, `docker\ncompose config` valid.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"2a67f4a69b90b2e0a9420f39e0f07f89d20344c4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/urule-ai/urule/git/trees/2a67f4a69b90b2e0a9420f39e0f07f89d20344c4"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/urule-ai/urule/git/commits/896e761369fe3819d3861cdb30885e92468ccbdb","verification":{"payload":"tree 2a67f4a69b90b2e0a9420f39e0f07f89d20344c4\nparent 03fa4337c7f3a025740b0bd31a41004a4281b4ce\nauthor PanoramicRum <ricardobarcar@gmail.com> 1778603528 -0600\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1778603528 -0600\n\nfix(auth-middleware): fail closed on JWKS error; drop hardcoded ''account'' audience (#1, #13) (#92)\n\n#1 (C-01): when the JWKS endpoint was unreachable at startup, the plugin\nsilently fell back to authenticating EVERY request as the mock admin user\n(roles: [''admin'']) unless AUTH_FAIL_CLOSED=true was set. Now it fails closed\nunconditionally — 401 on every non-public route (/healthz and other\npublicRoutes still respond, for liveness probes). The only bypass is the\nexplicit SKIP_AUTH=true dev escape hatch. Removed the now-redundant\nfailClosed option / AUTH_FAIL_CLOSED env.\n\n#13 (H-01): the audience check accepted Keycloak''s built-in `account`\naudience alongside the configured one. Removed — extracted a testable\naudienceMatches(aud, expected) (no aud claim → ok; when present must include\nthe configured audience). Deployments should configure the Keycloak client\nwith an audience mapper so tokens carry `aud: urule-office`.\n\nRipple — the silent fail-open was load-bearing:\n- Tests that buildServer() or register the middleware without skipAuth and\n  without a reachable Keycloak relied on it. Added env: { SKIP_AUTH: ''true'' }\n  to the 6 services''/plugin''s vitest.config.ts; the auth-401 specs pin\n  skipAuth:false so they still exercise the real fail-closed path.\n- The dev compose ships no Keycloak, so all 9 backend services in\n  docker-compose.phase6.yaml now set SKIP_AUTH: ''true'' explicitly — the\n  dev-mode auth bypass is now intentional, not an accident of the fallback.\n\nVerified: typecheck 18/18, build:all 14/14, full test suite 14/14, `docker\ncompose config` valid.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqA1YICRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAABY8QAFDnLebWGfUpyrU7EEHsuyDn\nA5RU4JW0axr+1uWuhnrLX9c5OBnjZ5ebgRtqaUgzltiWZjDixbCbLRsvLmnXLgJl\npQDPdKo4DjxRZtY32LNPLDGpIAMz/Py7IQIE7q8aXuu/8jfGs8rN9uINxHmMMsxm\n/IJOL247ch25bT/HQ/zDOG01MMNqbqm/m/UVcY/vqQUIeZmWtCMUfAa2qVeOv7UV\n4P/8NlYIOzS8UsSi4exZSDrHuh4Xi5j7lS/YIlKTYXaS4IhkV+s0MgfsHxgELohU\nv2qJXQ94y665cEGruk9Pt4DCDyGYdc2Bw7pyAIRkRcennIZ+5wrVCAqy2Ux8WY2H\nF68Gk/V/leZB6EpfzIVj8PLwHhc24K9/CIcLg9DZTOXci77OQ1Rlrou8n3nkzOf4\naf2rj9gMqHracje5LcodqmmMVRZnnuRWhOk8Mc6CnY9wX/THInDRgu575/c/JPtP\nS5PoLppUR92Bx4tANfLZblf1pfgvyrUTneWfsI+paB9mpPTg6XCb3FFT4np9TANL\nKC0gheNCptGsFZhYPAYHDS3elwKjbD7Ppo7leCfbE9fWMoMsq2bRZkSyF8of1Ogi\nE3JH2/71ZoSU4Vipgt5DhRr3YJOyBXhr6GXBF7mzepLNm2IGh05GcpPEgHaDml8j\nFCYraW6wDDGb4fgMZ6ZQ\n=tB9o\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-05-12T16:37:13Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/urule-ai/urule/commit/896e761369fe3819d3861cdb30885e92468ccbdb","node_id":"C_kwDORxyz5NoAKDg5NmU3NjEzNjlmZTM4MTlkMzg2MWNkYjMwODg1ZTkyNDY4Y2NiZGI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/urule-ai/urule/commit/03fa4337c7f3a025740b0bd31a41004a4281b4ce","sha":"03fa4337c7f3a025740b0bd31a41004a4281b4ce","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/urule-ai/urule/commits/03fa4337c7f3a025740b0bd31a41004a4281b4ce"}],"sha":"896e761369fe3819d3861cdb30885e92468ccbdb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/urule-ai/urule/commits/896e761369fe3819d3861cdb30885e92468ccbdb"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6556452?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/PanoramicRum","id":6556452,"login":"PanoramicRum","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY1NTY0NTI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/urule-ai/urule/commits/03fa4337c7f3a025740b0bd31a41004a4281b4ce/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-12T14:11:27Z","email":"ricardobarcar@gmail.com","name":"PanoramicRum"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-12T14:11:27Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"ci: stop swallowing CI failures + npm ci; add ROADMAP §1.7 pen-test status (#19, #42) (#91)\n\nCI was hiding its own signals (#19):\n- typecheck: `npm run typecheck:all 2>/dev/null || echo \"...\"` → `npm run typecheck:all`\n- build (test job): `npm run build:all 2>/dev/null || true` → `npm run build:all`\n- audit: `npm audit --audit-level=high || true` + `continue-on-error: true` →\n  `npm audit --audit-level=critical` (no swallow). Gates at `critical` because the\n  residual high/moderate advisories need major bumps (tracked in #88 / #89);\n  tighten to `high` once those land.\n\nAlso `npm install` → `npm ci` in all three jobs (#42 — `npm install` mutates the\nlockfile in CI; verified `npm ci` resolves cleanly against the current lockfile).\n\nROADMAP: §1 \"Security (Critical)\" predates the 2026-05-08 external pen-test, so\n\"§1.1 ✅\" reads misleadingly. Added a ⚠️ callout at the top of §1 and a new §1.7\nlisting the pen-test findings (#1–#26) with Tier 0 (done) / Tier 1 / Tier 2 status\nand the #88/#89 dependency follow-ups.\n\nVerified locally: `npm run typecheck:all` (18/18), `npm run build:all` (14/14),\n`npm audit --audit-level=critical` exits 0, `npm ci` resolves clean.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"b642857c303d8364cda7843379cca48a90b9d28f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/urule-ai/urule/git/trees/b642857c303d8364cda7843379cca48a90b9d28f"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/urule-ai/urule/git/commits/03fa4337c7f3a025740b0bd31a41004a4281b4ce","verification":{"payload":"tree b642857c303d8364cda7843379cca48a90b9d28f\nparent 515dd2adbac027213cc23bdc3dc8b5a2166b7b4e\nauthor PanoramicRum <ricardobarcar@gmail.com> 1778595087 -0600\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1778595087 -0600\n\nci: stop swallowing CI failures + npm ci; add ROADMAP §1.7 pen-test status (#19, #42) (#91)\n\nCI was hiding its own signals (#19):\n- typecheck: `npm run typecheck:all 2>/dev/null || echo \"...\"` → `npm run typecheck:all`\n- build (test job): `npm run build:all 2>/dev/null || true` → `npm run build:all`\n- audit: `npm audit --audit-level=high || true` + `continue-on-error: true` →\n  `npm audit --audit-level=critical` (no swallow). Gates at `critical` because the\n  residual high/moderate advisories need major bumps (tracked in #88 / #89);\n  tighten to `high` once those land.\n\nAlso `npm install` → `npm ci` in all three jobs (#42 — `npm install` mutates the\nlockfile in CI; verified `npm ci` resolves cleanly against the current lockfile).\n\nROADMAP: §1 \"Security (Critical)\" predates the 2026-05-08 external pen-test, so\n\"§1.1 ✅\" reads misleadingly. Added a ⚠️ callout at the top of §1 and a new §1.7\nlisting the pen-test findings (#1–#26) with Tier 0 (done) / Tier 1 / Tier 2 status\nand the #88/#89 dependency follow-ups.\n\nVerified locally: `npm run typecheck:all` (18/18), `npm run build:all` (14/14),\n`npm audit --audit-level=critical` exits 0, `npm ci` resolves clean.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqAzUPCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA2WsQAH7AbPYd/nus9XxWJA1YMbHb\ngd+fCTW7OUkMXBDAMUcg4lF+ywIFOQucOgtuNzEmtEZuqQzFGpVtQVuLlmQjoPGa\nzkjS9xJlNST85bSnOBd/nBnhUPigURaZIoaydRP3cX4bn9Pw00duSeHwFm2UIOg6\nJlGsK97NOhdUD/q1hkHKKw9n6YwG4JV2Ewu1dlvZPA+ajDSHWifKtaSw8FQjJVqa\nonT0lp7AF1lHB1C49LlZPFVqtFsplVjUaSKbO6Esstpw5uJRl7FdIZ0zT6enLCem\n8MdSIL7VzipJ3oe9F4OuJ4iXScurXTu1qhGgetkWzCo4/r8CzVRV96BRXS3w2SFX\nvvyHmZwixYlv9fsgZEClt8u5myOlRCARcuJwozD1uZLqgeaQMHFFtZywtgyyzOKF\n/CgEbd/DNCHneOKjucb6wExxzcRDY9xdVOvFBEJbIo4yt9uyRRJ3LsPufLW+dV7h\nZImv5exvBK4mLf9e1jWRNgeNxeuG5RH5TTblj/x2FYsJZwLS1Tiv9KReo/lpCMKv\nQTbikQlTuSdv8JjWM8VKMlrvJUpOX9nnn7GNJYfEtX9ufx2s57Evr0aVKrc8ynJJ\nDASxCbLfZD2ASSTQ+qxqHj6jUEVFcs2WMgImgN1XrBTA7+IPIZS3aWfQsZRRPRg/\nAKikYzj7YIQ1zRyZGdsW\n=/jM3\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-05-12T14:16:38Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/urule-ai/urule/commit/03fa4337c7f3a025740b0bd31a41004a4281b4ce","node_id":"C_kwDORxyz5NoAKDAzZmE0MzM3YzdmM2EwMjU3NDBiMGJkMzFhNDEwMDRhNDI4MWI0Y2U","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/urule-ai/urule/commit/515dd2adbac027213cc23bdc3dc8b5a2166b7b4e","sha":"515dd2adbac027213cc23bdc3dc8b5a2166b7b4e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/urule-ai/urule/commits/515dd2adbac027213cc23bdc3dc8b5a2166b7b4e"}],"sha":"03fa4337c7f3a025740b0bd31a41004a4281b4ce","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/urule-ai/urule/commits/03fa4337c7f3a025740b0bd31a41004a4281b4ce"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6556452?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/PanoramicRum","id":6556452,"login":"PanoramicRum","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY1NTY0NTI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/urule-ai/urule/commits/515dd2adbac027213cc23bdc3dc8b5a2166b7b4e/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-12T13:46:11Z","email":"ricardobarcar@gmail.com","name":"PanoramicRum"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-12T13:46:11Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"chore(deps): bump next 14.2.35 + @fastify/jwt 10 — clear critical CVEs (#2, #3, #22) (#90)\n\n- next 14.2.5 → 14.2.35: clears CVE-2025-29927 (middleware auth bypass,\n  CVSS 9.1, #3) plus the middleware-redirect SSRF / cache-poisoning\n  advisories; also pulls a patched bundled postcss past several moderates.\n- @fastify/jwt ^9 → ^10: pulls fast-jwt 6.2.4, clearing the critical\n  \"accepts unknown crit header extensions\" advisory (#2). The 9.x line\n  caps at fast-jwt 5.x, which is still in the vulnerable range.\n- npm audit fix: fast-uri bumped past the path-traversal / host-confusion\n  highs (non-breaking).\n\nnpm audit: 23 → 17 findings, 2 critical → 0. Residuals all sit behind\nmajor bumps and are tracked separately — #88 (office-ui → Next 15, ~13\nApp Router advisories + bundled postcss + eslint-config-next/glob) and #89\n(@opentelemetry/* sdk-node 0.55→0.217 + vitest 2→4, dev-tree). Production-\nonly audit (`npm audit --omit=dev`) is down to 5, all next / bundled postcss.\n\nVerified: full `turbo run build` green; auth-middleware 11/11 and office-ui\n18/18 unit tests pass. (The `turbo run test` parallel flake — a different\nserver-spinning package fails on each run, each passes standalone — is\npre-existing and unrelated to this change.)\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"f9788effa49dafe54f02ae641300f2140f59222b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/urule-ai/urule/git/trees/f9788effa49dafe54f02ae641300f2140f59222b"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/urule-ai/urule/git/commits/515dd2adbac027213cc23bdc3dc8b5a2166b7b4e","verification":{"payload":"tree f9788effa49dafe54f02ae641300f2140f59222b\nparent afdc27e79dd28b7861469534cda1a677fa423aa8\nauthor PanoramicRum <ricardobarcar@gmail.com> 1778593571 -0600\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1778593571 -0600\n\nchore(deps): bump next 14.2.35 + @fastify/jwt 10 — clear critical CVEs (#2, #3, #22) (#90)\n\n- next 14.2.5 → 14.2.35: clears CVE-2025-29927 (middleware auth bypass,\n  CVSS 9.1, #3) plus the middleware-redirect SSRF / cache-poisoning\n  advisories; also pulls a patched bundled postcss past several moderates.\n- @fastify/jwt ^9 → ^10: pulls fast-jwt 6.2.4, clearing the critical\n  \"accepts unknown crit header extensions\" advisory (#2). The 9.x line\n  caps at fast-jwt 5.x, which is still in the vulnerable range.\n- npm audit fix: fast-uri bumped past the path-traversal / host-confusion\n  highs (non-breaking).\n\nnpm audit: 23 → 17 findings, 2 critical → 0. Residuals all sit behind\nmajor bumps and are tracked separately — #88 (office-ui → Next 15, ~13\nApp Router advisories + bundled postcss + eslint-config-next/glob) and #89\n(@opentelemetry/* sdk-node 0.55→0.217 + vitest 2→4, dev-tree). Production-\nonly audit (`npm audit --omit=dev`) is down to 5, all next / bundled postcss.\n\nVerified: full `turbo run build` green; auth-middleware 11/11 and office-ui\n18/18 unit tests pass. (The `turbo run test` parallel flake — a different\nserver-spinning package fails on each run, each passes standalone — is\npre-existing and unrelated to this change.)\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqAy8jCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA2doQAEZ6q1JGyvUsZXrU4qycC7yJ\nWnwon7pMJYT27hIVsVVa52rEEhMF6xB+yrQB681abZTrbr0T9/pGD0hZQa5c/Fya\nR/c2q3rFSvXJd0+YdtJNzUyith/X6lXbBQOFkmg7iBrH821OP9BWhzuBpN07xKjt\nm96OBUoT3/00bm/SQthWW3Zq7O40pZfEs+UhuZjM2SG8L66nNzbaRmgbOxSPc0II\n3C5NTOpIcpX/GkoFIDW06pp+f98bi6LIbdcSbREpn/kdTGUZMP4oV0qBDYzCRn7i\n8VY3h/q6vnl3IGb/ck2DvWZfnWjXWluPkqxW/EEhSrwho8eY3dun++t0GaRxYgv+\n6ppgQ7zQF0CEGD+tU+5CcqZg/g4y9SbHYL6kX6B1BMJks8QlDCABQ9ZkRPVf5isd\nq5euO3+/tEsQW5cOQ9/6Oazc1/I6fRF37DGW1fXAmkRTGEjgQQKRb8+giswM6MrD\nEFu1/MBhkg4ZmgGFIuFzSpAeDU9N+QCbCdiaE69bbabKVlZYmJrFuTFdND3QXo2T\nbWqDSfByVr+kzmVAQY3kMoxvY6DZRw9+vHIf+L602enSn403afwlOCp6iK6LoMaO\nVY7TBY/1ZJ/xqz6jUJ8XeCDmTGAP7IXABsVBMT/CJLGcfGDnDNcSfAJ1HHhgPRgH\nK+muBjV6Wd6fhsNVK74K\n=t9KX\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-05-12T13:47:39Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/urule-ai/urule/commit/515dd2adbac027213cc23bdc3dc8b5a2166b7b4e","node_id":"C_kwDORxyz5NoAKDUxNWRkMmFkYmFjMDI3MjEzY2MyM2JkYzNkYzhiNWEyMTY2YjdiNGU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/urule-ai/urule/commit/afdc27e79dd28b7861469534cda1a677fa423aa8","sha":"afdc27e79dd28b7861469534cda1a677fa423aa8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/urule-ai/urule/commits/afdc27e79dd28b7861469534cda1a677fa423aa8"}],"sha":"515dd2adbac027213cc23bdc3dc8b5a2166b7b4e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/urule-ai/urule/commits/515dd2adbac027213cc23bdc3dc8b5a2166b7b4e"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6556452?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/PanoramicRum","id":6556452,"login":"PanoramicRum","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY1NTY0NTI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/urule-ai/urule/commits/afdc27e79dd28b7861469534cda1a677fa423aa8/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-12T06:24:19Z","email":"ricardobarcar@gmail.com","name":"PanoramicRum"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-12T06:24:19Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"docs(roadmap): add Human Todo section for the office-ui hard-nav auth-redirect bug (#87)\n\n* test(office-ui): fix onboarding provider-options spec + add ROADMAP Human Todo\n\n## onboarding.spec.ts\n\n`should display provider options` was fixme''d under #65. Root cause\n(found via a local repro): the test gated its assertion on\n`page.textContent(''body'').includes(''Provider'')`, but `textContent`\nincludes the content of inlined `<script>` tags — and the Next.js\nRSC / hydration blob on every page contains \"Provider\" (e.g.\n`QueryClientProvider`, `AuthProvider`, chunk names). So the guard\ntripped on `/login` (where unauthenticated `page.goto(''/setup'')`\nredirects to), and the follow-up visible-text assertion\n`getByText(/claude|openai|provider/i)` then found nothing.\n\nRewrite: import `test`/`expect` from `./fixtures/auth` (still exposes\nplain `page` for the other two tests in the file), use the\n`authenticatedPage` fixture for this one, navigate to `/setup` — which\nrenders the wizard''s step-0 provider selector for a real session — and\nassert the \"Select AI Model\" heading + the Claude / OpenAI provider\ncards directly. Verified locally: 3/3 stable runs.\n\n## ROADMAP.md\n\nAdd a \"## Human Todo — needs a browser / interactive session\" section\nat the top. First entry: the `page.reload()` → `/login` redirect bug\nthat blocks the remaining 2 #65 specs (`notification-center.spec.ts`\ntoast-surfaces + clear-all). AI debugging pinned the symptom\n(localStorage has `isAuthenticated: true` at the moment the layout\nredirects, so #80''s hydration gate isn''t fully closing the race) but\nthe cause needs eyes on the live page with React DevTools — the entry\nhas the repro command, what to watch for, and candidate fixes.\n\n#65 scorecard after this lands: 15/17 (5 auth + 4 notification-center\n+ 4 command-palette + 1 widgets + 1 onboarding).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* revert onboarding rewrite — same hard-nav hydration bug, only manifests in CI prod build\n\nPR #87''s onboarding rewrite (use `authenticatedPage` + goto `/setup` +\nassert the wizard heading) passed locally 3/3 against `next dev` but\nfails in CI: the \"Select AI Model\" heading times out at 15s, because\n`page.goto(''/setup'')` from `/office` (a hard navigation) hits the same\nauth-redirect-on-hydration-race as the notification-center reload\nspecs — the page redirects to `/login` before the wizard renders. The\nrace apparently only opens in the `next build` + standalone server CI\nruns, not under local `next dev`.\n\nSo this isn''t a separate fix — it''s the same root cause as the 2\nnotification reload specs. Reverted onboarding back to `test.fixme()`;\nthe ROADMAP \"Human Todo\" entry is expanded to cover all 3 specs and to\nnote that a local repro needs the production build (not `next dev`).\n\nNet effect of this PR after squash: just the ROADMAP \"Human Todo\"\nsection.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"aa276bac66fe8b6d1787f2ee210f4375639763cd","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/urule-ai/urule/git/trees/aa276bac66fe8b6d1787f2ee210f4375639763cd"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/urule-ai/urule/git/commits/afdc27e79dd28b7861469534cda1a677fa423aa8","verification":{"payload":"tree aa276bac66fe8b6d1787f2ee210f4375639763cd\nparent 27df853e58c72a9b980a46c960c7341140a046e4\nauthor PanoramicRum <ricardobarcar@gmail.com> 1778567059 -0600\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1778567059 -0600\n\ndocs(roadmap): add Human Todo section for the office-ui hard-nav auth-redirect bug (#87)\n\n* test(office-ui): fix onboarding provider-options spec + add ROADMAP Human Todo\n\n## onboarding.spec.ts\n\n`should display provider options` was fixme''d under #65. Root cause\n(found via a local repro): the test gated its assertion on\n`page.textContent(''body'').includes(''Provider'')`, but `textContent`\nincludes the content of inlined `<script>` tags — and the Next.js\nRSC / hydration blob on every page contains \"Provider\" (e.g.\n`QueryClientProvider`, `AuthProvider`, chunk names). So the guard\ntripped on `/login` (where unauthenticated `page.goto(''/setup'')`\nredirects to), and the follow-up visible-text assertion\n`getByText(/claude|openai|provider/i)` then found nothing.\n\nRewrite: import `test`/`expect` from `./fixtures/auth` (still exposes\nplain `page` for the other two tests in the file), use the\n`authenticatedPage` fixture for this one, navigate to `/setup` — which\nrenders the wizard''s step-0 provider selector for a real session — and\nassert the \"Select AI Model\" heading + the Claude / OpenAI provider\ncards directly. Verified locally: 3/3 stable runs.\n\n## ROADMAP.md\n\nAdd a \"## Human Todo — needs a browser / interactive session\" section\nat the top. First entry: the `page.reload()` → `/login` redirect bug\nthat blocks the remaining 2 #65 specs (`notification-center.spec.ts`\ntoast-surfaces + clear-all). AI debugging pinned the symptom\n(localStorage has `isAuthenticated: true` at the moment the layout\nredirects, so #80''s hydration gate isn''t fully closing the race) but\nthe cause needs eyes on the live page with React DevTools — the entry\nhas the repro command, what to watch for, and candidate fixes.\n\n#65 scorecard after this lands: 15/17 (5 auth + 4 notification-center\n+ 4 command-palette + 1 widgets + 1 onboarding).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* revert onboarding rewrite — same hard-nav hydration bug, only manifests in CI prod build\n\nPR #87''s onboarding rewrite (use `authenticatedPage` + goto `/setup` +\nassert the wizard heading) passed locally 3/3 against `next dev` but\nfails in CI: the \"Select AI Model\" heading times out at 15s, because\n`page.goto(''/setup'')` from `/office` (a hard navigation) hits the same\nauth-redirect-on-hydration-race as the notification-center reload\nspecs — the page redirects to `/login` before the wizard renders. The\nrace apparently only opens in the `next build` + standalone server CI\nruns, not under local `next dev`.\n\nSo this isn''t a separate fix — it''s the same root cause as the 2\nnotification reload specs. Reverted onboarding back to `test.fixme()`;\nthe ROADMAP \"Human Todo\" entry is expanded to cover all 3 specs and to\nnote that a local repro needs the production build (not `next dev`).\n\nNet effect of this PR after squash: just the ROADMAP \"Human Todo\"\nsection.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqAseTCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAABI8QAJHJNCtlo4aDxywtqio79fAC\nUn7T5faiK20V/OOHIrZeZfRQWVu+tYn3LvsQzdni8J+8y9+zbm+2bIqFmcJSNOVv\nqdKZpJQY8Mldv7M/QwngqN3GqnoQN+WmRdeccrdKC+PU/Ey4jj3i4ZKKWvkIUS2e\nYo7BPlv6wv5QvEppv/8XG5fjccmGZmEcb+MWIu1lSHsc0uGSk0HjlBAy1yM+m1lk\n02Aa2ZbDHO+FUand6h4XCrUd+WTdunvV8B9wlbTCrRfpArZjH/B+RSeoE+EgUlZE\ned0cZvASThjUG6PMWKS5XTVLm6xKOPyClxB+WfWJsb8p++iyRHzOOIYpxM0q9n3V\ngdd+9KyHOKLZgxaMmQWcGSIs04ZU4KQtHaWhF0fcPUdC6haLIoHfhtncYgH0LIDb\ndaQbCQaYtcVfJONbzqFn3XCYTeXktRUOgcv3ruf3qDjB8PMOUWuyzs/jtAhu1rW+\nmAcMkrz+gb1OAO9BDY5dntY9sNFcGiuYlNCt4E0GYQa10hbNz6gjB0sPx5q++BXZ\nj7rgzCz4TJ6M1XwXJ4XVjUXdzCWH+vnJOwlkLEcfvNbaat0V2FabhHEAqmz12v/t\nKkrUOJQGZM+Frsdln/t4hUbFbalErVs3/WCMTBfN+Skt2ayE/96aBgEponpSqAT3\ntSi8iLxQXJ+5pUFNDP+A\n=Y+Xw\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-05-12T06:24:19Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/urule-ai/urule/commit/afdc27e79dd28b7861469534cda1a677fa423aa8","node_id":"C_kwDORxyz5NoAKGFmZGMyN2U3OWRkMjhiNzg2MTQ2OTUzNGNkYTFhNjc3ZmE0MjNhYTg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/urule-ai/urule/commit/27df853e58c72a9b980a46c960c7341140a046e4","sha":"27df853e58c72a9b980a46c960c7341140a046e4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/urule-ai/urule/commits/27df853e58c72a9b980a46c960c7341140a046e4"}],"sha":"afdc27e79dd28b7861469534cda1a677fa423aa8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/urule-ai/urule/commits/afdc27e79dd28b7861469534cda1a677fa423aa8"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6556452?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/PanoramicRum","id":6556452,"login":"PanoramicRum","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY1NTY0NTI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/urule-ai/urule/commits/27df853e58c72a9b980a46c960c7341140a046e4/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-12T04:48:14Z","email":"ricardobarcar@gmail.com","name":"PanoramicRum"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-12T04:48:14Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"test(office-ui): rewrite widgets host-shell nav spec to use layout-stable fixture (#85)\n\nUn-fixmes `widgets.spec.ts:51` (''navigation between widget-backed pages\ndoes not lose the host shell'') with the same rewrite that fixed\nnotification-center (#83) and command-palette (#84):\n\n- Drop the redundant `page.goto(''/office'')` + `waitForTimeout(800)` —\n  the auth fixture already lands on /office and waits for the office\n  shell to commit, so `page.url()` is `/office` when the test body\n  starts.\n- After `page.goto(''/office/approvals'')` (which re-mounts the office\n  layout), wait for the persistent sidebar `<nav>` to re-commit before\n  asserting URL + nav visibility. `/office/approvals` actually commits\n  faster than `/office` since the layout''s setup-status API call is\n  skipped for non-root pathnames.\n\nTouches #65 — should bring the scorecard to 14/17. CI on this PR is\nthe verification.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"fce830e07a8841d5a7a9390732b01dbafb1b760f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/urule-ai/urule/git/trees/fce830e07a8841d5a7a9390732b01dbafb1b760f"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/urule-ai/urule/git/commits/27df853e58c72a9b980a46c960c7341140a046e4","verification":{"payload":"tree fce830e07a8841d5a7a9390732b01dbafb1b760f\nparent 0a07881ceebcfa4cd840e549d162ca13a56b8f1b\nauthor PanoramicRum <ricardobarcar@gmail.com> 1778561294 -0600\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1778561294 -0600\n\ntest(office-ui): rewrite widgets host-shell nav spec to use layout-stable fixture (#85)\n\nUn-fixmes `widgets.spec.ts:51` (''navigation between widget-backed pages\ndoes not lose the host shell'') with the same rewrite that fixed\nnotification-center (#83) and command-palette (#84):\n\n- Drop the redundant `page.goto(''/office'')` + `waitForTimeout(800)` —\n  the auth fixture already lands on /office and waits for the office\n  shell to commit, so `page.url()` is `/office` when the test body\n  starts.\n- After `page.goto(''/office/approvals'')` (which re-mounts the office\n  layout), wait for the persistent sidebar `<nav>` to re-commit before\n  asserting URL + nav visibility. `/office/approvals` actually commits\n  faster than `/office` since the layout''s setup-status API call is\n  skipped for non-root pathnames.\n\nTouches #65 — should bring the scorecard to 14/17. CI on this PR is\nthe verification.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqArEOCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAITEQABqM+Tqc0O1sNNHAcnpI+swf\nGX7D7nbMm3hnwTNy1fCTNT5RWU9K6X2Au8A1fpKjsPEpvZ09mjLOWj9JiCVysTCV\nEpQBMmP+mVkMfEc/I1XRax2dtb4arL1YUvEvo5KvOxtijEZimKNUYEfAq8fx+QVO\nwqeCM0OWQR6SgpJisJaN6RxgEvjPSGEGe65ETEVkNmVbMjRFJdIjOYOUYmTK8nM7\nmbqr3gDlB4uvC/Y6MNhpHldSyvN9bEQ30Kzns96DwLxCnngq1OFnwE471ziNK8K7\nfyhhYzIlsen8VThK1clHwm+lz9lO4v/nn+jTOAK7S+xU5t3iPHOIh9BsY+ceD/fo\ndnScnvF1a8SbjlA0Ec09OjV2kwkdVt3cVAJ5yIhcV/