/6556452?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/PanoramicRum","id":6556452,"login":"PanoramicRum","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY1NTY0NTI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/urule-ai/urule/commits/0a07881ceebcfa4cd840e549d162ca13a56b8f1b/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-12T04:28:40Z","email":"ricardobarcar@gmail.com","name":"PanoramicRum"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-12T04:28:40Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"test(office-ui): rewrite command-palette spec to use layout-stable fixture (#84)\n\nUn-fixmes the 4 command-palette specs from #65, applying the same\nrewrite that fixed notification-center in #83:\n\n- Drop the redundant `page.goto(''/office'')` + `waitForTimeout(800)` —\n  the auth fixture already lands on /office and waits for the office\n  shell to commit, so the CommandPalette''s `window` keydown listener\n  is wired by the time the test body runs.\n- Extract an `openPalette()` helper that presses Meta+K, falls back\n  to Control+K if that didn''t toggle, and asserts the palette is\n  visible. The component opens on `(e.metaKey || e.ctrlKey) && key\n  === ''k''` so either modifier works.\n\nThe `exportData` helper test (Journey 9) was already passing — left\nverbatim.\n\nTouches #65 (4 of the 8 remaining fixme''d specs). CI on this PR is\nthe verification.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"16749a838aa5df44021f55dcdb05c27e304b0ba3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/urule-ai/urule/git/trees/16749a838aa5df44021f55dcdb05c27e304b0ba3"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/urule-ai/urule/git/commits/0a07881ceebcfa4cd840e549d162ca13a56b8f1b","verification":{"payload":"tree 16749a838aa5df44021f55dcdb05c27e304b0ba3\nparent 18ea12d33913be97fc34c14a43c38075bd1e544f\nauthor PanoramicRum <ricardobarcar@gmail.com> 1778560120 -0600\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1778560120 -0600\n\ntest(office-ui): rewrite command-palette spec to use layout-stable fixture (#84)\n\nUn-fixmes the 4 command-palette specs from #65, applying the same\nrewrite that fixed notification-center in #83:\n\n- Drop the redundant `page.goto(''/office'')` + `waitForTimeout(800)` —\n  the auth fixture already lands on /office and waits for the office\n  shell to commit, so the CommandPalette''s `window` keydown listener\n  is wired by the time the test body runs.\n- Extract an `openPalette()` helper that presses Meta+K, falls back\n  to Control+K if that didn''t toggle, and asserts the palette is\n  visible. The component opens on `(e.metaKey || e.ctrlKey) && key\n  === ''k''` so either modifier works.\n\nThe `exportData` helper test (Journey 9) was already passing — left\nverbatim.\n\nTouches #65 (4 of the 8 remaining fixme''d specs). CI on this PR is\nthe verification.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqAqx4CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAACMwQAIVudITxvGZWpvGRYKw6pA4Y\nOXedGZLPVKVZ9Rxn7epa/dg+vjCIiWl1vpR+RGx+PealxhTtJVRW3RezOrWHU0wS\nFsg0Va/KGQYNorUOUZCA/3GVkzHY4uuFIDxNokgWK7uSIVQErpCnuWbrxpQXepOn\nitqXSs0v2W+ZdMNojgBicJvUuzaSW2qcqNK9aV3VHcMh2pZLlT1jzoe5+vaKTOfu\ncn2kh8KAAaPXgFfVKzIRhlvQacwzsZfQAMB99JqHO/qDbGluiKZlwePuR1iqx6fk\n5W+B9/9zxR443w6Tn0Npd0ZrhJjTYYg9/8+1YJit4sdYMz6PjwWJ/HU13pAC2UFR\ngQu+amwl5mErIxnWvopnw+APRBisW9axnGZa+LO/YPCsIT/17u5lU5HJb4q/I4q3\nJYgUPycALLcf6/x3tbQbKqzLm35hhgWfGJXg7FQhlI4MRLaz4C0gKEFgYR3ZFr9g\n6FA19Xj875WjUs7pA0xdIXBbggmfjvNgHihAQvZDJDZJ/qFES4+XQPLnygs6UA/U\n7LOmHzutHawsWyTQ0VtEr10bAdxLo0R+cDDTg0qOpeJtQBeiC2e/s9mLYlPYiFfY\n+k8kvVQEH6kYMAw0VsipeGH4wN1Nf+do1LVqxqObKg+/S9EXEV90iLvCQb5M+t81\nXr1DIt+alyGvZEdo7JgE\n=vuZi\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-05-12T04:28:40Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/urule-ai/urule/commit/0a07881ceebcfa4cd840e549d162ca13a56b8f1b","node_id":"C_kwDORxyz5NoAKDBhMDc4ODFjZWViY2ZhNGNkODQwZTU0OWQxNjJjYTEzYTU2YjhmMWI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/urule-ai/urule/commit/18ea12d33913be97fc34c14a43c38075bd1e544f","sha":"18ea12d33913be97fc34c14a43c38075bd1e544f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/urule-ai/urule/commits/18ea12d33913be97fc34c14a43c38075bd1e544f"}],"sha":"0a07881ceebcfa4cd840e549d162ca13a56b8f1b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/urule-ai/urule/commits/0a07881ceebcfa4cd840e549d162ca13a56b8f1b"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6556452?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/PanoramicRum","id":6556452,"login":"PanoramicRum","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY1NTY0NTI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/urule-ai/urule/commits/18ea12d33913be97fc34c14a43c38075bd1e544f/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-12T04:03:35Z","email":"ricardobarcar@gmail.com","name":"PanoramicRum"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-12T04:03:35Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"test(office-ui): rewrite notification-center spec to wait on layout-stable (#83)\n\n* test(office-ui): rewrite notification-center spec to wait on layout-stable\n\nUn-fixmes the 6 notification-center specs from #65 with a rewrite that\nremoves the timing assumptions that were breaking them in CI.\n\nWhat changed:\n- Drop the redundant `page.goto(''/office'')` from each test — the auth\n  fixture already lands on /office and (post-#82) waits for the office\n  shell to commit via `data-testid=\"dashboard-stats\"`, so the bell is\n  already in the DOM by the time the test body runs.\n- Replace `await page.waitForTimeout(800)` with the bell visibility\n  assertion itself (`expect(...).toBeVisible()`), which Playwright\n  auto-retries. No fixed sleeps.\n- For the two tests that need to seed `localStorage` and reload, the\n  reload restarts the hydration → setup-status chain, so they re-wait\n  on `getByTestId(''notification-bell'').toBeVisible({ timeout: 15000 })`\n  before interacting.\n- The \"empty state\" test no longer clears `urule-notification-center`\n  — Playwright gives each test a fresh browser context, so the store\n  starts empty already.\n\nTouches #65 (6 of the 12 remaining fixme''d specs). CI on this PR is\nthe verification; the bell-as-layout-marker pattern mirrors what\ndashboard.spec.ts does with the stat grid.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* test(office-ui): wait for layout marker after reload in notification specs\n\nCI on the previous commit showed 4/6 notification-center specs pass,\nbut the 2 reload-using ones (toast surfaces / clear all) failed:\nPlaywright resolves the bell element but reports it \"not visible,\nenabled and stable\" mid-render — the office shell is still settling\nafter the hard reload.\n\nWait for `data-testid=\"dashboard-stats\"` (the layout-stable marker)\nafter each reload before clicking the bell, so the header has\nfinished committing. Mirrors how dashboard.spec.ts gates on the same\nmarker.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* test(office-ui): re-fixme the 2 reload-based notification specs\n\nCI confirms the 4 non-reload notification-center specs pass with the\nrewrite (bell present, click toggles, Escape closes, empty state).\nThe 2 that seed localStorage then `page.reload()` still fail — after\nthe hard reload the office layout never re-commits in CI (the\n`dashboard-stats` marker times out at 15s). That''s a distinct\nseeded-localStorage + hard-reload interaction, not the timing issue\nthe rewrite fixed.\n\nRe-fixme''d those 2 with a TODO(#65) note explaining the symptom.\nNet: 4 of 6 notification-center specs un-fixme''d in this PR.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"9a2691d64240c4d92a6266e713d8dc42a1baf13d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/urule-ai/urule/git/trees/9a2691d64240c4d92a6266e713d8dc42a1baf13d"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/urule-ai/urule/git/commits/18ea12d33913be97fc34c14a43c38075bd1e544f","verification":{"payload":"tree 9a2691d64240c4d92a6266e713d8dc42a1baf13d\nparent 75c4fca445f95ed983806813c4a91124540d3ea3\nauthor PanoramicRum <ricardobarcar@gmail.com> 1778558615 -0600\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1778558615 -0600\n\ntest(office-ui): rewrite notification-center spec to wait on layout-stable (#83)\n\n* test(office-ui): rewrite notification-center spec to wait on layout-stable\n\nUn-fixmes the 6 notification-center specs from #65 with a rewrite that\nremoves the timing assumptions that were breaking them in CI.\n\nWhat changed:\n- Drop the redundant `page.goto(''/office'')` from each test — the auth\n  fixture already lands on /office and (post-#82) waits for the office\n  shell to commit via `data-testid=\"dashboard-stats\"`, so the bell is\n  already in the DOM by the time the test body runs.\n- Replace `await page.waitForTimeout(800)` with the bell visibility\n  assertion itself (`expect(...).toBeVisible()`), which Playwright\n  auto-retries. No fixed sleeps.\n- For the two tests that need to seed `localStorage` and reload, the\n  reload restarts the hydration → setup-status chain, so they re-wait\n  on `getByTestId(''notification-bell'').toBeVisible({ timeout: 15000 })`\n  before interacting.\n- The \"empty state\" test no longer clears `urule-notification-center`\n  — Playwright gives each test a fresh browser context, so the store\n  starts empty already.\n\nTouches #65 (6 of the 12 remaining fixme''d specs). CI on this PR is\nthe verification; the bell-as-layout-marker pattern mirrors what\ndashboard.spec.ts does with the stat grid.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* test(office-ui): wait for layout marker after reload in notification specs\n\nCI on the previous commit showed 4/6 notification-center specs pass,\nbut the 2 reload-using ones (toast surfaces / clear all) failed:\nPlaywright resolves the bell element but reports it \"not visible,\nenabled and stable\" mid-render — the office shell is still settling\nafter the hard reload.\n\nWait for `data-testid=\"dashboard-stats\"` (the layout-stable marker)\nafter each reload before clicking the bell, so the header has\nfinished committing. Mirrors how dashboard.spec.ts gates on the same\nmarker.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* test(office-ui): re-fixme the 2 reload-based notification specs\n\nCI confirms the 4 non-reload notification-center specs pass with the\nrewrite (bell present, click toggles, Escape closes, empty state).\nThe 2 that seed localStorage then `page.reload()` still fail — after\nthe hard reload the office layout never re-commits in CI (the\n`dashboard-stats` marker times out at 15s). That''s a distinct\nseeded-localStorage + hard-reload interaction, not the timing issue\nthe rewrite fixed.\n\nRe-fixme''d those 2 with a TODO(#65) note explaining the symptom.\nNet: 4 of 6 notification-center specs un-fixme''d in this PR.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqAqaXCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAV6YQAIF953EOoH6sSRm2bGrlsIkA\n3/8IHwPZvH3mVhZ3jmrsudEeKThCoE/jsHUfYFI5w2+TDqNHdrhP2LS1dHkwTrR3\nr41PWbesNfoDBztxdkVzeLCkba//ghYbA4KPMvVWeja/nLq0e6vvkFYw6y5T7y6+\nHlJgsvh1F50WLsunO66fCaVnmUG9VWWfKJhqCUBzrlBF47V7KMGSSW/Q9BuKtWUt\nhwbYh73Mc3nBYihuBUokjML0rfB9LNAfpuFFoJ0aUdIrzMkLWC0lUaQB/POQxone\nnZan1LlTYyGaDPT3SmwMVWoTyA4czbtVW0OknPgH967PAaB+rcyEeIXRL1Y5eJ4Q\n9wH+KKiweOxmuQEqx4bQc/YP+wAijm08BuPwoq5Yx1XrGr7mw3eMUK+xgj0iKerl\nXgqFA4C07L8UkrubgaEvUNTNRJKXi4BNb/OvsRiQnT4Bgu1/62vBVS5hs+x1FhaR\nnTupdF4fyYkNYtDuPdw65jkMNZE1fnLkIWIl4Bd34zNjCPDXoKexEjrwH/o0XT6L\nF5NwL+CDammOtrTgf8IgFKRZpeKJqPQSNX5KD4XNNA7ljIBMmsjHr6MnD1h/TWOF\nWSZjsuAKaO3PQXcT76k6mJcGnhmQcLeaQdI7lZRmw5r3gubzNdIr4l+QPc5zxKPB\nCrWrfoSpIJ6zVKfiugHB\n=lUQx\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-05-12T04:03:35Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/urule-ai/urule/commit/18ea12d33913be97fc34c14a43c38075bd1e544f","node_id":"C_kwDORxyz5NoAKDE4ZWExMmQzMzkxM2JlOTdmYzM0YzE0YTQzYzM4MDc1YmQxZTU0NGY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/urule-ai/urule/commit/75c4fca445f95ed983806813c4a91124540d3ea3","sha":"75c4fca445f95ed983806813c4a91124540d3ea3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/urule-ai/urule/commits/75c4fca445f95ed983806813c4a91124540d3ea3"}],"sha":"18ea12d33913be97fc34c14a43c38075bd1e544f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/urule-ai/urule/commits/18ea12d33913be97fc34c14a43c38075bd1e544f"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6556452?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/PanoramicRum","id":6556452,"login":"PanoramicRum","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY1NTY0NTI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/urule-ai/urule/commits/75c4fca445f95ed983806813c4a91124540d3ea3/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-11T22:55:22Z","email":"ricardobarcar@gmail.com","name":"PanoramicRum"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-11T22:55:22Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"test(office-ui): wait for layout-stable in auth fixture (#82)\n\n* test(office-ui): wait for layout-stable in auth fixture, un-fixme 12 specs\n\nThe remaining 12 chromium specs from #65 all share a timing root cause:\neach test does its own `page.goto(''/office'')` followed by an 800ms\nwait, then asserts something inside the office layout (notification\nbell, command palette, navigation, etc.). In CI the office layout''s\nuseEffect chain takes longer than 800ms to settle — auth hydration\nneeds to finish, then the setup-status API call needs to time out,\nthen `setupChecked` becomes true and AppHeader / dashboard finally\nmount. So at 800ms the bell / palette / nav simply isn''t on the page\nyet, and assertions fail before the layout commits.\n\nFix in two parts:\n1. `e2e/fixtures/auth.ts` — after the demo-login URL change, wait\n   for `data-testid=\"dashboard-stats\"` to be visible (15s timeout,\n   swallowed so non-/office tests aren''t blocked). That testid landed\n   in #76 specifically as a stable layout marker; it only renders\n   once `authHydrated && isAuthenticated && setupChecked` flips true.\n2. Un-fixme the 12 specs that were waiting on this: 1 in\n   onboarding, 1 in widgets:51, 4 in command-palette, 6 in\n   notification-center.\n\nThe tests'' own `page.goto(''/office'')` + waitForTimeout(800) stays —\nthose are still needed for the tests that reload to clear\nlocalStorage state (notification-center.spec.ts:30, 48, 94). After\nthose reloads the layout commits within Playwright''s default 5s\nassertion timeout because most of the slow path (auth hydration,\nzustand persist) is already warm from the fixture.\n\nCloses #65 once CI is green.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* test(office-ui): revert un-fixme — fixture wait alone isn''t enough\n\nCI on the previous commit (\\`c15d2386\\`) showed the fixture''s wait-for-\ndashboard-stats helps the FIRST landing on /office (and didn''t regress\nany passing tests), but the 12 fixme''d specs each do their own\n\\`page.goto(''/office'')\\` AFTER the fixture, which resets the page state\nand starts the hydration + setup-status chain over. By the time the\ntest''s own 800ms wait elapses, the bell / palette / nav still isn''t on\nthe page.\n\nReverting the un-fixme on those 12 specs. The fixture improvement\nstays — it''s the right shape for future tests that don''t goto-again,\nand it''s a no-op for tests that do.\n\nReal per-spec fix for the remaining 12 needs to be either:\n- Drop the redundant \\`page.goto(''/office'')\\` from each test (the\n  fixture already lands there); OR\n- After each goto / reload, wait for the same dashboard-stats marker\n  before asserting against in-layout elements.\n\nDoing either is per-test work that''s beyond a single batch PR. The\nfixmes + TODO(#65) comments stay so the broken specs are still\ndiscoverable and tracked.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"18ed473acc64a8b89066e661452e9709409cf5cb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/urule-ai/urule/git/trees/18ed473acc64a8b89066e661452e9709409cf5cb"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/urule-ai/urule/git/commits/75c4fca445f95ed983806813c4a91124540d3ea3","verification":{"payload":"tree 18ed473acc64a8b89066e661452e9709409cf5cb\nparent 652a7e41049c924e941483fc5dbfc86db62ef785\nauthor PanoramicRum <ricardobarcar@gmail.com> 1778540122 -0600\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1778540122 -0600\n\ntest(office-ui): wait for layout-stable in auth fixture (#82)\n\n* test(office-ui): wait for layout-stable in auth fixture, un-fixme 12 specs\n\nThe remaining 12 chromium specs from #65 all share a timing root cause:\neach test does its own `page.goto(''/office'')` followed by an 800ms\nwait, then asserts something inside the office layout (notification\nbell, command palette, navigation, etc.). In CI the office layout''s\nuseEffect chain takes longer than 800ms to settle — auth hydration\nneeds to finish, then the setup-status API call needs to time out,\nthen `setupChecked` becomes true and AppHeader / dashboard finally\nmount. So at 800ms the bell / palette / nav simply isn''t on the page\nyet, and assertions fail before the layout commits.\n\nFix in two parts:\n1. `e2e/fixtures/auth.ts` — after the demo-login URL change, wait\n   for `data-testid=\"dashboard-stats\"` to be visible (15s timeout,\n   swallowed so non-/office tests aren''t blocked). That testid landed\n   in #76 specifically as a stable layout marker; it only renders\n   once `authHydrated && isAuthenticated && setupChecked` flips true.\n2. Un-fixme the 12 specs that were waiting on this: 1 in\n   onboarding, 1 in widgets:51, 4 in command-palette, 6 in\n   notification-center.\n\nThe tests'' own `page.goto(''/office'')` + waitForTimeout(800) stays —\nthose are still needed for the tests that reload to clear\nlocalStorage state (notification-center.spec.ts:30, 48, 94). After\nthose reloads the layout commits within Playwright''s default 5s\nassertion timeout because most of the slow path (auth hydration,\nzustand persist) is already warm from the fixture.\n\nCloses #65 once CI is green.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* test(office-ui): revert un-fixme — fixture wait alone isn''t enough\n\nCI on the previous commit (\\`c15d2386\\`) showed the fixture''s wait-for-\ndashboard-stats helps the FIRST landing on /office (and didn''t regress\nany passing tests), but the 12 fixme''d specs each do their own\n\\`page.goto(''/office'')\\` AFTER the fixture, which resets the page state\nand starts the hydration + setup-status chain over. By the time the\ntest''s own 800ms wait elapses, the bell / palette / nav still isn''t on\nthe page.\n\nReverting the un-fixme on those 12 specs. The fixture improvement\nstays — it''s the right shape for future tests that don''t goto-again,\nand it''s a no-op for tests that do.\n\nReal per-spec fix for the remaining 12 needs to be either:\n- Drop the redundant \\`page.goto(''/office'')\\` from each test (the\n  fixture already lands there); OR\n- After each goto / reload, wait for the same dashboard-stats marker\n  before asserting against in-layout elements.\n\nDoing either is per-test work that''s beyond a single batch PR. The\nfixmes + TODO(#65) comments stay so the broken specs are still\ndiscoverable and tracked.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqAl5aCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAI3cQAJ8Zn5RI70UIJDFBuNK99t4T\ndMi/eAyw7T6xkDzYfjKy7sljZHsG1rQlpNJrZvPdk2ZpM0akr3nehKkml/Vqo136\nBujjKkTV32gwgB6vaS35s/yInRCtrjxYvrAyoixjOjTf7uyUAwaFpTu6SooAaa9O\n/eFZuZ1qkj3MTrJtpvP+L954Jo3+Ci0nNkeYyttWf60XRkRTe7jqXFY/C7wRI1Im\nw0rJFgikzRF5DgQ8p2+MqT1OqQ83SC5q9mMkmPq1p2RNdwe7CbKT4Z0Mg9/infxe\nsEalb5n7N5kvqlLdomFQ1boOytEc0wbJwW36sUufKDu1ADAvF/6xFTBnGiKkuNkn\nK6bHbceqdR5A1ioOQfZk6i9xKgq306MdeJ5g2ZDtMiEBcbbCAQaBBmxWhHAGEbQv\n8pkE6i0tbvXROgMNnpJ++M5rfnAseJJRZBen1u7OOMxVQRKvgwQBCDvvfX4wqFLT\nWIzpXZE33qod43Mif54vuWwmgHBXLHW4AgX9wokFdcMqc8+VpT5GOW2fqDwyNGhu\n66w37pzhVCwPjSGYTYD38VcvEUDELmG+4pLZa/g2MuGKRtQZRXOb/tSm6CElfmMO\nH5klRA0r067+dWZZAQLMZ5I9KBOPmwDcBJPQEaBulIXMP/y6Ui8kBaIUuVZkxCCN\nUXTa0Hp8R+4WTRQBpdr+\n=qcuJ\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-05-11T22:55:23Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/urule-ai/urule/commit/75c4fca445f95ed983806813c4a91124540d3ea3","node_id":"C_kwDORxyz5NoAKDc1YzRmY2E0NDVmOTVlZDk4MzgwNjgxM2M0YTkxMTI0NTQwZDNlYTM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/urule-ai/urule/commit/652a7e41049c924e941483fc5dbfc86db62ef785","sha":"652a7e41049c924e941483fc5dbfc86db62ef785","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/urule-ai/urule/commits/652a7e41049c924e941483fc5dbfc86db62ef785"}],"sha":"75c4fca445f95ed983806813c4a91124540d3ea3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/urule-ai/urule/commits/75c4fca445f95ed983806813c4a91124540d3ea3"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6556452?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/PanoramicRum","id":6556452,"login":"PanoramicRum","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY1NTY0NTI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/urule-ai/urule/commits/652a7e41049c924e941483fc5dbfc86db62ef785/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-11T16:12:12Z","email":"ricardobarcar@gmail.com","name":"PanoramicRum"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-11T16:12:12Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(office-ui): gate auth-redirect effects on persist hydration (#80)\n\n* fix(office-ui): gate auth-redirect effects on persist hydration\n\n`useAuthStore` is backed by zustand-persist, which rehydrates from\nlocalStorage asynchronously after first render. The office layout\nand /setup page both read `isAuthenticated` and call `router.replace`\nin a useEffect — that effect fires once with the default\n(`isAuthenticated: false`) state before rehydration completes, races\nthe hydration update, and redirects to /login even when the user is\nin fact authenticated.\n\nIn CI this surfaces as the test failure pattern documented on #65:\ntests that do `page.goto(''/office'')` followed by an immediate URL\nassertion (`expect(initialUrl).toContain(''/office'')`) fail because the\nURL has already flipped to /login. In production it shows up as a\nbrief redirect flicker on slow devices.\n\nFix: new `useAuthHasHydrated()` hook subscribes to zustand-persist''s\n`onFinishHydration` callback and re-reads `hasHydrated()` after the\neffect runs (to handle the case where hydration finished between\ninitial state read and effect setup). The office layout and /setup\npage now gate both their useEffect bodies AND their `return null`\nguards on `authHydrated`.\n\nLocal verification:\n- `npm --workspace @urule/office-ui run typecheck` — clean\n- `cd apps/office-ui && npx next build --no-lint` — all 23 static\n  pages generate cleanly; no `ReferenceError`\n\nUnblocks the 12 remaining `test.fixme()`''d specs from #65\n(onboarding/widgets:51/command-palette/notification-center). Those\nget un-fixme''d in a follow-up PR once this lands.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(office-ui): make useAuthHasHydrated SSR-safe\n\nCI build broke with `TypeError: Cannot read properties of undefined\n(reading ''hasHydrated'')` during static gen because the zustand-persist\nAPI isn''t fully wired on the server side and the useState initializer\nwas calling it unconditionally.\n\nDefaulting to `false` when `typeof window === \"undefined\"` is correct:\non the server there''s no localStorage to rehydrate from, so the\n\"unhydrated\" path (which renders `null` in the consumer) is the right\nbehavior. The client takes over after hydration and the effect flips\nthe flag to true once persist signals completion.\n\nAlso added optional-chain guards on `useAuthStore.persist?.hasHydrated`\ninside the effect so a partially-shimmed persist API doesn''t crash\nthe effect either.\n\nLocal verification: `cd apps/office-ui && npx next build --no-lint`\ngenerates all 23 static pages cleanly.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"6d36e014d523a315158143f5778a141471e12f85","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/urule-ai/urule/git/trees/6d36e014d523a315158143f5778a141471e12f85"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/urule-ai/urule/git/commits/652a7e41049c924e941483fc5dbfc86db62ef785","verification":{"payload":"tree 6d36e014d523a315158143f5778a141471e12f85\nparent a447411a7a24ffa22d1bf85081e3462b6d47f99d\nauthor PanoramicRum <ricardobarcar@gmail.com> 1778515932 -0600\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1778515932 -0600\n\nfix(office-ui): gate auth-redirect effects on persist hydration (#80)\n\n* fix(office-ui): gate auth-redirect effects on persist hydration\n\n`useAuthStore` is backed by zustand-persist, which rehydrates from\nlocalStorage asynchronously after first render. The office layout\nand /setup page both read `isAuthenticated` and call `router.replace`\nin a useEffect — that effect fires once with the default\n(`isAuthenticated: false`) state before rehydration completes, races\nthe hydration update, and redirects to /login even when the user is\nin fact authenticated.\n\nIn CI this surfaces as the test failure pattern documented on #65:\ntests that do `page.goto(''/office'')` followed by an immediate URL\nassertion (`expect(initialUrl).toContain(''/office'')`) fail because the\nURL has already flipped to /login. In production it shows up as a\nbrief redirect flicker on slow devices.\n\nFix: new `useAuthHasHydrated()` hook subscribes to zustand-persist''s\n`onFinishHydration` callback and re-reads `hasHydrated()` after the\neffect runs (to handle the case where hydration finished between\ninitial state read and effect setup). The office layout and /setup\npage now gate both their useEffect bodies AND their `return null`\nguards on `authHydrated`.\n\nLocal verification:\n- `npm --workspace @urule/office-ui run typecheck` — clean\n- `cd apps/office-ui && npx next build --no-lint` — all 23 static\n  pages generate cleanly; no `ReferenceError`\n\nUnblocks the 12 remaining `test.fixme()`''d specs from #65\n(onboarding/widgets:51/command-palette/notification-center). Those\nget un-fixme''d in a follow-up PR once this lands.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(office-ui): make useAuthHasHydrated SSR-safe\n\nCI build broke with `TypeError: Cannot read properties of undefined\n(reading ''hasHydrated'')` during static gen because the zustand-persist\nAPI isn''t fully wired on the server side and the useState initializer\nwas calling it unconditionally.\n\nDefaulting to `false` when `typeof window === \"undefined\"` is correct:\non the server there''s no localStorage to rehydrate from, so the\n\"unhydrated\" path (which renders `null` in the consumer) is the right\nbehavior. The client takes over after hydration and the effect flips\nthe flag to true once persist signals completion.\n\nAlso added optional-chain guards on `useAuthStore.persist?.hasHydrated`\ninside the effect so a partially-shimmed persist API doesn''t crash\nthe effect either.\n\nLocal verification: `cd apps/office-ui && npx next build --no-lint`\ngenerates all 23 static pages cleanly.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqAf/cCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAALgIQAHYI6lsoTk0Et6Iz/x7BYBN0\nLQnntvH875CcRd8ltEDRconuB/QQzNLGW4S8gIO9YNIpTUKpt7z3mByTqESJR7VX\nYjWIwOfQHKI+bD4HbThmhc0e49nkg65RAqw9fQyHUuntlYMjOWsAcn6b8hfWpAq9\nt+yPOdav73ULVqQyqoOcqdAq+6J8kNS2dkxBNeHkK7AIjAx/HeLRoJtGpkjV2p7X\nfqSggPOthB3AyIbjXKNGbJ7QW478G/t6UYVhYHdO5Hl9sRfkf2N+uLbcxV4VKf/i\n6Hfyk7asZJjnckRUAg4kvoq5Rwz+tEr9HpnRgC9S4ECeBRK7iUIxRJLa2SQZLCjJ\n+ynMNvUEaCb2a1dUNZhc16TyYyXRJ2Az5uLsiyHIBvUyw4oPJL1S6B4luSqDJY8/\n9n0k/dFLiRnigwoJb1KU7MWzr36qxVqf7Ura35UUgrU/DWGG4w5jjjyQlAiQjv2q\nse5VQNvpAbj8Ndz6LgfIiFqe4Mf/G10uqT0X7xsG5mfLoLt0XsYLYjeGqHa9kbUs\n8pB5P59sCw9y62YLhQrg6ivmXI9vcJzWGeV82eRr1zXgCgDBkkF3W7sQXt1rNeAk\n8SG/6zoZNAZ1UeGA4BgXcMIzYg9r2Cz9uijswgaxSzvKHY7MouKIrYGtQNepxb7j\nXMAzWxyrN3tTFIWRjuSG\n=/Hnf\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-05-11T16:12:12Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/urule-ai/urule/commit/652a7e41049c924e941483fc5dbfc86db62ef785","node_id":"C_kwDORxyz5NoAKDY1MmE3ZTQxMDQ5YzkyNGU5NDE0ODNmYzVkYmZjODZkYjYyZWY3ODU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/urule-ai/urule/commit/a447411a7a24ffa22d1bf85081e3462b6d47f99d","sha":"a447411a7a24ffa22d1bf85081e3462b6d47f99d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/urule-ai/urule/commits/a447411a7a24ffa22d1bf85081e3462b6d47f99d"}],"sha":"652a7e41049c924e941483fc5dbfc86db62ef785","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/urule-ai/urule/commits/652a7e41049c924e941483fc5dbfc86db62ef785"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6556452?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/PanoramicRum","id":6556452,"login":"PanoramicRum","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY1NTY0NTI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/urule-ai/urule/commits/a447411a7a24ffa22d1bf85081e3462b6d47f99d/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-11T15:16:01Z","email":"ricardobarcar@gmail.com","name":"PanoramicRum"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-11T15:16:01Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"test(office-ui): fix auth.spec assertion drift — switch to semantic selectors (#79)\n\nThe 5 broken chromium auth specs from #65 were assertion drift, not\nbroken UI. Switch the selectors from fragile-placeholder + loose-text\npatterns to stable role/label selectors that match what''s actually\nrendered.\n\nRoot causes per test:\n- L5 ''should show login page'': `getByPlaceholder(/email/i)` failed\n  because the email input''s placeholder is \"name@company.ai\" (no\n  \"email\" substring). Switch to `getByLabel(/work email/i)`.\n- L18 ''should show error for invalid credentials'': same placeholder\n  issue for email + the password placeholder is \"••••••••\". Switch\n  both to `getByLabel`.\n- L62 ''should show registration page'': `getByText(/create.*workspace|\n  create.*account/i)` triggered strict-mode multi-match (the regex\n  matched the heading \"Create Account\", the submit button, and inline\n  copy). Scope to `getByRole(''heading'', { name: /create account/i })`.\n- L78 ''should show forgot password page'': `getByText(/reset/i)`\n  multi-matched the heading \"Reset your password\" + body copy (\"we''ll\n  send a reset link\"). Scope to heading.\n- L83 ''should show success after submitting email'': placeholder issue\n  + multi-match on the success view (heading \"Check your email\" + body\n  message \"reset link\"). Switch to `locator(''input[type=\"email\"]'')`\n  for the form (forgot-password''s label has no htmlFor association)\n  and `getByRole(''heading'', { name: /check your email/i })` for the\n  success assertion.\n\nThe other 5 auth specs (`should show validation errors for empty\nfields`, `should demo login successfully`, SSO redirect, `should\nvalidate password requirements`, `should navigate back to login`)\nwere already passing — left untouched.\n\nCloses 5 of 17 fixme''d specs from #65 (auth.spec.ts complete).\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"ad4dcc5c8a63238ae39aad10e68860ee86c82330","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/urule-ai/urule/git/trees/ad4dcc5c8a63238ae39aad10e68860ee86c82330"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/urule-ai/urule/git/commits/a447411a7a24ffa22d1bf85081e3462b6d47f99d","verification":{"payload":"tree ad4dcc5c8a63238ae39aad10e68860ee86c82330\nparent 9bacfbde6660c182f9e009db7bd5043a4b88c3d8\nauthor PanoramicRum <ricardobarcar@gmail.com> 1778512561 -0600\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1778512561 -0600\n\ntest(office-ui): fix auth.spec assertion drift — switch to semantic selectors (#79)\n\nThe 5 broken chromium auth specs from #65 were assertion drift, not\nbroken UI. Switch the selectors from fragile-placeholder + loose-text\npatterns to stable role/label selectors that match what''s actually\nrendered.\n\nRoot causes per test:\n- L5 ''should show login page'': `getByPlaceholder(/email/i)` failed\n  because the email input''s placeholder is \"name@company.ai\" (no\n  \"email\" substring). Switch to `getByLabel(/work email/i)`.\n- L18 ''should show error for invalid credentials'': same placeholder\n  issue for email + the password placeholder is \"••••••••\". Switch\n  both to `getByLabel`.\n- L62 ''should show registration page'': `getByText(/create.*workspace|\n  create.*account/i)` triggered strict-mode multi-match (the regex\n  matched the heading \"Create Account\", the submit button, and inline\n  copy). Scope to `getByRole(''heading'', { name: /create account/i })`.\n- L78 ''should show forgot password page'': `getByText(/reset/i)`\n  multi-matched the heading \"Reset your password\" + body copy (\"we''ll\n  send a reset link\"). Scope to heading.\n- L83 ''should show success after submitting email'': placeholder issue\n  + multi-match on the success view (heading \"Check your email\" + body\n  message \"reset link\"). Switch to `locator(''input[type=\"email\"]'')`\n  for the form (forgot-password''s label has no htmlFor association)\n  and `getByRole(''heading'', { name: /check your email/i })` for the\n  success assertion.\n\nThe other 5 auth specs (`should show validation errors for empty\nfields`, `should demo login successfully`, SSO redirect, `should\nvalidate password requirements`, `should navigate back to login`)\nwere already passing — left untouched.\n\nCloses 5 of 17 fixme''d specs from #65 (auth.spec.ts complete).\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----