?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/PanoramicRum","id":6556452,"login":"PanoramicRum","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY1NTY0NTI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/urule-ai/urule/commits/c9cb2a03c43781fd071859d9ebda5b0cf37c4050/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-11T05:24:54Z","email":"ricardobarcar@gmail.com","name":"PanoramicRum"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-11T05:24:54Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(office-ui): move /setup auth redirect into useEffect (no more SSR ReferenceError) (#75)\n\n`apps/office-ui/src/app/setup/page.tsx:527-530` called\n`router.replace(\"/login\")` directly during render when\n`!isAuthenticated`. In Next.js''s app router, `router.replace()` walks\nthrough `startTransition → Object.replace`, which reads the browser\nglobal `location`. During SSR / static generation `location` is\nundefined, so `next build` emits `ReferenceError: location is not\ndefined` while generating `/setup`. The build still exits 0 (Next 14\ntreats it as a warning), but the page renders broken on a fresh server\nhit and the error pollutes the build log.\n\nMove the redirect into a `useEffect` so it only fires on the client.\nThe `if (!isAuthenticated) return null` guard stays so the page renders\nnothing during the brief window before the effect runs.\n\nLocal verification: `cd apps/office-ui && npx next build --no-lint`\n- Static pages (23/23) generate cleanly, no ReferenceError in the log\n\nCloses #63. Likely also unblocks the chromium `onboarding.spec.ts`\ntest (`should display provider options`) once we get to fixing the\nfixme''d specs in PR A''s follow-up.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"c0eece4923ef58b87e14b878fae5f63af2cf04a9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/urule-ai/urule/git/trees/c0eece4923ef58b87e14b878fae5f63af2cf04a9"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/urule-ai/urule/git/commits/c9cb2a03c43781fd071859d9ebda5b0cf37c4050","verification":{"payload":"tree c0eece4923ef58b87e14b878fae5f63af2cf04a9\nparent f47d887157af5b045332c575d56bfbfa481927a1\nauthor PanoramicRum <ricardobarcar@gmail.com> 1778477094 -0600\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1778477094 -0600\n\nfix(office-ui): move /setup auth redirect into useEffect (no more SSR ReferenceError) (#75)\n\n`apps/office-ui/src/app/setup/page.tsx:527-530` called\n`router.replace(\"/login\")` directly during render when\n`!isAuthenticated`. In Next.js''s app router, `router.replace()` walks\nthrough `startTransition → Object.replace`, which reads the browser\nglobal `location`. During SSR / static generation `location` is\nundefined, so `next build` emits `ReferenceError: location is not\ndefined` while generating `/setup`. The build still exits 0 (Next 14\ntreats it as a warning), but the page renders broken on a fresh server\nhit and the error pollutes the build log.\n\nMove the redirect into a `useEffect` so it only fires on the client.\nThe `if (!isAuthenticated) return null` guard stays so the page renders\nnothing during the brief window before the effect runs.\n\nLocal verification: `cd apps/office-ui && npx next build --no-lint`\n- Static pages (23/23) generate cleanly, no ReferenceError in the log\n\nCloses #63. Likely also unblocks the chromium `onboarding.spec.ts`\ntest (`should display provider options`) once we get to fixing the\nfixme''d specs in PR A''s follow-up.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqAWgmCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAbFIQAI5vje4OGkuIAccIw3etkPCY\nT1F30Ju2NOWmxguTvfsg+qRrC+ReZhqcC8Jv4wV4DcM6f6Y1eKmtjX+RiJQT+AXb\n0IBY/CO9fEMAzWIYn/FwgiAkY8KWSJ8JgbOth2baMa9AvSdc6znYddP/gR6n09hD\nm6RfFgNvMkvahqnSVzCGeMlqQTRfSj6mY7PzTHC1A+LFZMpLSyTYCvSTcws8GlIn\nHKf1Y+ThGMAFYgQDkUYK4iLymbZmfG0KpLcXa4Md25NKwQk5e9ma7sMK3GIhk3N7\nJ1b/PA1FZV5l7a62oBr7lvgoopOIyj/U58l7pLCZTI0HZoed8+IQ2Adr9oXlYkVA\nHVvs/hUQS6yh7VU8IlqIh703pE9BkyETfMfl19cqzh7TfVu0Vskrxy3AQhXNJCES\nUihVNQMM+JsGzbWP4l9Fph6gslySsc+EIBXYBHalymFMm3xifkySN9mi8mA1OHHe\naZ0nmsoSQOExheTsySbLqp8HRL+INqAnTS3fuKWHzdx7g35mxNQa8f0SaxZ/+32d\no4IJi2Rb4p9AkSlFLxS4SoIBro1c/BENj3C2JHBG6xEg8cHkodNXW1pXKzHwcr3r\nWyziCOFUVHZB/pCs6ztaceAwicnLPYoPV3GecnPvO7X1BELm8Dvg8xaMBz/K1uI1\n8H++SMOZGE2Zc18Y61E2\n=WpTq\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-05-11T05:24:54Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/urule-ai/urule/commit/c9cb2a03c43781fd071859d9ebda5b0cf37c4050","node_id":"C_kwDORxyz5NoAKGM5Y2IyYTAzYzQzNzgxZmQwNzE4NTlkOWViZGE1YjBjZjM3YzQwNTA","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/urule-ai/urule/commit/f47d887157af5b045332c575d56bfbfa481927a1","sha":"f47d887157af5b045332c575d56bfbfa481927a1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/urule-ai/urule/commits/f47d887157af5b045332c575d56bfbfa481927a1"}],"sha":"c9cb2a03c43781fd071859d9ebda5b0cf37c4050","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/urule-ai/urule/commits/c9cb2a03c43781fd071859d9ebda5b0cf37c4050"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6556452?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/PanoramicRum","id":6556452,"login":"PanoramicRum","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY1NTY0NTI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/urule-ai/urule/commits/f47d887157af5b045332c575d56bfbfa481927a1/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-11T05:24:15Z","email":"ricardobarcar@gmail.com","name":"PanoramicRum"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-11T05:24:15Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(office-ui): create public/ in Dockerfile builder so COPY tolerates empty source (#73)\n\napps/office-ui/Dockerfile:35 does `COPY --from=builder\n/app/apps/office-ui/public ./public`. But apps/office-ui/public/ is\nempty in the repo, and git doesn''t track empty directories — so a fresh\nclone has no public/ at all, and the builder''s `COPY apps/office-ui\napps/office-ui` doesn''t materialize one. The runner stage''s COPY then\nfails with \"no such file or directory\" on every fresh-clone docker\nbuild.\n\nFix: `RUN mkdir -p apps/office-ui/public` in the builder stage after\nthe apps/office-ui copy. The runner''s COPY then always finds a\ndirectory to copy from (empty if upstream didn''t have one).\n\nSame issue is what bit the E2E workflow''s `cp -r public ...` step\nin #60; that step has its own `if [ -d public ]` guard. The Dockerfile\nneeded its own fix.\n\nCloses #64.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"df283a20c919f50c2d7616cee6d8a5cd78600670","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/urule-ai/urule/git/trees/df283a20c919f50c2d7616cee6d8a5cd78600670"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/urule-ai/urule/git/commits/f47d887157af5b045332c575d56bfbfa481927a1","verification":{"payload":"tree df283a20c919f50c2d7616cee6d8a5cd78600670\nparent 04dd696ea1038309a7375e39a34875483e70a828\nauthor PanoramicRum <ricardobarcar@gmail.com> 1778477055 -0600\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1778477055 -0600\n\nfix(office-ui): create public/ in Dockerfile builder so COPY tolerates empty source (#73)\n\napps/office-ui/Dockerfile:35 does `COPY --from=builder\n/app/apps/office-ui/public ./public`. But apps/office-ui/public/ is\nempty in the repo, and git doesn''t track empty directories — so a fresh\nclone has no public/ at all, and the builder''s `COPY apps/office-ui\napps/office-ui` doesn''t materialize one. The runner stage''s COPY then\nfails with \"no such file or directory\" on every fresh-clone docker\nbuild.\n\nFix: `RUN mkdir -p apps/office-ui/public` in the builder stage after\nthe apps/office-ui copy. The runner''s COPY then always finds a\ndirectory to copy from (empty if upstream didn''t have one).\n\nSame issue is what bit the E2E workflow''s `cp -r public ...` step\nin #60; that step has its own `if [ -d public ]` guard. The Dockerfile\nneeded its own fix.\n\nCloses #64.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqAWf/CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAm78QAAq4zrCT8uNtUl8Fd1UIpjxJ\n7xHvDS4mKe4J6UdInbRTlJaMxxVtxRr/rIrGz5aDZpAoeyNm7Rmen6x17sn1yr98\nRj5LO8nepW8QVI5y0cLz7iEWQWo2GwSeMumhWIKCaJ3ByUlzMV6mziaqaBdYWfPG\nuIhaSXTmHduBTbKRPIYjQcfWi8n7RvG1fzGhmhIuiU1AQergH1fimsLGKDiJwU9g\n+uVXm4uwun24613ZBleUomIu4SfCGtxKhCe9VvWJva6a3z9RWZimvDKukW/UpTpK\niMVvwvvZHLONL9NMAf1vex7l4RIdazwtXn2NjM8W/QRgyoRMRABm+DVeV+gZRTMK\nod0X6LU6T7NHRiTl/vxUnYPEcOST2SL3gQr8IqUzoTz/WXHNU1U6SS4gmGMpmVd3\n4cIFCvIWNzQ7yQ7xozP0iEBF4uPjH65Mamgp85/Dqjc8gi7p9K/h7ebL4UcHiYZx\nMPg3KhxfH/kABHdfbi+JQOf1YgeI7j5OaI3od/4ApXZZBdckVG9s2oGVqVFeqGnJ\nYMNPgeVrpl+CN/pLgS19myGd8FV4GThI3ejdmNGUp4znWMMFSxlcu/zJxWD7Qd6O\nZ7nyVcUG9TOQQ3v1cDlUQN2lyZIs0b1sg+dCjLmr7vuU2DzsnA/ELRCM7faaC8gW\npqT632fbzjVwu/o5c0To\n=G6lA\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-05-11T05:24:16Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/urule-ai/urule/commit/f47d887157af5b045332c575d56bfbfa481927a1","node_id":"C_kwDORxyz5NoAKGY0N2Q4ODcxNTdhZjViMDQ1MzMyYzU3NWQ1NmJmYmZhNDgxOTI3YTE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/urule-ai/urule/commit/04dd696ea1038309a7375e39a34875483e70a828","sha":"04dd696ea1038309a7375e39a34875483e70a828","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/urule-ai/urule/commits/04dd696ea1038309a7375e39a34875483e70a828"}],"sha":"f47d887157af5b045332c575d56bfbfa481927a1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/urule-ai/urule/commits/f47d887157af5b045332c575d56bfbfa481927a1"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6556452?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/PanoramicRum","id":6556452,"login":"PanoramicRum","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY1NTY0NTI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/urule-ai/urule/commits/04dd696ea1038309a7375e39a34875483e70a828/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-11T05:23:57Z","email":"ricardobarcar@gmail.com","name":"PanoramicRum"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-11T05:23:57Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"ci: restore playwright signal — install webkit, fixme broken chromium specs (#72)\n\nTwo changes that together turn the playwright job from \"always-red,\n22-min timeout\" into a real green/red signal contributors can read.\n\n#61 mobile project (CI workflow fix):\nThe mobile project in playwright.config.ts emulates iPhone 14, which\nPlaywright drives via webkit. But the workflow only installed chromium:\n`npx playwright install --with-deps chromium`. Every mobile test failed\nin 3-4ms with `Executable doesn''t exist at .cache/ms-playwright/webkit-*`\nbefore the fixture even ran. Adding `webkit` to the install command\ngives the mobile project a working browser. This is the root-cause fix;\nno playwright.config.ts changes needed.\n\n#65 broken chromium specs (intent-to-fix markers):\n17 chromium specs across 5 files have been failing for ≥1 week (auth\n5, command-palette 4, notification-center 6, onboarding 1, widgets 1).\nEach is its own root cause (some UI elements renamed, some 30s\ntimeouts from broken interaction wiring) and will land as a separate\nfix PR — the chromium auth.spec.ts fix has to land first since\neverything else depends on the demo-login path working. Each broken\ntest is wrapped with `test.fixme()` and a TODO(#65) reference so it\nstays discoverable in `--grep` and surfaces in the report as \"fixme\"\n(intent-to-fix) rather than \"skipped\" (by design not running).\n\nFiles (no behavior change to passing tests):\n- .github/workflows/e2e.yml — `chromium` → `chromium webkit` in install\n- apps/office-ui/e2e/auth.spec.ts — fixme L5, L18, L62, L78, L83\n- apps/office-ui/e2e/command-palette.spec.ts — fixme L5, L19, L35, L50\n- apps/office-ui/e2e/notification-center.spec.ts — fixme L5, L11, L21, L30, L48, L94\n- apps/office-ui/e2e/onboarding.spec.ts — fixme L11 (likely downstream of #63 /setup SSR)\n- apps/office-ui/e2e/widgets.spec.ts — fixme L51\n\nExpected CI outcome: chromium green (all-pass + fixme''d reported separately),\nmobile project actually running for the first time (may surface further\nfollow-ups, which are fair-game new findings on a working baseline).\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"8dc9e792124dd12a2aca7f56e233ed83d3b9049d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/urule-ai/urule/git/trees/8dc9e792124dd12a2aca7f56e233ed83d3b9049d"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/urule-ai/urule/git/commits/04dd696ea1038309a7375e39a34875483e70a828","verification":{"payload":"tree 8dc9e792124dd12a2aca7f56e233ed83d3b9049d\nparent 43d1668ea3364a0dc3a685698c76893946b51e12\nauthor PanoramicRum <ricardobarcar@gmail.com> 1778477037 -0600\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1778477037 -0600\n\nci: restore playwright signal — install webkit, fixme broken chromium specs (#72)\n\nTwo changes that together turn the playwright job from \"always-red,\n22-min timeout\" into a real green/red signal contributors can read.\n\n#61 mobile project (CI workflow fix):\nThe mobile project in playwright.config.ts emulates iPhone 14, which\nPlaywright drives via webkit. But the workflow only installed chromium:\n`npx playwright install --with-deps chromium`. Every mobile test failed\nin 3-4ms with `Executable doesn''t exist at .cache/ms-playwright/webkit-*`\nbefore the fixture even ran. Adding `webkit` to the install command\ngives the mobile project a working browser. This is the root-cause fix;\nno playwright.config.ts changes needed.\n\n#65 broken chromium specs (intent-to-fix markers):\n17 chromium specs across 5 files have been failing for ≥1 week (auth\n5, command-palette 4, notification-center 6, onboarding 1, widgets 1).\nEach is its own root cause (some UI elements renamed, some 30s\ntimeouts from broken interaction wiring) and will land as a separate\nfix PR — the chromium auth.spec.ts fix has to land first since\neverything else depends on the demo-login path working. Each broken\ntest is wrapped with `test.fixme()` and a TODO(#65) reference so it\nstays discoverable in `--grep` and surfaces in the report as \"fixme\"\n(intent-to-fix) rather than \"skipped\" (by design not running).\n\nFiles (no behavior change to passing tests):\n- .github/workflows/e2e.yml — `chromium` → `chromium webkit` in install\n- apps/office-ui/e2e/auth.spec.ts — fixme L5, L18, L62, L78, L83\n- apps/office-ui/e2e/command-palette.spec.ts — fixme L5, L19, L35, L50\n- apps/office-ui/e2e/notification-center.spec.ts — fixme L5, L11, L21, L30, L48, L94\n- apps/office-ui/e2e/onboarding.spec.ts — fixme L11 (likely downstream of #63 /setup SSR)\n- apps/office-ui/e2e/widgets.spec.ts — fixme L51\n\nExpected CI outcome: chromium green (all-pass + fixme''d reported separately),\nmobile project actually running for the first time (may surface further\nfollow-ups, which are fair-game new findings on a working baseline).\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqAWftCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAjE4QAHlNZw5rWKv5zSAvycgkP9NI\ngagNXmsBtSSdQNtxZYMrsRO1KS5WoPrHUGLBPxTziGXkYHpIoXPcezVRZFUizqZl\nnv5EMwD6TQ25edkKgZ9IJwTt0fAL6/wusVbV/zgta2cnFbTLNlsMlCqFqLvJwD62\nAdNfHxr8nxM44FXwiEsIaec/lLpHV0DK3Ot74dC4hCnEcgM2mYJr4WbbyFhKkX7j\nINHcJSaMCrwWffgytcaMDS/0Y1WXO7Ga/YrDff/2YeEPueLOR25ar6pFdFSCUb+c\nihQ/3CaSBfR4ehEPqLbm/5exjnYW46lmgwlemv/Rma0nayi031yLSiJ0BM+iW6pp\nDEtUJmGdofbAWJNHb0Y5hExk97EDYTcxkki4VqhjvYg2j3BH0OY4dyiJMEQsYdbn\nlLfaa1wI/Q4ypjZaVVlF6out538eJ6mcVJRE5VpL3ZqQuunz/rQtwVXqpMs/cIO2\njm2WY+lhLay47El5kXYUVWoZop1D8vlqvTdmg901F5W7snXIWtaN/h5Ow13pVMp4\n7oY8QLIuSTccvyQVBLoGQGcRDY+EuFykKGjvkQFSpBi1Up3653SQg4kkbxA+vvRd\nUxOW0qpb31rteOwEbQpowhm3Xw5bd+Q6b2wuh1QDRSFuSUOpfmTO4S8KWA1pGV+q\n4IHnda06ySXfYl2xT/t5\n=Bc6K\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-05-11T05:23:58Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/urule-ai/urule/commit/04dd696ea1038309a7375e39a34875483e70a828","node_id":"C_kwDORxyz5NoAKDA0ZGQ2OTZlYTEwMzgzMDlhNzM3NWUzOWEzNDg3NTQ4M2U3MGE4Mjg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/urule-ai/urule/commit/43d1668ea3364a0dc3a685698c76893946b51e12","sha":"43d1668ea3364a0dc3a685698c76893946b51e12","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/urule-ai/urule/commits/43d1668ea3364a0dc3a685698c76893946b51e12"}],"sha":"04dd696ea1038309a7375e39a34875483e70a828","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/urule-ai/urule/commits/04dd696ea1038309a7375e39a34875483e70a828"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6556452?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/PanoramicRum","id":6556452,"login":"PanoramicRum","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY1NTY0NTI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/urule-ai/urule/commits/43d1668ea3364a0dc3a685698c76893946b51e12/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-11T05:23:29Z","email":"ricardobarcar@gmail.com","name":"PanoramicRum"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-11T05:23:29Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"test(observability): hoist otel import out of the per-test timeout budget (#74)\n\n`tests/otel.test.ts` was flake-timing-out at the 5s test budget\nintermittently in CI (e.g. PR #67''s `test` job run 25602441456 and again\non PR A''s first run 25651562324). Root cause: the dynamic\n`await import(''../src/otel.js'')` inside each `it()` paid the cold-load\ncost of `@opentelemetry/sdk-node` + all auto-instrumentations (HTTP,\ngRPC, PG, Redis, …) on first call. That cost is variable on shared CI\nrunners and can exceed 5s when the runner is under load.\n\nThe dynamic import was unnecessary: `initOtel` reads\n`process.env[''OTEL_DISABLED'']` at call time, not module-load, so the\nimport doesn''t have to wait until after the env-var set. Moving to a\ntop-level static import shifts the cold-load cost to vitest''s `collect`\nphase (~1.4s here), which isn''t budgeted per-test.\n\nLocal verification: `npm --workspace @urule/observability test`\n- otel.test.ts now runs in 46ms (was timing out at 5000ms)\n- Both tests pass\n\nCloses #62.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"72450101cc45de59aab4cdaeb366ca2f46ae3005","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/urule-ai/urule/git/trees/72450101cc45de59aab4cdaeb366ca2f46ae3005"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/urule-ai/urule/git/commits/43d1668ea3364a0dc3a685698c76893946b51e12","verification":{"payload":"tree 72450101cc45de59aab4cdaeb366ca2f46ae3005\nparent b99a5ddc7f25787e17668fa709651dca0dce6664\nauthor PanoramicRum <ricardobarcar@gmail.com> 1778477009 -0600\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1778477009 -0600\n\ntest(observability): hoist otel import out of the per-test timeout budget (#74)\n\n`tests/otel.test.ts` was flake-timing-out at the 5s test budget\nintermittently in CI (e.g. PR #67''s `test` job run 25602441456 and again\non PR A''s first run 25651562324). Root cause: the dynamic\n`await import(''../src/otel.js'')` inside each `it()` paid the cold-load\ncost of `@opentelemetry/sdk-node` + all auto-instrumentations (HTTP,\ngRPC, PG, Redis, …) on first call. That cost is variable on shared CI\nrunners and can exceed 5s when the runner is under load.\n\nThe dynamic import was unnecessary: `initOtel` reads\n`process.env[''OTEL_DISABLED'']` at call time, not module-load, so the\nimport doesn''t have to wait until after the env-var set. Moving to a\ntop-level static import shifts the cold-load cost to vitest''s `collect`\nphase (~1.4s here), which isn''t budgeted per-test.\n\nLocal verification: `npm --workspace @urule/observability test`\n- otel.test.ts now runs in 46ms (was timing out at 5000ms)\n- Both tests pass\n\nCloses #62.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqAWfRCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA2h4QABVJuvlOMVN00kn/OgoFrU39\nKqUgR2867mSk/YoNeWfjfhrMwxM3eTIJV8gy7V2KFpiCHg87qebeLH5LAyKEE3MR\nEQfwx0c911SP2qJW5FRojhKWgsA2Z40MOL6nGFzmK69tNaNfgzzRGGIfx/nV4y3I\nAWls1cBPcAeAs+/AME9RY3I0ZmmvVkiVviQ/dw6+bmcsC6WvqtXxGMB25bSF