893946b51e12","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/urule-ai/urule/commits/43d1668ea3364a0dc3a685698c76893946b51e12"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6556452?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/PanoramicRum","id":6556452,"login":"PanoramicRum","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY1NTY0NTI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/urule-ai/urule/commits/b99a5ddc7f25787e17668fa709651dca0dce6664/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-11T04:50:58Z","email":"ricardobarcar@gmail.com","name":"PanoramicRum"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-11T04:50:58Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"chore(roadmap): catch up §5.5 / §5.6 / §6.2 / §6.3 + test-coverage + follow-ups (#71)\n\nReflect what actually landed across the recent PR series (#67 Zod\ntype-provider migration, #68 widget marketplace UI, #69 Sigstore\nverification, #70 cross-service test coverage) and the parallel\nwork in the standalone orchestrator-adapters monorepo. ROADMAP was\nprovisionally marked [x] for some of these during the dirty-tree\nphase; this commit replaces those entries with the longer, accurate\ndescriptions and adds the open follow-ups each effort produced.\n\n- §2.3 Phase 7 E2E (new [ ]) — Marketplace install + widget install\n  + conversation branching + agent memory CRUD + MCP server\n  registration journeys.\n- §2.3 Cross-service test coverage expansion (2026-05) (new [x]) —\n  +52 tests across registry/governance/packages/state plus the\n  first office-ui Vitest setup. Open follow-ups: office-ui Vitest\n  fan-out, mcp-gateway dispatch tests (downstream of /invoke route),\n  approvals audit-event emission + concurrent-decision tests.\n- §5.5 Per-route schema annotations — rewrite of the [x] entry to\n  cover both the route-level JSDoc + `fastify-type-provider-zod`\n  body/params/querystring upgrade actually shipped, including the\n  standalone-repo fan-out (5 standalone services). Section §5.5\n  is now closed.\n- §5.6 Widget marketplace UI — replace [ ] with the [x] entry\n  describing the cheap-path implementation (packagehub package\n  `type: ''widget''`, zustand+persist install store, boot-time\n  hydration via providers.tsx). Open follow-ups: server-side\n  `installed_widgets` table (cross-device parity), detail-page\n  CTA state machine reading from the store, publishing UI, seed\n  widget package.\n- §6.2 Orchestrator adapter additions — new [x] entry for the\n  CrewAI / AutoGen / ADK adapters that shipped as `0.1.0-spike.0`\n  workspace packages in the orchestrator-adapters monorepo. Open\n  follow-ups: real `*Client` impls (Python subprocess / sidecar),\n  GooseClient real impl, GeminiProvider + OllamaProvider in\n  `@urule/llm-providers`, opt-in LLM integration tests, compose\n  service entries for the three new adapters.\n- §6.3 Sigstore — replace my earlier [x] entry from #69 with the\n  fuller description: TUF mirror env vars, identity-JSON parsing\n  rationale (issuer URLs contain `://`), schema migration column\n  widenings, test-seam dispatch, mock-based test coverage strategy,\n  and the explicit reason offline integration tests are deferred.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"31a12e0fe4e2ab4fb2e077ac2ea0f61153868031","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/urule-ai/urule/git/trees/31a12e0fe4e2ab4fb2e077ac2ea0f61153868031"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/urule-ai/urule/git/commits/b99a5ddc7f25787e17668fa709651dca0dce6664","verification":{"payload":"tree 31a12e0fe4e2ab4fb2e077ac2ea0f61153868031\nparent deae3fd968cb16fd105469b5b6fce8418fd09bad\nauthor PanoramicRum <ricardobarcar@gmail.com> 1778475058 -0600\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1778475058 -0600\n\nchore(roadmap): catch up §5.5 / §5.6 / §6.2 / §6.3 + test-coverage + follow-ups (#71)\n\nReflect what actually landed across the recent PR series (#67 Zod\ntype-provider migration, #68 widget marketplace UI, #69 Sigstore\nverification, #70 cross-service test coverage) and the parallel\nwork in the standalone orchestrator-adapters monorepo. ROADMAP was\nprovisionally marked [x] for some of these during the dirty-tree\nphase; this commit replaces those entries with the longer, accurate\ndescriptions and adds the open follow-ups each effort produced.\n\n- §2.3 Phase 7 E2E (new [ ]) — Marketplace install + widget install\n  + conversation branching + agent memory CRUD + MCP server\n  registration journeys.\n- §2.3 Cross-service test coverage expansion (2026-05) (new [x]) —\n  +52 tests across registry/governance/packages/state plus the\n  first office-ui Vitest setup. Open follow-ups: office-ui Vitest\n  fan-out, mcp-gateway dispatch tests (downstream of /invoke route),\n  approvals audit-event emission + concurrent-decision tests.\n- §5.5 Per-route schema annotations — rewrite of the [x] entry to\n  cover both the route-level JSDoc + `fastify-type-provider-zod`\n  body/params/querystring upgrade actually shipped, including the\n  standalone-repo fan-out (5 standalone services). Section §5.5\n  is now closed.\n- §5.6 Widget marketplace UI — replace [ ] with the [x] entry\n  describing the cheap-path implementation (packagehub package\n  `type: ''widget''`, zustand+persist install store, boot-time\n  hydration via providers.tsx). Open follow-ups: server-side\n  `installed_widgets` table (cross-device parity), detail-page\n  CTA state machine reading from the store, publishing UI, seed\n  widget package.\n- §6.2 Orchestrator adapter additions — new [x] entry for the\n  CrewAI / AutoGen / ADK adapters that shipped as `0.1.0-spike.0`\n  workspace packages in the orchestrator-adapters monorepo. Open\n  follow-ups: real `*Client` impls (Python subprocess / sidecar),\n  GooseClient real impl, GeminiProvider + OllamaProvider in\n  `@urule/llm-providers`, opt-in LLM integration tests, compose\n  service entries for the three new adapters.\n- §6.3 Sigstore — replace my earlier [x] entry from #69 with the\n  fuller description: TUF mirror env vars, identity-JSON parsing\n  rationale (issuer URLs contain `://`), schema migration column\n  widenings, test-seam dispatch, mock-based test coverage strategy,\n  and the explicit reason offline integration tests are deferred.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqAWAyCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAqkoQAKxzFRZQJOcVgaCVzcfvivRR\nq9wbbjqnrds2ViIDvAdrA276FQXvl26L5UV3pz7p/Xy7fhi4B/TDjmFiYul4+54X\nV1nL0hdQk6B71+z/Rr6cG2bAwkSqxptC5dPRY1LnfBWSFVbX/oJhqNMTvF5/csJc\nlStCr5Ss/MLY2qe6tWIhyPRFqvMH/TNNFu+Y06iO8uQMijV9EXzswP6SgENvJXVb\n1fja35zRQ3WVlVkMom0UhWRgQq4aAU3XbdiY2fEtP9x7ZdVr149dRcQpM4o/p2KG\nuZJDBI6nQvApX46nXiZR0mw8hhS1uJIEhcca8XnUDu1akDJS8htnoTRY14A2HSbr\nhTE7oUlnR1yZR2yeKIWjVdHfko84dgLkWMzO2ebiDfZ5UgSojjj00AvLueMWb8Pu\nshe7uvZ6058xBMaR1iu6fOseIMpKHAfUXmYLqt5MHXK7mSVXLQ47ErU4QNPyjFDu\ndeXAMcBSdgyQTqCLyitFW5ZEvgGdnCNCBwQv9Y5Y0qTFOLQpudCoGO/APNUjGt87\nEGmu1s051MZorJqmubHsEgLCOtsfhzZ2ASyUXOgT8ERo2DyB6VhpMpiQbz5yxH38\n08vv/S82XHOhCzgz5JJXSrEJEmQfmzI6o/TNfwsnB1bijeStly7SLU5CUkKMQY+Y\n7vBRa5313POnFSPH45xr\n=Yw4o\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-05-11T04:50: