ar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6556452?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/PanoramicRum","id":6556452,"login":"PanoramicRum","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY1NTY0NTI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/urule-ai/urule/commits/6de8c1184ed8bffcd3ef14175890fd7ad282dcb0/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-11T04:45:48Z","email":"ricardobarcar@gmail.com","name":"PanoramicRum"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-11T04:45:48Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(packagehub): sigstore verification path (#69)\n\nAdd an optional GitHub Sigstore OIDC signing path alongside the\nexisting Ed25519 verification, so packages published from a GitHub\nActions workflow can present a cosign-bundle signature witnessed by\nFulcio + Rekor instead of (or in addition to) a raw Ed25519 key.\n\nHow it slots in:\n- New `services/packagehub/src/services/sigstore-verifier.ts` carries\n  a `SigstoreVerifier` interface with one async `verify()` method.\n  The default implementation delegates to the upstream `sigstore` npm\n  package for the heavy lifting (TUF root resolution, Fulcio cert-chain\n  validation, Rekor inclusion proof) and adds an identity match against\n  the stored `<issuer>:<subject>` on top. A `setSigstoreVerifier()`\n  setter provides a test seam — tests swap in a stub so they don''t\n  need a TUF mirror or network access.\n- `verifyAgainstActiveKeys()` in `services/packagehub/src/services/signing.ts`\n  is now async to accommodate the upstream `sigstore` package''s\n  Promise-based API. The Ed25519 branch is still synchronous internally;\n  the wrapper just awaits the dispatch result. All 4 call sites in\n  `pubkeys.routes.ts` (add + revoke) and `versions.routes.ts` (publish\n  + verify) gain `await`.\n- The stored \"pubkey\" for a Sigstore-signed package is the expected\n  Sigstore identity in JSON (`{\"issuer\": \"...\", \"subject\": \"...\"}`),\n  not a base64 raw key. The \"signature\" is a base64 cosign bundle\n  (publishers generate with `cosign sign-blob --bundle`). Schema\n  migration 0005_sigstore_columns.sql widens `publisher_pubkey` /\n  `pubkey` / `signature` from `varchar` to `text` because cosign\n  bundles run several KB. Non-breaking: existing Ed25519 base64\n  strings fit in `text`.\n- Drizzle schema docstrings on `packages.ts`, `package-pubkeys.ts`,\n  and `versions.ts` document the Sigstore identity format and call\n  out the `pubkey_kind` discriminator (`ed25519` vs `sigstore-oidc`).\n\nROADMAP §6.3''s Sigstore line moves from [ ] to [x] with the\n\"offline integration test\" left as a [ ] follow-up — today''s tests\nmock the verifier, so CI doesn''t exercise the real upstream\nverification path. Adding a cosign-bundle fixture + local TUF cache\nis the natural next step.\n\nTested locally:\n- `npm --workspace @urule/packagehub run typecheck` clean\n- `npm --workspace @urule/packagehub test` — 97 tests pass (was 83\n  before this PR, +14 from sigstore-verifier.test.ts covering\n  identity-JSON parsing, malformed JSON, dispatch, mixed-key-type\n  packages, unknown kinds)\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"c8332fb82fd0633084ceff59e4232c4697354fbc","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/urule-ai/urule/git/trees/c8332fb82fd0633084ceff59e4232c4697354fbc"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/urule-ai/urule/git/commits/6de8c1184ed8bffcd3ef14175890fd7ad282dcb0","verification":{"payload":"tree c8332fb82fd0633084ceff59e4232c4697354fbc\nparent 0bea70688b4e36beed8e1cb63f93cb9a92c405dd\nauthor PanoramicRum <ricardobarcar@gmail.com> 1778474748 -0600\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1778474748 -0600\n\nfeat(packagehub): sigstore verification path (#69)\n\nAdd an optional GitHub Sigstore OIDC signing path alongside the\nexisting Ed25519 verification, so packages published from a GitHub\nActions workflow can present a cosign-bundle signature witnessed by\nFulcio + Rekor instead of (or in addition to) a raw Ed25519 key.\n\nHow it slots in:\n- New `services/packagehub/src/services/sigstore-verifier.ts` carries\n  a `SigstoreVerifier` interface with one async `verify()` method.\n  The default implementation delegates to the upstream `sigstore` npm\n  package for the heavy lifting (TUF root resolution, Fulcio cert-chain\n  validation, Rekor inclusion proof) and adds an identity match against\n  the stored `<issuer>:<subject>` on top. A `setSigstoreVerifier()`\n  setter provides a test seam — tests swap in a stub so they don''t\n  need a TUF mirror or network access.\n- `verifyAgainstActiveKeys()` in `services/packagehub/src/services/signing.ts`\n  is now async to accommodate the upstream `sigstore` package''s\n  Promise-based API. The Ed25519 branch is still synchronous internally;\n  the wrapper just awaits the dispatch result. All 4 call sites in\n  `pubkeys.routes.ts` (add + revoke) and `versions.routes.ts` (publish\n  + verify) gain `await`.\n- The stored \"pubkey\" for a Sigstore-signed package is the expected\n  Sigstore identity in JSON (`{\"issuer\": \"...\", \"subject\": \"...\"}`),\n  not a base64 raw key. The \"signature\" is a base64 cosign bundle\n  (publishers generate with `cosign sign-blob --bundle`). Schema\n  migration 0005_sigstore_columns.sql widens `publisher_pubkey` /\n  `pubkey` / `signature` from `varchar` to `text` because cosign\n  bundles run several KB. Non-breaking: existing Ed25519 base64\n  strings fit in `text`.\n- Drizzle schema docstrings on `packages.ts`, `package-pubkeys.ts`,\n  and `versions.ts` document the Sigstore identity format and call\n  out the `pubkey_kind` discriminator (`ed25519` vs `sigstore-oidc`).\n\nROADMAP §6.3''s Sigstore line moves from [ ] to [x] with the\n\"offline integration test\" left as a [ ] follow-up — today''s tests\nmock the verifier, so CI doesn''t exercise the real upstream\nverification path. Adding a cosign-bundle fixture + local TUF cache\nis the natural next step.\n\nTested locally:\n- `npm --workspace @urule/packagehub run typecheck` clean\n- `npm --workspace @urule/packagehub test` — 97 tests pass (was 83\n  before this PR, +14 from sigstore-verifier.test.ts covering\n  identity-JSON parsing, malformed JSON, dispatch, mixed-key-type\n  packages, unknown kinds)\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqAV78CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA/iMQAJrb/IUECP9pMX17FCu7dpSl\n/UX1gZarKk9+40ojBOEXrawkt8XYMIU1iOadrK9rZJJbddXt0NNGzA7hkwlLRJkK\nOiLRDpoTg2hdtPzzeyfA/fVqoE6FUt6Oiip0x8bGPisDrBZywL4l9uBDrx3bCQNH\nRu8dcyFQZKOCt/y0/8ZbcilfqFDjowrcHmmlANDFYWDimQCqJVqhmw9d75X6OqYm\nkg1dWKethJk8GenqqeF62pDJcfNr7zPc6MWxAa/m/e5a96nUKW4SUwou4yuYVhnb\nLq5Qcw9EQJgrXPInsMflBOZg7PRUmjLUmt9Xk7OWq0yOIQUNjaQfZPwjP6iLDAzM\n3lH3XPNNSv38vEAvq0UdFCMPMNWExaSmKL/QIInwY8ahsIt7Baq1lym5ocrP5f/k\nQBeIdRPWsn0ZfW4vupAe40316yGpoqEzv/ctdzVfXGlzRtuU4Z8eeaY8bm0a01Bx\nFXCKwbZMl6+9BqU8y36nzvw5v/m4ALBU5Vt0F5CUYpUnKGhGc9x4Ka/vdkTI+WmL\n3F0YGrzjYl3qFsWYujuTUeRDvndYh5GcZebMH1cuJwWaZXQs2Tu+J0o1OtlYF1Ez\nvqNZzS4Sg0ymvpbY1X6/cjPVZtPEAnm7oFI7dMQT6swPyLbXnPZPmJmt3yrTxwF/\ngXxOOI9JVhqy/dPlIfmq\n=dASY\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-05-11T04:45:48Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/urule-ai/urule/commit/6de8c1184ed8bffcd3ef14175890fd7ad282dcb0","node_id":"C_kwDORxyz5NoAKDZkZThjMTE4NGVkOGJmZmNkM2VmMTQxNzU4OTBmZDdhZDI4MmRjYjA","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/urule-ai/urule/commit/0bea70688b4e36beed8e1cb63f93cb9a92c405dd","sha":"0bea70688b4e36beed8e1cb63f93cb9a92c405dd","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/urule-ai/urule/commits/0bea70688b4e36beed8e1cb63f93cb9a92c405dd"}],"sha":"6de8c1184ed8bffcd3ef14175890fd7ad282dcb0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/urule-ai/urule/commits/6de8c1184ed8bffcd3ef14175890fd7ad282dcb0"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6556452?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/PanoramicRum","id":6556452,"login":"PanoramicRum","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY1NTY0NTI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/urule-ai/urule/commits/0bea70688b4e36beed8e1cb63f93cb9a92c405dd/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-11T03:41:13Z","email":"ricardobarcar@gmail.com","name":"PanoramicRum"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-11T03:41:13Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(office-ui): widget marketplace browse + install (#68)\n\nAdd a frontend widget marketplace surface so users can discover, install,\nand persist third-party widgets alongside the built-in ones.\n\nCheap integration: widgets piggyback on the existing packagehub package\ntype (`type: ''widget''`) — no schema change. The marketplace UI calls the\nsame `/api/v1/packages` endpoints used for personality / skill / mcp\npackages and forks the install handler when `pkg.type === ''widget''`.\n\n- New `apps/office-ui/src/lib/marketplace-api.ts` exposes\n  `searchPackages()`, `getPackage()`, `getPackageVersions()`, plus\n  `extractWidgetManifest()` + `isValidWidgetManifest()` shape validators\n  (id / name / version / description / author / mountPoints / entryType\n  / entryUrl-required-for-external / permissions / defaultConfig). A\n  malformed package can''t poison the registry — invalid manifests\n  return null and the install path no-ops.\n- New `apps/office-ui/src/store/useInstalledWidgetsStore.ts` (zustand +\n  persist, namespace `urule-installed-widgets`, keyed by workspaceId)\n  holds installed manifests across sessions. `install()` is idempotent\n  (re-installing same id replaces the entry).\n- `apps/office-ui/src/app/providers.tsx` hydrates the in-memory\n  `widgetRegistry` from `useInstalledWidgetsStore.byWorkspace` at boot\n  so installed widgets survive a page refresh.\n- New marketplace pages under `apps/office-ui/src/app/office/marketplace/`\n  (browse list + per-package detail). Browse adds a Widget filter pill\n  alongside personality / skill / mcp_connector / design.\n- First office-ui Vitest setup: `apps/office-ui/vitest.config.ts`\n  separates unit (`src/**/*.test.ts`) from Playwright e2e\n  (`e2e/**/*.spec.ts`); `vitest`, `@vitest/ui`, and `jsdom` added as\n  devDependencies. 18 tests pass (7 in useInstalledWidgetsStore + 11 in\n  marketplace-api).\n- `docs/PACKAGES.md` documents the install convention: a widget package''s\n  `manifest.widget` field carries a `WidgetManifest` JSON.\n\nTested locally:\n- `npm --workspace @urule/office-ui run typecheck` clean\n- `npm --workspace @urule/office-ui test` — 18 passed\n\nOut of scope (tracked as ROADMAP follow-ups):\n- Server-side per-workspace `installed_widgets` table — today the\n  store is localStorage-only, so installed widgets are per-browser.\n- Detail-page CTA state machine doesn''t yet read from the store, so\n  the button stays \"INSTALL FOR FREE\" after install (re-clicking is\n  idempotent — store dedups — but the visual signal is missing).\n- Marketplace publishing flow from the office-ui side (publishers\n  push via the existing CLI/API for now).\n- Sample seed widget packages in seed-packagehub.sql.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"7d1de1ca89a89707fb6d0bb7bbe3e68306f2f3e0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/urule-ai/urule/git/trees/7d1de1ca89a89707fb6d0bb7bbe3e68306f2f3e0"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/urule-ai/urule/git/commits/0bea70688b4e36beed8e1cb63f93cb9a92c405dd","verification":{"payload":"tree 7d1de1ca89a89707fb6d0bb7bbe3e68306f2f3e0\nparent 9fd18b2ded31f576462a7fc593dbb0e967127d72\nauthor PanoramicRum <ricardobarcar@gmail.com> 1778470873 -0600\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1778470873 -0600\n\nfeat(office-ui): widget marketplace browse + install (#68)\n\nAdd a frontend widget marketplace surface so users can discover, install,\nand persist third-party widgets alongside the built-in ones.\n\nCheap integration: widgets piggyback on the existing packagehub package\ntype (`type: ''widget''`) — no schema change. The marketplace UI calls the\nsame `/api/v1/packages` endpoints used for personality / skill / mcp\npackages and forks the install handler when `pkg.type === ''widget''`.\n\n- New `apps/office-ui/src/lib/marketplace-api.ts` exposes\n  `searchPackages()`, `getPackage()`, `getPackageVersions()`, plus\n  `extractWidgetManifest()` + `isValidWidgetManifest()` shape validators\n  (id / name / version / description / author / mountPoints / entryType\n  / entryUrl-required-for-external / permissions / defaultConfig). A\n  malformed package can''t poison the registry — invalid manifests\n  return null and the install path no-ops.\n- New `apps/office-ui/src/store/useInstalledWidgetsStore.ts` (zustand +\n  persist, namespace `urule-installed-widgets`, keyed by workspaceId)\n  holds installed manifests across sessions. `install()` is idempotent\n  (re-installing same id replaces the entry).\n- `apps/office-ui/src/app/providers.tsx` hydrates the in-memory\n  `widgetRegistry` from `useInstalledWidgetsStore.byWorkspace` at boot\n  so installed widgets survive a page refresh.\n- New marketplace pages under `apps/office-ui/src/app/office/marketplace/`\n  (browse list + per-package detail). Browse adds a Widget filter pill\n  alongside personality / skill / mcp_connector / design.\n- First office-ui Vitest setup: `apps/office-ui/vitest.config.ts`\n  separates unit (`src/**/*.test.ts`) from Playwright e2e\n  (`e2e/**/*.spec.ts`); `vitest`, `@vitest/ui`, and `jsdom` added as\n  devDependencies. 18 tests pass (7 in useInstalledWidgetsStore + 11 in\n  marketplace-api).\n- `docs/PACKAGES.md` documents the install convention: a widget package''s\n  `manifest.widget` field carries a `WidgetManifest` JSON.\n\nTested locally:\n- `npm --workspace @urule/office-ui run typecheck` clean\n- `npm --workspace @urule/office-ui test` — 18 passed\n\nOut of scope (tracked as ROADMAP follow-ups):\n- Server-side per-workspace `installed_widgets` table — today the\n  store is localStorage-only, so installed widgets are per-browser.\n- Detail-page CTA state machine doesn''t yet read from the store, so\n  the button stays \"INSTALL FOR FREE\" after install (re-clicking is\n  idempotent — store dedups — but the visual signal is missing).\n- Marketplace publishing flow from the office-ui side (publishers\n  push via the existing CLI/API for now).\n- Sample seed widget packages in seed-packagehub.sql.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqAU/ZCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAPVMQAJwQi8e5EXjAKF2GqjjxZpiv\nYeG9Y61vOydJuUysqqmDFaSrl6cQhjxN6l1PXVoYEVqhL0pMWY3SoAGHi19DK8rh\ndubOjls8IIIKoJ45st5sig8oBjS8txzM3GImKjvSx/raxsh/WKoERYHXOEkFg1zQ\nDFHMCnY4610OfbJA5l7/s4u6Wf+7mOTYDE36+KeIyGbU5rAQTq9V/hu6LSdh6UcD\noG4QX7Ny7n1YdbKSRTS6cFH8tansPx9eBBkxcbL+8y4IePWT16c7emX+cOOs+7Fi\nCWDR2WFmlBowbrSx3JroeQYkcra7Vu7VMS/eRoyw5eaRSGPrEXQDwuRmKjoR2ocm\nZ6L+g9p7ABkILBo2okT6Ok4DUI0WXNYe7eQIx+0mL+U3m7R9LVePoopsXi3+ZUui\n9+Y82+PJOcX3DIx6I7xG+N8kWdwMPgf/0BovqXup21Xv4vfi0fxcFznO5lNOMf7Q\nkIOlwQCHJZ1JbPlRzEe9kIT0CvZ7ltPMCGxRfcfCx5PbR4xFtErNix9zA0k6EMFV\nsNNlU3mJKvmEEPYjW9xSm79xp/WrTfzAKLOmePKdpu+5vVFvebWbIFgmvN5RHhur\na1jGRRJnRsFSt3j5zUb0yBbJ6FHGVDt6jyvkV4N+FXWdo35uFp8KIaIxN9Cu3A2f\nWJOWdzvvF0Dr2vqgjHa6\n=27/E\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-05-11T03:41:14Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/urule-ai/urule/commit/0bea70688b4e36beed8e1cb63f93cb9a92c405dd","node_id":"C_kwDORxyz5NoAKDBiZWE3MDY4OGI0ZTM2YmVlZDhlMWNiNjNmOTNjYjlhOTJjNDA1ZGQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/urule-ai/urule/commit/9fd18b2ded31f576462a7fc593dbb0e967127d72","sha":"9fd18b2ded31f576462a7fc593dbb0e967127d72","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/urule-ai/urule/commits/9fd18b2ded31f576462a7fc593dbb0e967127d72"}],"sha":"0bea70688b4e36beed8e1cb63f93cb9a92c405dd","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/urule-ai/urule/commits/0bea70688b4e36beed8e1cb63f93cb9a92c405dd"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6556452?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/PanoramicRum","id":6556452,"login":"PanoramicRum","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY1NTY0NTI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/urule-ai/urule/commits/9fd18b2ded31f576462a7fc593dbb0e967127d72/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-09T18:25:50Z","email":"ricardobarcar@gmail.com","name":"PanoramicRum"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-09T18:25:50Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"refactor: adopt fastify-type-provider-zod across services (#67)\n\nMigrate 113 routes across 5 in-repo services (registry, packagehub,\npackages, governance, state) from manual `schema.safeParse()` validation\nto declarative `schema.body/params/querystring` powered by\n`fastify-type-provider-zod@^6`. Fastify validates request bodies at the\ntype-system level, swagger-ui surfaces real request schemas (not just\ndescriptions), and route handlers consume `request.body` directly with\nits inferred type instead of unwrapping `parsed.data` from a SafeParse\nreturn.\n\n- Each service''s `src/server.ts` now `.withTypeProvider<ZodTypeProvider>()`\n  and registers `validatorCompiler` + `serializerCompiler` +\n  `jsonSchemaTransform` for swagger.\n- Each service''s error handler (registry/packagehub/governance via\n  `middleware/error-handler.ts`; packages/state inline via\n  `setErrorHandler`) detects `hasZodFastifySchemaValidationErrors` and\n  re-emits the historical `{ error: ''Validation failed'', details }`\n  envelope, so existing API consumers + cross-service tests don''t see\n  the type-provider''s default error shape.\n- Per-service route files lift their inline schemas onto\n  `schema.body/params/querystring`. The `parsed.data` destructuring is\n  replaced by `request.body`/`request.params`/`request.query` usage.\n- `services/state` bumps `zod@^3.23` → `^4.3.6` to align with the rest\n  of the workspace and meet the type-provider''s `>= 4.1.5` peer; the\n  only Zod 4 syntax change was `z.object({}).passthrough()` → `.loose()`\n  in two widget-state schemas (and one schema reused in\n  `services/packagehub/src/routes/versions.routes.ts`).\n- `services/governance` adds `zod@^4.3.6` net-new (no Zod schemas\n  before this change).\n- Test wiring: minor `+5/+8` line additions to existing route tests\n  in registry + packagehub to register the validator/serializer compilers\n  so the new `schema.body` route definitions are exercised in unit tests.\n\nVerified: typecheck + test pass for all 5 services on this branch\n(243 tests across registry/packagehub/packages/governance/state, all\ngreen). The historical `{ error: ''Validation failed'', details }`\nresponse shape is preserved end-to-end. Sigstore-related route changes\n(async `await verifyAgainstActiveKeys()`) are deliberately deferred to\na follow-up PR — only the Zod schema migration lands here.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"fa20119bd80b60d5ab696f9960a28aca2c4adc5c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/urule-ai/urule/git/trees/fa20119bd80b60d5ab696f9960a28aca2c4adc5c"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/urule-ai/urule/git/commits/9fd18b2ded31f576462a7fc593dbb0e967127d72","verification":{"payload":"tree fa20119bd80b60d5ab696f9960a28aca2c4adc5c\nparent 759f5592a8b1fd1fbb2010288a59e957ded47819\nauthor PanoramicRum <ricardobarcar@gmail.com> 1778351150 -0600\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1778351150 -0600\n\nrefactor: adopt fastify-type-provider-zod across services (#67)\n\nMigrate 113 routes across 5 in-repo services (registry, packagehub,\npackages, governance, state) from manual `schema.safeParse()` validation\nto declarative `schema.body/params/querystring` powered by\n`fastify-type-provider-zod@^6`. Fastify validates request bodies at the\ntype-system level, swagger-ui surfaces real request schemas (not just\ndescriptions), and route handlers consume `request.body` directly with\nits inferred type instead of unwrapping `parsed.data` from a SafeParse\nreturn.\n\n- Each service''s `src/server.ts` now `.withTypeProvider<ZodTypeProvider>()`\n  and registers `validatorCompiler` + `serializerCompiler` +\n  `jsonSchemaTransform` for swagger.\n- Each service''s error handler (registry/packagehub/governance via\n  `middleware/error-handler.ts`; packages/state inline via\n  `setErrorHandler`) detects `hasZodFastifySchemaValidationErrors` and\n  re-emits the historical `{ error: ''Validation failed'', details }`\n  envelope, so existing API consumers + cross-service tests don''t see\n  the type-provider''s default error shape.\n- Per-service route files lift their inline schemas onto\n  `schema.body/params/querystring`. The `parsed.data` destructuring is\n  replaced by `request.body`/`request.params`/`request.query` usage.\n- `services/state` bumps `zod@^3.23` → `^4.3.6` to align with the rest\n  of the workspace and meet the type-provider''s `>= 4.1.5` peer; the\n  only Zod 4 syntax change was `z.object({}).passthrough()` → `.loose()`\n  in two widget-state schemas (and one schema reused in\n  `services/packagehub/src/routes/versions.routes.ts`).\n- `services/governance` adds `zod@^4.3.6` net-new (no Zod schemas\n  before this change).\n- Test wiring: minor `+5/+8` line additions to existing route tests\n  in registry + packagehub to register the validator/serializer compilers\n  so the new `schema.body` route definitions are exercised in unit tests.\n\nVerified: typecheck + test pass for all 5 services on this branch\n(243 tests across registry/packagehub/packages/governance/state, all\ngreen). The historical `{ error: ''Validation failed'', details }`\nresponse shape is preserved end-to-end. Sigstore-related route changes\n(async `await verifyAgainstActiveKeys()`) are deliberately deferred to\na follow-up PR — only the Zod schema migration lands here.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJp/3wuCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA69kQABDIUxji/y3dYAYSAg5un8Pl\nd/BJOa3vTYCeFz8JMW/7GAlKb1nAH9E8p5oxrjNzZ9GQvV7e92VnnsIkacvg48Lf\nd23No4KzMpxGTCmiJRavtNO5l+BWz7/9/7Z+0u+Uy5PvLurRkTeEe3lmC5Fcl4hn\nsXeJhtsqm1/Xf+RwZ1F9OrP14N4aWkdi+IXnjfp08yR7ecrFO8X8Sbaq8X9pzCn9\nQO4pMBB0OncwhB/IuEUQbCjMYV+rWzv42CD28g6hJxOflpze8ExU4qpNqyovhQ6N\nNguoeGX04rWktqEosp7qk3B/QFX8ZYTgo4gHly5Gs0GCehLKNr4ftXuGlbWF/7og\nhrhGUl/XkMyGkTDSxrtd90GHJUBn/eg9z/DX3BeL1Zg9+VHZbSxizAUlvM3XzGIq\n45THJ3k5tzsFbM8u1pYFnoKgMDedIL+cmYxD5FBCGgWfx0EObGKt6ofj2Rm4A9M7\nt9baX61meRneYNUiqQhc4C3INh5tOigb9cTYjwjfibSkrNs/mhnf7ol9ZbXJJ+j0\n0hEKUrFm3uLAoEmE/K2qWeX1qS3Hxf16ShKIG5YxDif+X/xUZONFxU/tbBBSi2ZB\n9JCiTMjyXnAKTAg4i4ajYIuHEk/E49X+434/+RiZfTaOINgA9VmINKi2Fi7XnbMc\njIVsIBC95Ro/nnW3cM+D\n=cmNj\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-05-09T18:25:51Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/urule-ai/urule/commit/9fd18b2ded31f576462a7fc593dbb0e967127d72","node_id":"C_kwDORxyz5NoAKDlmZDE4YjJkZWQzMWY1NzY0NjJhN2ZjNTkzZGJiMGU5NjcxMjdkNzI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/urule-ai/urule/commit/759f5592a8b1fd1fbb2010288a59e957ded47819","sha":"759f5592a8b1fd1fbb2010288a59e957ded47819","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/urule-ai/urule/commits/759f5592a8b1fd1fbb2010288a59e957ded47819"}],"sha":"9fd18b2ded31f576462a7fc593dbb0e967127d72","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/urule-ai/urule/commits/9fd18b2ded31f576462a7fc593dbb0e967127d72"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6556452?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/PanoramicRum","id":6556452,"login":"PanoramicRum","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY1NTY0NTI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/urule-ai/urule/commits/759f5592a8b1fd1fbb2010288a59e957ded47819/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-09T15:10:03Z","email":"ricardobarcar@gmail.com","name":"PanoramicRum"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-09T15:10:03Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"docs: add PR review protocol and mirror e2e CI path filter (#59)\n\nCodifies the pre-merge checks discovered during PR #55 review so future\nfork PRs don''t slip past the workflow-approval gate uncovered by CI:\n\n- CONTRIBUTING.md gains a \"Reviewing a Pull Request\" section covering\n  fork-PR workflow approval, SHA pinning across re-pushes, the required\n  green checks (playwright + ci.yml), the worktree-based local fallback,\n  and squash-merge as default.\n- \"Making Changes\" step 4 now requires contributors who touch\n  apps/office-ui/**, services/**, or infra/** to paste e2e results into\n  the PR body.\n- pull_request_template.md''s Testing checklist is reshaped to match the\n  path filter in .github/workflows/e2e.yml so the contributor checklist\n  and CI gate agree.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"e310c1f153345280b9a6b5d226b7a462e8fcbd77","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/urule-ai/urule/git/trees/e310c1f153345280b9a6b5d226b7a462e8fcbd77"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/urule-ai/urule/git/commits/759f5592a8b1fd1fbb2010288a59e957ded47819","verification":{"payload":"tree e310c1f153345280b9a6b5d226b7a462e8fcbd77\nparent 6b7cab512cd6e1906b5af7ae27ba81a8e3c2d250\nauthor PanoramicRum <ricardobarcar@gmail.com> 1778339403 -0600\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1778339403 -0500\n\ndocs: add PR review protocol and mirror e2e CI path filter (#59)\n\nCodifies the pre-merge checks discovered during PR #55 review so future\nfork PRs don''t slip past the workflow-approval gate uncovered by CI:\n\n- CONTRIBUTING.md gains a \"Reviewing a Pull Request\" section covering\n  fork-PR workflow approval, SHA pinning across re-pushes, the required\n  green checks (playwright + ci.yml), the worktree-based local fallback,\n  and squash-merge as default.\n- \"Making Changes\" step 4 now requires contributors who touch\n  apps/office-ui/**, services/**, or infra/** to paste e2e results into\n  the PR body.\n- pull_request_template.md''s Testing checklist is reshaped to match the\n  path filter in .github/workflows/e2e.yml so the contributor checklist\n  and CI gate agree.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJp/05LCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAJA8QAIC2io+dEF43TeXBNkj+7gYj\nyfK5HvjRrQqJY5ELFBqh3/ttACcZyxz8kNTO4+Ej+OdDGzGRlGeMm5x56IK0JUNy\nUxx/28DJr+I8hEnkmeaSGxRORnl6+r+wIoEJ5LiDYh+E8acOvqeyVIUjLHwnm203\nY+wgvK6sVTapg/MAYDdhNnuIahqXsbYKdo0WJnzX+4W7TEahXH6VkOnWgzpmQIQM\nwMMd777NCmM8BtUNsrpslYPdiJdtW/XNnpJb6QueqiDkrs8U8HLQav3dE/zcL6bI\nbDwA50bxLrk+KAbbY3pCYrQOxcg8uxAlA9+9KOCP30q6hEN5vt6mo9/Cx5IyxC+S\nkjZvxzNTRow3WQcblp4lEtZDYsXPWmvvmRgPLq0FJ3dBtEegb9OK7pnfxnw+ziq5\n+eyLrt3z1Lskh9Cm+OuRItQJ42ukl6IVKLMEyZs12iRr1krmHNx56YDRcYVq/HyT\ntSwoYh7ChCedO5If11IqHSoPuM6fd+Y8sO60XVudgflXpP5pYUX9cZ5R44Rr1xR2\nKHljKBNGU5BMyOPf/J8hQlwfsWC3rKbjKC5oPxXOB1GuT19/bbqiH4NTNqJvFSgu\n/joKdGelwSUwOliMJwhmoe47dSfgPg/f7Lu+Xmc02mwIQw9Rbs0HBOsXq9wAFbQg\nu3xRLiE2Co7cTm+FIrhg\n=1QFq\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-05-09T15:10:04Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/urule-ai/urule/commit/759f5592a8b1fd1fbb2010288a59e957ded47819","node_id":"C_kwDORxyz5NoAKDc1OWY1NTkyYThiMWZkMWZiYjIwMTAyODhhNTllOTU3ZGVkNDc4MTk","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/urule-ai/urule/commit/6b7cab512cd6e1906b5af7ae27ba81a8e3c2d250","sha":"6b7cab512cd6e1906b5af7ae27ba81a8e3c2d250","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/urule-ai/urule/commits/6b7cab512cd6e1906b5af7ae27ba81a8e3c2d250"}],"sha":"759f5592a8b1fd1fbb2010288a59e957ded47819","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/urule-ai/urule/commits/759f5592a8b1fd1fbb2010288a59e957ded47819"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6556452?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/PanoramicRum","id":6556452,"login":"PanoramicRum","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY1NTY0NTI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/urule-ai/urule/commits/6b7cab512cd6e1906b5af7ae27ba81a8e3c2d250/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-09T15:04:07Z","email":"ricardobarcar@gmail.com","name":"PanoramicRum"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-09T15:04:07Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"ci: launch standalone server in e2e workflow (#60)\n\n* ci: launch standalone server in e2e workflow\n\nThe Next config sets `output: \"standalone\"` because the production\nDockerfile (apps/office-ui/Dockerfile) ships only the standalone\nbundle. With that mode, `next start` prints \"Ready\" but never binds\nto a port, so `wait-on http://localhost:3000` was timing out and the\nplaywright job never actually ran (every E2E run on main has been\nred for the last week+).\n\nLaunch `.next/standalone/apps/office-ui/server.js` directly, the\nsame way the Dockerfile does. The standalone bundle excludes\n`.next/static` and `public/` (those live on a CDN in real prod), so\ncopy them into the standalone tree first. Setting HOSTNAME=0.0.0.0\nmatches Next''s standalone default and avoids any localhost-only\nbinding surprises on the runner.\n\nUnrelated build warning still present (`ReferenceError: location is\nnot defined` during static gen of /setup) — to be fixed separately;\nthe build still exits 0 and `/setup` isn''t on the e2e auth path.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* ci: trigger e2e workflow on its own changes\n\nWithout this, edits to .github/workflows/e2e.yml don''t fire the e2e\njob (the path filter only matched app/service/infra paths), so a CI\nfix can''t self-validate on the PR that introduces it. Adds the\nworkflow file itself to the path filter for both push and\npull_request triggers.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* ci: debug standalone output layout (temp)\n\n* ci: correct standalone output paths (no monorepo subtree)\n\nThe earlier attempt copied to .next/standalone/apps/office-ui/.next,\nbut Next 14 in this repo emits the standalone tree at the top of\n.next/standalone (server.js + .next/) rather than preserving the\napps/office-ui/ subtree. That happens because next.config.mjs does\nnot set outputFileTracingRoot, so Next does not detect the workspace\nroot.\n\nSame caveat applies to apps/office-ui/Dockerfile — its WORKDIR points\nat /app/apps/office-ui expecting server.js to land there. Worth a\nfollow-up; out of scope here.\n\nAlso drop the temporary debug listing step now that the layout is\nknown.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* ci: skip public/ copy when absent\n\napps/office-ui/public/ exists locally as an empty directory but git\ndoes not track empty dirs, so it is absent in CI checkouts. The cp\nwas failing with \"cannot stat ''public'': No such file or directory\".\nThe app serves favicon via the Next 14 metadata API, so an empty\npublic/ is fine.\n\napps/office-ui/Dockerfile has the same latent issue (copies public\nunconditionally) — flag for follow-up.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(office-ui): set outputFileTracingRoot for standalone in monorepo\n\nWithout outputFileTracingRoot, Next 14 in this workspace emits an\nincomplete standalone bundle: `.next/standalone/server.js` at the top,\nno node_modules/ alongside it. At start time the require-hook then\nresolves Next internals against the workspace''s hoisted\nnode_modules — and at least one file (./node-polyfill-crypto) is\nmissing there, so the server crashes before binding to a port. That\nis what was masking the E2E breakage as a \"wait-on timeout\".\n\nSetting outputFileTracingRoot to the workspace root (`../../` from\napps/office-ui/) makes Next trace and emit the standalone tree rooted\nat `.next/standalone/apps/office-ui/`, with a pruned node_modules/\nbeside it. This matches what apps/office-ui/Dockerfile already expects\n(its WORKDIR points at /app/apps/office-ui after copying standalone),\nso the production image starts working as a side benefit.\n\nThe e2e workflow''s start-server step is updated to the new layout.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* ci: re-add layout inspection (temp, debugging)\n\n* fix: nest outputFileTracingRoot under experimental for Next 14\n\nIn Next 14.2.5 the option lives at experimental.outputFileTracingRoot\n(it was promoted to top-level in Next 15). The previous commit set it\nat top level, which Next ignored with the warning:\n\n  ⚠ Unrecognized key(s) in object: ''outputFileTracingRoot''\n\nNet effect: the standalone bundle still shipped without node_modules\nand the server still crashed on missing internals. Move the option\nunder `experimental` so it actually applies. Revert the workflow\ncopy paths back to the flat .next/standalone/ layout (the option\nadds node_modules/ alongside server.js but does not introduce an\napps/office-ui/ subtree). Drop the temporary inspect step.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* ci: detect server.js path and create parent dirs (debug + adaptive)\n\n* ci: nohup+disown the server, capture and dump logs on failure\n\n* ci: probe with curl + switch wait-on to 127.0.0.1 (likely ::1 vs IPv4 issue)\n\n* ci: use TCP probe for server readiness; drop curl diagnostic\n\nThe HTTP probe was the actual blocker. The Office UI returns 307 on `/`\n(redirects unauthenticated users), and wait-on''s HTTP mode only resolves\non 2xx. A 60s timeout never resolves. Switched to a TCP probe that just\nverifies the listener is up — Playwright handles the actual page\nnavigation and any redirects.\n\nDrop the curl diagnostic step now that the cause is known. Keep the\non-failure log dump as it remains useful for any future regression.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"0fc3ba26cc6155dcce7db3119c8b943cc29a870e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/urule-ai/urule/git/trees/0fc3ba26cc6155dcce7db3119c8b943cc29a870e"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/urule-ai/urule/git/commits/6b7cab512cd6e1906b5af7ae27ba81a8e3c2d250","verification":{"payload":"tree 0fc3ba26cc6155dcce7db3119c8b943cc29a870e\nparent 0b165c675ca68232a052b038726c04e09fcbed2c\nauthor PanoramicRum <ricardobarcar@gmail.com> 1778339047 -0600\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1778339047 -0600\n\nci: launch standalone server in e2e workflow (#60)\n\n* ci: launch standalone server in e2e workflow\n\nThe Next config sets `output: \"standalone\"` because the production\nDockerfile (apps/office-ui/Dockerfile) ships only the standalone\nbundle. With that mode, `next start` prints \"Ready\" but never binds\nto a port, so `wait-on http://localhost:3000` was timing out and the\nplaywright job never actually ran (every E2E run on main has been\nred for the last week+).\n\nLaunch `.next/standalone/apps/office-ui/server.js` directly, the\nsame way the Dockerfile does. The standalone bundle excludes\n`.next/static` and `public/` (those live on a CDN in real prod), so\ncopy them into the standalone tree first. Setting HOSTNAME=0.0.0.0\nmatches Next''s standalone default and avoids any localhost-only\nbinding surprises on the runner.\n\nUnrelated build warning still present (`ReferenceError: location is\nnot defined` during static gen of /setup) — to be fixed separately;\nthe build still exits 0 and `/setup` isn''t on the e2e auth path.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* ci: trigger e2e workflow on its own changes\n\nWithout this, edits to .github/workflows/e2e.yml don''t fire the e2e\njob (the path filter only matched app/service/infra paths), so a CI\nfix can''t self-validate on the PR that introduces it. Adds the\nworkflow file itself to the path filter for both push and\npull_request triggers.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* ci: debug standalone output layout (temp)\n\n* ci: correct standalone output paths (no monorepo subtree)\n\nThe earlier attempt copied to .next/standalone/apps/office-ui/.next,\nbut Next 14 in this repo emits the standalone tree at the top of\n.next/standalone (server.js + .next/) rather than preserving the\napps/office-ui/ subtree. That happens because next.config.mjs does\nnot set outputFileTracingRoot, so Next does not detect the workspace\nroot.\n\nSame caveat applies to apps/office-ui/Dockerfile — its WORKDIR points\nat /app/apps/office-ui expecting server.js to land there. Worth a\nfollow-up; out of scope here.\n\nAlso drop the temporary debug listing step now that the layout is\nknown.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* ci: skip public/ copy when absent\n\napps/office-ui/public/ exists locally as an empty directory but git\ndoes not track empty dirs, so it is absent in CI checkouts. The cp\nwas failing with \"cannot stat ''public'': No such file or directory\".\nThe app serves favicon via the Next 14 metadata API, so an empty\npublic/ is fine.\n\napps/office-ui/Dockerfile has the same latent issue (copies public\nunconditionally) — flag for follow-up.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(office-ui): set outputFileTracingRoot for standalone in monorepo\n\nWithout outputFileTracingRoot, Next 14 in this workspace emits an\nincomplete standalone bundle: `.next/standalone/server.js` at the top,\nno node_modules/ alongside it. At start time the require-hook then\nresolves Next internals against the workspace''s hoisted\nnode_modules — and at least one file (./node-polyfill-crypto) is\nmissing there, so the server crashes before binding to a port. That\nis what was masking the E2E breakage as a \"wait-on timeout\".\n\nSetting outputFileTracingRoot to the workspace root (`../../` from\napps/office-ui/) makes Next trace and emit the standalone tree rooted\nat `.next/standalone/apps/office-ui/`, with a pruned node_modules/\nbeside it. This matches what apps/office-ui/Dockerfile already expects\n(its WORKDIR points at /app/apps/office-ui after copying standalone),\nso the production image starts working as a side benefit.\n\nThe e2e workflow''s start-server step is updated to the new layout.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* ci: re-add layout inspection (temp, debugging)\n\n* fix: nest outputFileTracingRoot under experimental for Next 14\n\nIn Next 14.2.5 the option lives at experimental.outputFileTracingRoot\n(it was promoted to top-level in Next 15). The previous commit set it\nat top level, which Next ignored with the warning:\n\n  ⚠ Unrecognized key(s) in object: ''outputFileTracingRoot''\n\nNet effect: the standalone bundle still shipped without node_modules\nand the server still crashed on missing internals. Move the option\nunder `experimental` so it actually applies. Revert the workflow\ncopy paths back to the flat .next/standalone/ layout (the option\nadds node_modules/ alongside server.js but does not introduce an\napps/office-ui/ subtree). Drop the temporary inspect step.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* ci: detect server.js path and create parent dirs (debug + adaptive)\n\n* ci: nohup+disown the server, capture and dump logs on failure\n\n* ci: probe with curl + switch wait-on to 127.0.0.1 (likely ::1 vs IPv4 issue)\n\n* ci: use TCP probe for server readiness; drop curl diagnostic\n\nThe HTTP probe was the actual blocker. The Office UI returns 307 on `/`\n(redirects unauthenticated users), and wait-on''s HTTP mode only resolves\non 2xx. A 60s timeout never resolves. Switched to a TCP probe that just\nverifies the listener is up — Playwright handles the actual page\nnavigation and any redirects.\n\nDrop the curl diagnostic step now that the cause is known. Keep the\non-failure log dump as it remains useful for any future regression.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJp/0znCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAlHYQAGSp9+ZVXVi9wxrQcFwoojf/\nm+h5O5zxEsSAkixrbm+wf/raClhemML+FIvOniOC+A9/RMwwhU3rwunCDGTF9iLg\nRIuZPFQvFddomw+kjAo9n81E6XMZV/hHbA+2qj/0yQaAXgvgTzDDBiZZppgP976u\nVzpQL23cMuEKucZB1or/KI46+BjG8ZcoPwpK+KXCmyD27SRnO8/9ZoYZaCVJ1Swl\n05ogvrVtsu1MpBmRj1os0zuSah/m69x19KfunEMiA1IwoKsTsJl8fbXOjcC738sT\nR+EYwkYAMhslEPAiBGqNtBYyFyuQDGuvL0Msw548NoR2Ul8JR6achRaodH0R23hf\nwWMe4333t52b8lRkdeINP7dCcPG/WZsttIh0LNEjf9eS/K168jPT8JH/+O22icQE\nfPEmRxSkBSnNxYLBQf0+eBlRq1zBJf0GdJPyy1Q0d5YKQwqdPeAq2E64pAQt+lzt\nawsO9HVm5wUyXBoICHpBbw9h9njPasxbd4gxHqril7kol7NfS+xQWTngxJ7HZuJi\np7XFA2I4lsCrUwVqHsqAMKFkQd/i87kRC2QOBuLSWTvYThNgaZNR7N+XJYhb7Ecw\nz3DTL8eLI+8Ifk1gMxI64EFjEEMDfWj00wmTUY6IvPrdL5eUteYpnvrsuYECpR3e\ns+UQhBDt4XASq0Agc0Xk\n=oHyw\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-05-09T15:04:08Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/urule-ai/urule/commit/6b7cab512cd6e1906b5af7ae27ba81a8e3c2d250","node_id":"C_kwDORxyz5NoAKDZiN2NhYjUxMmNkNmUxOTA2YjVhZjdhZTI3YmE4MWE4ZTNjMmQyNTA","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/urule-ai/urule/commit/0b165c675ca68232a052b038726c04e09fcbed2c","sha":"0b165c675ca68232a052b038726c04