node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY1NTY0NTI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/urule-ai/urule/commits/8500e88ea14b35c963201187bc2121153d79a23d/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-05T03:41:35Z","email":"richy@nimiq.com","name":"Richy"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-05T03:41:35Z","email":"richy@nimiq.com","name":"Richy"},"message":"feat(office-ui): mobile bottom navigation bar\n\nAdds a 5-item bottom nav (Home / Chat / Agents / Approve / More) shown\nbelow the lg: breakpoint. Desktop layout is untouched — sidebar stays.\nMain content gets pb-16 so the last row clears the bar; the status-bar\nWidgetZone is hidden on mobile (32px slice would fight the bottom nav\nfor the same thumb zone). Honours env(safe-area-inset-bottom) for iOS.\nActive-tab highlight echoes AppSidebar''s isActive() so the same route\nlights up the same item across both navs.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"d2f27cae84c34746fd23d23f67f6622515351dc3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/urule-ai/urule/git/trees/d2f27cae84c34746fd23d23f67f6622515351dc3"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/urule-ai/urule/git/commits/8500e88ea14b35c963201187bc2121153d79a23d","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6556452?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/PanoramicRum","id":6556452,"login":"PanoramicRum","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY1NTY0NTI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/urule-ai/urule/commit/8500e88ea14b35c963201187bc2121153d79a23d","node_id":"C_kwDORxyz5NoAKDg1MDBlODhlYTE0YjM1Yzk2MzIwMTE4N2JjMjEyMTE1M2Q3OWEyM2Q","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/urule-ai/urule/commit/141f15ab8c706619526fd5904e60f5014c4d707b","sha":"141f15ab8c706619526fd5904e60f5014c4d707b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/urule-ai/urule/commits/141f15ab8c706619526fd5904e60f5014c4d707b"}],"sha":"8500e88ea14b35c963201187bc2121153d79a23d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/urule-ai/urule/commits/8500e88ea14b35c963201187bc2121153d79a23d"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6556452?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/PanoramicRum","id":6556452,"login":"PanoramicRum","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY1NTY0NTI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/urule-ai/urule/commits/141f15ab8c706619526fd5904e60f5014c4d707b/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-05T03:22:48Z","email":"richy@nimiq.com","name":"Richy"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-05T03:22:48Z","email":"richy@nimiq.com","name":"Richy"},"message":"feat(office-ui): enforce 44px touch-target floor on coarse pointers\n\nWCAG 2.5.5 / Apple HIG / Material all recommend >=44x44 hit areas. The\nsite has many inline icon-only buttons sized via Tailwind h-8/h-10 that\nare fine with a mouse but cramped on a phone. Rather than auditing every\ncomponent, a single @media (pointer: coarse) layer in globals.css\napplies min-height/min-width: 44px to button, [role=\"button\"], and\na[role=\"button\"]. Desktop spacing is untouched (so toolbars stay dense\nand the 1.5-px scrollbar isn''t affected), and data-touch-exempt /\ndata-inline opt-outs cover the rare tightly-packed cases.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"2cbecd65a0cd4872f5a78802a5d9d0124aad4f57","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/urule-ai/urule/git/trees/2cbecd65a0cd4872f5a78802a5d9d0124aad4f57"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/urule-ai/urule/git/commits/141f15ab8c706619526fd5904e60f5014c4d707b","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6556452?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/PanoramicRum","id":6556452,"login":"PanoramicRum","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY1NTY0NTI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/urule-ai/urule/commit/141f15ab8c706619526fd5904e60f5014c4d707b","node_id":"C_kwDORxyz5NoAKDE0MWYxNWFiOGM3MDY2MTk1MjZmZDU5MDRlNjBmNTAxNGM0ZDcwN2I","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/urule-ai/urule/commit/f98d65551efa27a5a6f2eeae6764fb683c3a731d","sha":"f98d65551efa27a5a6f2eeae6764fb683c3a731d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/urule-ai/urule/commits/f98d65551efa27a5a6f2eeae6764fb683c3a731d"}],"sha":"141f15ab8c706619526fd5904e60f5014c4d707b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/urule-ai/urule/commits/141f15ab8c706619526fd5904e60f5014c4d707b"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6556452?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/PanoramicRum","id":6556452,"login":"PanoramicRum","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY1NTY0NTI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/urule-ai/urule/commits/f98d65551efa27a5a6f2eeae6764fb683c3a731d/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-05T03:21:21Z","email":"richy@nimiq.com","name":"Richy"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-05T03:21:21Z","email":"richy@nimiq.com","name":"Richy"},"message":"feat(office-ui): consistent 401/403 handling in axios interceptor\n\n403 (authenticated-but-unauthorised) was previously unhandled and bubbled\nraw to React Query callers. It now surfaces a toast via the existing\nuseToastStore — toast-and-stay is the consistent UX since redirecting an\nalready-authenticated user to /login on a permission denial is wrong.\n\n401 still triggers the refresh-token dance, but the redirect-to-login\npath goes through a redirectToLogin() guard that no-ops when the caller\nis already on /login, /register, or /forgot-password — those auth pages\nissue session-probe requests that 401 by design, and the prior code\nreload-looped them.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"2ce6bdecb9b94be2ca34e02191d268456d27a43f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/urule-ai/urule/git/trees/2ce6bdecb9b94be2ca34e02191d268456d27a43f"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/urule-ai/urule/git/commits/f98d65551efa27a5a6f2eeae6764fb683c3a731d","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6556452?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/PanoramicRum","id":6556452,"login":"PanoramicRum","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY1NTY0NTI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/urule-ai/urule/commit/f98d65551efa27a5a6f2eeae6764fb683c3a731d","node_id":"C_kwDORxyz5NoAKGY5OGQ2NTU1MWVmYTI3YTVhNmYyZWVhZTY3NjRmYjY4M2MzYTczMWQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/urule-ai/urule/commit/52fc9a42e3fe5b0de32b8f62eda7180c3d98cc94","sha":"52fc9a42e3fe5b0de32b8f62eda7180c3d98cc94","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/urule-ai/urule/commits/52fc9a42e3fe5b0de32b8f62eda7180c3d98cc94"}],"sha":"f98d65551efa27a5a6f2eeae6764fb683c3a731d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/urule-ai/urule/commits/f98d65551efa27a5a6f2eeae6764fb683c3a731d"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6556452?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/PanoramicRum","id":6556452,"login":"PanoramicRum","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY1NTY0NTI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/urule-ai/urule/commits/52fc9a42e3fe5b0de32b8f62eda7180c3d98cc94/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-05T03:15:55Z","email":"richy@nimiq.com","name":"Richy"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-05T03:15:55Z","email":"richy@nimiq.com","name":"Richy"},"message":"feat(packagehub): wire review-author authorisation cross-check\n\nCloses the explicit TODO left in §6.3 ratings/reviews. POST rejects with\n403 REVIEWER_MISMATCH when the body''s reviewerId doesn''t match the\nauthenticated user (anti-impersonation). PATCH and DELETE pre-fetch\nthe existing row and return 403 NOT_REVIEW_OWNER when the caller\ndidn''t write it — keeps \"exists but not yours\" distinct from \"no such\nreview\". 401 UNAUTHENTICATED on every mutating route when no user is\ndecorated. 3 new tests cover the new rejection paths; total reviews.test\ngoes from 13 to 16.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"971a098150a88b04f11c213583b4d56730aaf10b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/urule-ai/urule/git/trees/971a098150a88b04f11c213583b4d56730aaf10b"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/urule-ai/urule/git/commits/52fc9a42e3fe5b0de32b8f62eda7180c3d98cc94","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6556452?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/following{/othe