","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/urule-ai/urule/commits/7ac4448a8a6a99f195f7595c8dbc4d110a8c1ce2/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-05T03:00:32Z","email":"richy@nimiq.com","name":"Richy"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-05T03:00:32Z","email":"richy@nimiq.com","name":"Richy"},"message":"docs: flip §6.3 auto-update notifications box (follow-up to f1a1505a)\n\nShould have been in the previous commit but the ROADMAP edit was\nblocked by stale-read state. Squashing into a follow-up rather than\namending pushed history.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"71ca07643634b7c8131a239a79ca20e201f64ea5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/urule-ai/urule/git/trees/71ca07643634b7c8131a239a79ca20e201f64ea5"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/urule-ai/urule/git/commits/7ac4448a8a6a99f195f7595c8dbc4d110a8c1ce2","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6556452?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/PanoramicRum","id":6556452,"login":"PanoramicRum","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY1NTY0NTI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/urule-ai/urule/commit/7ac4448a8a6a99f195f7595c8dbc4d110a8c1ce2","node_id":"C_kwDORxyz5NoAKDdhYzQ0NDhhOGE2YTk5ZjE5NWY3NTk1YzhkYmM0ZDExMGE4YzFjZTI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/urule-ai/urule/commit/f1a1505a259a1b69bea607bc24f58a8a494565b3","sha":"f1a1505a259a1b69bea607bc24f58a8a494565b3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/urule-ai/urule/commits/f1a1505a259a1b69bea607bc24f58a8a494565b3"}],"sha":"7ac4448a8a6a99f195f7595c8dbc4d110a8c1ce2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/urule-ai/urule/commits/7ac4448a8a6a99f195f7595c8dbc4d110a8c1ce2"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6556452?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/PanoramicRum","id":6556452,"login":"PanoramicRum","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY1NTY0NTI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/urule-ai/urule/commits/f1a1505a259a1b69bea607bc24f58a8a494565b3/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-05T03:00:04Z","email":"richy@nimiq.com","name":"Richy"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-05T03:00:04Z","email":"richy@nimiq.com","name":"Richy"},"message":"feat(packages,events): close §6.3 auto-update notifications\n\nNEW NATS TOPIC.\n  packages/events: PACKAGE_TOPICS.UPDATE_AVAILABLE =\n  ''urule.packages.update.available''. Emitted (one event per outdated\n  installation) when a workspace''s /updates endpoint is polled and the\n  packages svc finds a newer non-yanked version published in\n  packagehub. office-ui consumes via the §3.5 notification center.\n\n  Payload: workspaceId, installationId, packageName, installedVersion,\n  latestVersion. Enough to deep-link a user to the upgrade flow.\n\nCHECK + EMIT.\n  PackageManager.checkUpdates(workspaceId) iterates each installation,\n  fetches the package''s versions list from packagehub via\n  fetchWithCorrelation (so §4.3 trace IDs flow through the cross-svc\n  hop), picks the latest non-yanked, and returns an outdated-set when\n  newer than installed.\n\n  Version comparison via a new compareVersions() helper:\n    - splits on ''.'', numeric per segment (''1.10'' > ''1.9'', not lex)\n    - missing patch defaults to 0 (''1.2'' === ''1.2.0'')\n    - pre-release (''-rc.1'') orders below the base; lexicographic on\n      the suffix when both have one\n\n  Floor implementation tracked alongside true semver-range matching\n  as a single ROADMAP follow-up (the dep-tree''s versionRange field\n  has the same forward-compat note).\n\n  GET /api/v1/workspaces/:wsId/updates returns\n  { workspaceId, updates, count } and fire-and-forget-publishes one\n  UPDATE_AVAILABLE per outdated installation. Doesn''t block the HTTP\n  response on NATS publish; logs at warn if publish fails.\n\n  packages svc optionally connects to NATS at boot (config.natsUrl).\n  Unreachable → service still boots; /updates skips the publish step\n  rather than failing the route. /updates returns the same JSON\n  shape either way so office-ui doesn''t need to handle a missing\n  side effect.\n\n  New @urule/events + nats deps in packages package.json.\n\nTESTS.\n  tests/auto-update.test.ts (12 new):\n    compareVersions:\n      - numeric vs lex segment ordering\n      - equal returns 0\n      - pre-release < base\n      - pre-release tag lex compare\n      - missing patch === 0\n    checkUpdates:\n      - empty for no installations\n      - empty when installed === latest\n      - flags outdated with correct latestVersion\n      - skips yanked latest, falls back to next non-yanked\n      - no downgrades (installed > latest published returns empty)\n      - transient packagehub failure → empty (no exception)\n      - only status=''installed'' considered (not failed/installing)\n\n  injectInstallationForTest() seam added to PackageManager so tests\n  can pre-populate state without exercising the install path\n  (entitlement check + manifest load).\n\n  Total packages tests: 43 → 55 (+12).\n\nROADMAP §6.3 auto-update bullet flipped. Open follow-ups remain:\nGitHub Sigstore OIDC, Stripe webhooks, persisted version history,\nkey rotation, marketplace UI, review-author auth check, true\nsemver-range resolution, frontend NATS subscriber for the §3.5\nnotification center.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"7e0f355c3b7bc60ce41296c07a34db40ea590712","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/urule-ai/urule/git/trees/7e0f355c3b7bc60ce41296c07a34db40ea590712"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/urule-ai/urule/git/commits/f1a1505a259a1b69bea607bc24f58a8a494565b3","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6556452?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/PanoramicRum","id":6556452,"login":"PanoramicRum","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY1NTY0NTI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/urule-ai/urule/commit/f1a1505a259a1b69bea607bc24f58a8a494565b3","node_id":"C_kwDORxyz5NoAKGYxYTE1MDVhMjU5YTFiNjliZWE2MDdiYzI0ZjU4YThhNDk0NTY1YjM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/urule-ai/urule/commit/96d99bf3b7d32b1f2c64e7bc0efe52d18ba22992","sha":"96d99bf3b7d32b1f2c64e7bc0efe52d18ba22992","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/urule-ai/urule/commits/96d99bf3b7d32b1f2c64e7bc0efe52d18ba22992"}],"sha":"f1a1505a259a1b69bea607bc24f58a8a494565b3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/urule-ai/urule/commits/f1a1505a259a1b69bea607bc24f58a8a494565b3"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6556452?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/PanoramicRum","id":6556452,"login":"PanoramicRum","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY1NTY0NTI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/urule-ai/urule/commits/96d99bf3b7d32b1f2c64e7bc0efe52d18ba22992/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-05T02:46:56Z","email":"richy@nimiq.com","name":"Richy"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-05T02:46:56Z","email":"richy@nimiq.com","name":"Richy"},"message":"feat(packagehub): close §6.3 dependency tree visualization\n\nConcrete §6.3 follow-up to ratings/reviews. Pure server-side recursive\nwalker over manifest.dependencies — no external infra, just SQL +\nin-memory recursion.\n\nSERVICE (services/dependency-tree.ts).\n  buildDependencyTree(db, name, version, options) → DependencyTreeNode\n    | null. Returns null for unknown root pkg/version; otherwise walks\n  recursively. Each node carries:\n    - name, versionRange (verbatim), resolvedVersion (latest non-yanked\n      match, or null)\n    - dependencies: child nodes, recursively\n    - unresolved?: ''missing'' | ''no_version'' | ''cycle'' | ''max_depth'' so\n      consumers can render unresolvable nodes differently\n\n  Cycle detection uses a per-path Set<string>. A node is only marked\n  ''cycle'' when it''s on its own ancestor chain — sibling-shared\n  transitive deps (root → a → shared, root → b → shared) resolve\n  fully under both branches. This is what users expect from a\n  dependency tree.\n\n  maxDepth cuts off pathological graphs (default 8, route allows\n  1..16). Default 8 covers all real-world graphs; 16 is the API\n  ceiling.\n\n  Resolution rule: latest non-yanked version per dependency. The\n  versionRange from the parent manifest is preserved verbatim so\n  consumers can see what was requested vs what was resolved. When\n  proper semver.satisfies range matching lands as a follow-up, only\n  this file changes — public contract unchanged.\n\nROUTE (routes/dependency-tree.routes.ts).\n  GET /api/v1/packages/:name/versions/:version/dependency-tree?maxDepth=N\n    400 on out-of-range maxDepth, 404 on unknown root. Returns the\n  full tree (single recursive JSON object).\n\nTESTS (tests/dependency-tree.test.ts).\n  9 new tests via a pure-TS reimplementation of the resolver loop\n  driven by an in-memory Map<name, PkgRecord>. Drives the same\n  decision logic verbatim — recursion + cycle + max-depth — without\n  reverse-engineering Drizzle''s predicate tree. Coverage:\n    - null when root pkg or version is missing\n    - leaf node when no deps\n    - one-level walk\n    - missing transitive → unresolved: missing\n    - yanked-only transitive → unresolved: no_version\n    - root↔child cycle → unresolved: cycle (only on path)\n    - sibling-shared dep → both resolve fully (NOT cycle)\n    - maxDepth=2 cuts off the 3rd level\n\nTotal packagehub tests: 48 → 57 (+9).\n\nROADMAP §6.3: dep tree bullet flipped. Open §6.3 follow-ups remain:\nGitHub Sigstore OIDC, Stripe webhooks, auto-update notifications,\npersisted version history, key rotation, marketplace UI, review-\nauthor auth check, true semver-range resolution.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"83fd2306893be4197192244ae9bb54180de70128","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/urule-ai/urule/git/trees/83fd2306893be4197192244ae9bb54180de70128"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/urule-ai/urule/git/commits/96d99bf3b7d32b1f2c64e7bc0efe52d18ba22992","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6556452?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/PanoramicRum","id":6556452,"login":"PanoramicRum","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY1NTY0NTI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/urule-ai/urule/commit/96d99bf3b7d32b1f2c64e7bc0efe52d18ba22992","node_id":"C_kwDORxyz5NoAKDk2ZDk5YmYzYjdkMzJiMWYyYzY0ZTdiYzBlZmU1MmQxOGJhMjI5OTI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/urule-ai/urule/commit/205f199cefa4cbd1da2addee3ad39cf850890d58","sha":"205f199cefa4cbd1da2addee3ad39cf850890d58","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/urule-ai/urule/commits/205f199cefa4cbd1da2addee3ad39cf850890d58"}],"sha":"96d99bf3b7d32b1f2c64e7bc0efe52d18ba22992","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/urule-ai/urule/commits/96d99bf3b7d32b1f2c64e7bc0efe52d18ba22992"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6556452?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/PanoramicRum","id":6556452,"login":"PanoramicRum","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY1NTY0NTI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/urule-ai/urule/commits/205f199cefa4cbd1da2addee3ad39cf850890d58/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-05T02:40:53Z","email":"richy@nimiq.com","name":"Richy"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-05T02:40:53Z","email":"richy@nimiq.com","name":"Richy"},"message":"docs: flip §6.3 ratings/reviews box (follow-up to 4c95a054)\n\nShould have been in the previous commit but the ROADMAP edit was\nblocked by stale-read state. Squashing into a follow-up rather than\namending pushed history.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"19c45c91bb5de51618478a147f0605c2f08053d2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/urule-ai/urule/git/trees/19c45c91bb5de51618478a147f0605c2f08053d2"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/urule-ai/urule/git/commits/205f199cefa4cbd1da2addee3ad39cf850890d58","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6556452?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/PanoramicRum","id":6556452,"login":"PanoramicRum","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY1NTY0NTI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/urule-ai/urule/commit/205f199cefa4cbd1da2addee3ad39cf850890d58","node_id":"C_kwDORxyz5NoAKDIwNWYxOTljZWZhNGNiZDFkYTJhZGRlZTNhZDM5Y2Y4NTA4OTBkNTg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/urule-ai/urule/commit/4c95a054a562933afc8f250d6dec5b415d192df4","sha":"4c95a054a562933afc8f250d6dec5b415d192df4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/urule-ai/urule/commits/4c95a054a562933afc8f250d6dec5b415d192df4"}],"sha":"205f199cefa4cbd1da2addee3ad39cf850890d58","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/urule-ai/urule/commits/205f199cefa4cbd1da2addee3ad39cf850890d58"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6556452?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/PanoramicRum","id":6556452,"login":"PanoramicRum","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY1NTY0NTI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/urule-ai/urule/commits/4c95a054a562933afc8f250d6dec5b415d192df4/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-05T02:40:26Z","email":"richy@nimiq.com","name":"Richy"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-05T02:40:26Z","email":"richy@nimiq.com","name":"Richy"},"message":"feat(packagehub): close §6.3 ratings + reviews\n\nConcrete §6.3 follow-up to the signing/marketplace work — adds package\nratings + written reviews with one row per (package, reviewer).\n\nSCHEMA (db/schema/reviews.ts).\n  package_reviews: id ULID + packageId FK ON DELETE CASCADE + reviewerId\n  + rating int (1-5) + title ≤200 + body ≤10K (default '''') + optional\n  version + timestamps. UNIQUE(packageId, reviewerId) blocks duplicate\n  submissions at the database level so concurrent POSTs can''t race\n  past the application check.\n\n  Drizzle migration 0003_reviews.sql generated. Index on packageId\n  for the most common query (listing per package); UNIQUE doubles as\n  the per-reviewer lookup index.\n\nROUTES (routes/reviews.routes.ts).\n  GET    /api/v1/packages/:name/reviews\n    Newest-first pagination (limit ≤100 + offset) + optional\n    reviewerId filter for \"my reviews\" views. Returns\n      { reviews: [...], summary: {averageRating, reviewCount},\n        pagination: {limit, offset} }\n    Aggregate computed via SQL AVG()::float + COUNT()::int — no\n    cached materialised view, runs on every read which is fine until\n    a package has many thousands of reviews.\n\n  POST   /api/v1/packages/:name/reviews\n    Zod-validated body. 404 for unknown package, 409 REVIEW_EXISTS on\n    UNIQUE-constraint violation pointing the caller at PATCH.\n\n  PATCH  /api/v1/packages/:name/reviews/:reviewId\n    Partial update; 400 if no fields provided (Zod refine).\n    updatedAt bumped automatically.\n\n  DELETE /api/v1/packages/:name/reviews/:reviewId\n    204 on success, 404 if no row matches both pkg + review id.\n\n  Authorisation TODO (request.uruleUser.id == reviewerId on\n  PATCH/DELETE) noted in route comments — auth-middleware already\n  decorates request.uruleUser; today''s floor accepts any authenticated\n  reviewerId so a follow-up commit can wire the cross-check without\n  API changes.\n\nTESTS (tests/reviews.test.ts).\n  13 new tests covering:\n    - validation: missing reviewerId, out-of-range rating, empty title,\n      oversized title, empty PATCH body\n    - 404 paths: unknown package, missing review row\n    - happy paths: POST 201, PATCH 200, DELETE 204\n    - duplicate-reviewer 409 dispatch (regex match on the unique-\n      constraint error message text from postgres)\n\n  Mock-Drizzle pattern matches §6.2''s agent-endpoints test — chain\n  proxy returns predictable arrays/aggregates by select-call ordering\n  so we can simulate package-found vs missing without a real DB.\n\nTotal packagehub tests: 35 → 48 (+13).\n\nROADMAP §6.3: ratings/reviews bullet flipped. Open follow-ups remain:\nGitHub Sigstore OIDC, Stripe/Lemonsqueezy webhooks, dep tree, auto-\nupdate notifications, persisted version history, key rotation,\nmarketplace UI in office-ui.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"a451867b307f4824f5cff86ea4a8420f125c9eb6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/urule-ai/urule/git/trees/a451867b307f4824f5cff86ea4a8420f125c9eb6"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/urule-ai/urule/git/commits/4c95a054a562933afc8f250d6dec5b415d192df4","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6556452?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/PanoramicRum","id":6556452,"login":"PanoramicRum","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY1NTY0NTI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/urule-ai/urule/commit/4c95a054a562933afc8f250d6dec5b415d192df4","node_id":"C_kwDORxyz5NoAKDRjOTVhMDU0YTU2MjkzM2FmYzhmMjUwZDZkZWM1YjQxNWQxOTJkZjQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/urule-ai/urule/commit/48c19a01f4ac3c926d3f69ec1264c010dc9b2ce0","sha":"48c19a01f4ac3c926d3f69ec1264c010dc9b2ce0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/urule-ai/urule/commits/48c19a01f4ac3c926d3f69ec1264c010dc9b2ce0"}],"sha":"4c95a054a562933afc8f250d6dec5b415d192df4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/urule-ai/urule/commits/4c95a054a562933afc8f250d6dec5b415d192df4"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6556452?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/PanoramicRum","id":6556452,"login":"PanoramicRum","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY1NTY0NTI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/urule-ai/urule/commits/48c19a01f4ac3c926d3f69ec1264c010dc9b2ce0/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-05T02:24:36Z","email":"richy@nimiq.com","name":"Richy"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-05T02:24:36Z","email":"richy@nimiq.com","name":"Richy"},"message":"docs: flip §3.5 notification center box (follow-up to 6da44239)\n\nShould have been in the previous commit but the ROADMAP edit was\nblocked by stale-read state. Squashing into a follow-up rather than\namending pushed history.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"0445c499d3276ebc65c962f63f635d2fea628cf3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/urule-ai/urule/git/trees/0445c499d3276ebc65c962f63f635d2fea628cf3"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/urule-ai/urule/git/commits/48c19a01f4ac3c926d3f69ec1264c010dc9b2ce0","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6556452?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/PanoramicRum","id":6556452,"login":"PanoramicRum","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY1NTY0NTI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/urule-ai/urule/commit/48c19a01f4ac3c926d3f69ec1264c010dc9b2ce0","node_id":"C_kwDORxyz5NoAKDQ4YzE5YTAxZjRhYzNjOTI2ZDNmNjllYzEyNjRjMDEwZGM5YjJjZTA","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/urule-ai/urule/commit/6da44239b8400b02d782546ad8058d2a1a366db4","sha":"6da44239b8400b02d782546ad8058d2a1a366db4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/urule-ai/urule/commits/6da44239b8400b02d782546ad8058d2a1a366db4"}],"sha":"48c19a01f4ac3c926d3f69ec1264c010dc9b2ce0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/urule-ai/urule/commits/48c19a01f4ac3c926d3f69ec1264c010dc9b2ce0"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6556452?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/PanoramicRum","id":6556452,"login":"PanoramicRum","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY1NTY0NTI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/urule-ai/urule/commits/6da44239b8400b02d782546ad8058d2a1a366db4/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-05T02:23:21Z","email":"richy@nimiq.com","name":"Richy"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-05T02:23:21Z","email":"richy@nimiq.com","name":"Richy"},"message":"feat(office-ui): close §3.5 notification center — bell, panel, capture\n\nNOTIFICATION CENTER (§3.5).\n  store/useNotificationCenterStore.ts: zustand+persist, namespace\n  urule-notification-center. Per entry: id, kind, title, body?,\n  createdAt, read, href?, source?. Capped at 100 entries to keep\n  localStorage bounded — newest-first, oldest pruned on overflow.\n  Actions: add/markRead/markAllRead/remove/clear/setOpen/toggle +\n  unreadCount selector.\n\n  components/layout/NotificationCenter.tsx: popover anchored to a bell\n  button (NotificationBell exported alongside). Mounted globally in\n  office/layout.tsx; fixed to top-right under the header. List items\n  show kind icon + title + truncated body + relative timestamp + unread\n  dot. Click marks read and routes to href if set. Hover reveals a\n  per-entry dismiss button. Top-bar mark-all-read + clear-all actions.\n  Outside-click + Escape close. ARIA: role=\"dialog\" aria-modal=\"false\"\n  with proper labelling; bell button reflects open state via\n  aria-expanded and surfaces unread count via aria-label.\n\n  hooks/useNotificationCapture.ts: subscribes to useToastStore (same\n  pattern as useNotificationSounds) and mirrors every new toast into\n  the center. Toasts are ephemeral (auto-dismiss after a few seconds);\n  the center keeps the history. Wired in office/layout.tsx.\n\n  AppHeader''s stub bell button replaced with <NotificationBell>.\n  Unread badge with 99+ overflow.\n\nPLAYWRIGHT (e2e/notification-center.spec.ts).\n  Journey 10: bell visibility, click toggles panel, Escape closes,\n  empty state, programmatically-seeded notification renders + badge,\n  clear-all empties the list. 5 specs across 2 sub-journeys.\n\nTotal Playwright surface: 17 → 18 spec files.\n\nDEFERRED with rationale in ROADMAP:\n  - WebSocket-pushed approval events. The store accepts href deep-links\n    + source: ''approval'' so the data shape is ready. Needs a backend\n    push channel — either langgraph-adapter''s WS extended OR a fresh\n    notifications service that subscribes to urule.approvals.* NATS\n    topics. Defer until concrete user pull; today''s polling-based\n    approval queue UX is fine for the demo flow.\n\n§3.5 score: 2/3 (was 1/3). Total cross-§3 open: §3.1 retry buttons,\n§3.2 screen-reader QA, §3.3 SSO/email-verify (both Keycloak-blocked),\n§3.5 WS approvals.\n\nNo new npm dependencies.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"f0cfad1da6685b6270a0d6157afc005486c633c7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/urule-ai/urule/git/trees/f0cfad1da6685b6270a0d6157afc005486c633c7"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/urule-ai/urule/git/commits/6da44239b8400b02d782546ad8058d2a1a366db4","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6556452?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/PanoramicRum","id":6556452,"login":"PanoramicRum","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY1NTY0NTI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/urule-ai/urule/commit/6da44239b8400b02d782546ad8058d2a1a366db4","node_id":"C_kwDORxyz5NoAKDZkYTQ0MjM5Yjg0MDBiMDJkNzgyNTQ2YWQ4MDU4ZDJhMWEzNjZkYjQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/urule-ai/urule/commit/fdcf2c33ca335e813cece5b2d0ed9b5402107357","sha":"fdcf2c33ca335e813cece5b2d0ed9b5402107357","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/urule-ai/urule/commits/fdcf2c33ca335e813cece5b2d0ed9b5402107357"}],"sha":"6da44239b8400b02d782546ad8058d2a1a366db4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/urule-ai/urule/commits/6da44239b8400b02d782546ad8058d2a1a366db4"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6556452?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/PanoramicRum","id":6556452,"login":"PanoramicRum","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY1NTY0NTI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/urule-ai/urule/commits/fdcf2c33ca335e813cece5b2d0ed9b5402107357/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-05T01:28:11Z","email":"richy@nimiq.com","name":"Richy"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-05T01:28:11Z","email":"richy@nimiq.com","name":"Richy"},"message":"feat(office-ui): close 3 of §3.x — offline banner + confirm dialog + focus trap\n\nOFFLINE DETECTION (§3.1).\n  hooks/useOnlineStatus.ts: subscribes to window ''online''/''offline''\n  events PLUS a 5s navigator.onLine poll fallback for browsers that\n  miss events (notably Safari toggling Wi-Fi). Visibility-aware so\n  polling stops when the tab is hidden.\n\n  components/layout/OfflineBanner.tsx: sticky top banner with\n  role=\"status\" aria-live=\"polite\" so screen readers announce the\n  state change without being intrusive. Slides in/out via CSS\n  transform; data-online attribute + test-id for Playwright. Mounted\n  once in the office layout.\n\nLOGOUT CONFIRMATION (§3.3).\n  components/ui/ConfirmDialog.tsx: modal with title + description +\n  cancel/confirm buttons. Configurable variant (''default'' or\n  ''destructive'' — destructive paints confirm red). Escape cancels;\n  Tab cycles between the two buttons (inline two-button focus trap);\n  backdrop-click cancels; autofocus on confirm so a quick Enter\n  accepts the default action.\n\n  Wired into the Cmd+K palette''s \"Sign out\" command. Instead of\n  immediate logout, opens the destructive confirm. The dialog lives\n  outside the palette''s open-gate so dismissing the palette while\n  the confirm is up doesn''t lose the confirmation. Reusable for\n  future destructive actions (delete agent, uninstall package, revoke\n  entitlement).\n\nKEYBOARD NAVIGATION (§3.2).\n  lib/focusTrap.ts: reusable utility that installs a Tab/Shift+Tab\n  handler bouncing focus inside a container''s focusable descendants\n  in DOM order. Modal components opt in via useEffect; useful for\n  any future modal with > 2 focusable elements (filter forms,\n  multi-step wizards). Two-button modals like ConfirmDialog inline\n  their own trap for simplicity.\n\nDEFERRED with rationale in ROADMAP:\n  - Retry buttons on failed fetches: needs an audit of every React\n    Query hook + each list page''s error state. Defer until all the\n    §6.x data-fetching surfaces have stabilised.\n  - Screen-reader testing (VoiceOver/NVDA): manual QA.\n  - SSO/OAuth + email verification: blocked on Keycloak realm\n    config + SMTP relay, out of scope for a frontend-only iteration.\n\n§3.x score: §3.1 → 5/6 (was 4/6), §3.2 → 6/8 (was 5/8 — kept\n\"screen reader test\" open), §3.3 → 4/6 (was 3/6).\n\nTotal office-ui surface: +5 new files (1 hook, 1 layout component,\n1 UI primitive, 1 lib helper, plus the existing CommandPalette\nedit). No new npm dependencies.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"cc64cb9d1cc42e03ef9c0db7d6f8dfd73c6302e7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/urule-ai/urule/git/trees/cc64cb9d1cc42e03ef9c0db7d6f8dfd73c6302e7"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/urule-ai/urule/git/commits/fdcf2c33ca335e813cece5b2d0ed9b5402107357","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6556452?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/PanoramicRum","id":6556452,"login":"PanoramicRum","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY1NTY0NTI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/PanoramicRum","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/urule-ai/urule/commit/fdcf2c33ca335e813cece5b2d0ed9b5402107357","node_id":"C_kwDORxyz5NoAKGZkY2YyYzMzY2EzMzVlODEzY2VjZTViMmQwZWQ5YjU0MDIxMDczNTc","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/urule-ai/urule/commit/0bbe6fa7508ddd86abf08d064bff9be90be89e79","sha":"0bbe6fa7508ddd86abf08d064bff9be90be89e79","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/urule-ai/urule/commits/0bbe6fa7508ddd86abf08d064bff9be90be89e79"}],"sha":"fdcf2c33ca335e813cece5b2d0ed9b5402107357","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/urule-ai/urule/commits/fdcf2c33ca335e813cece5b2d0ed9b5402107357"}],"requestUrl":"https://api.github.com/repos/urule-ai/urule/commits?per_page=100&page=1&sha=5b517017074d2c7de61094762ef1c4418e1e7c88&since=2025-03-31T23%3A59%3A59.000Z&until=2026-10-08T15%3A58%3A33.655Z"}');
