ers/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Carasent-ASMA/asma-qiankun-react-loader/commit/0c396568da1faffd68380e0a011cfb590a63fa57","node_id":"C_kwDORx1NT9oAKDBjMzk2NTY4ZGExZmFmZmQ2ODM4MGUwYTAxMWNmYjU5MGE2M2ZhNTc","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Carasent-ASMA/asma-qiankun-react-loader/commit/46e43b8b64425c3227e868b8d30882dd1531cc54","sha":"46e43b8b64425c3227e868b8d30882dd1531cc54","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Carasent-ASMA/asma-qiankun-react-loader/commits/46e43b8b64425c3227e868b8d30882dd1531cc54"}],"sha":"0c396568da1faffd68380e0a011cfb590a63fa57","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Carasent-ASMA/asma-qiankun-react-loader/commits/0c396568da1faffd68380e0a011cfb590a63fa57"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/118059335?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nikeedw/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nikeedw/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nikeedw/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nikeedw/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/nikeedw","id":118059335,"login":"nikeedw","node_id":"U_kgDOBwlxRw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nikeedw/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nikeedw/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nikeedw/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nikeedw/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nikeedw/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/nikeedw","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Carasent-ASMA/asma-qiankun-react-loader/commits/46e43b8b64425c3227e868b8d30882dd1531cc54/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-16T19:54:24Z","email":"118059335+nikeedw@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Nicolaev Eduard"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-16T19:54:24Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"ASMA-7866: self-heal a dead override on the qiankun path (#7)\n\nfeat(loader-queue): ASMA-7866 self-heal a dead override on the qiankun path\n\nWidgets that still mount through qiankun never reach EsmWidgetHost, so the\nself-heal shipped in asma-mfw-esmloader#5 does not cover them. When a pinned\n`pr<N>` preview is deleted on merge (ASMA-7863) those widgets fail on every\nload with no way for the tester to recover, since nothing brings the version\nback and the override outlives it.\n\nThe transport gate''s existing widgets.json probe cannot answer this. The CDN is\nthe object store itself and answers 403 for ANY key it does not hold — verified\nagainst the dev origin, which returns 403 AccessDenied for every path under a\nprefix that does not exist — and a healthy published qiankun version has no\nwidgets.json either. The two cases are identical on that path. The entry\ndocument is the discriminator: only a live version serves it, and it is also\nprecisely what qiankun is about to fetch.\n\nHealing requires proof of absence, never unreachability: 404/403 only. A 5xx, a\ntimeout or a network failure leaves the override alone, and a localhost\noverride is exempt outright because a dev server that is not running is\nrecoverable by starting it — silently discarding that setting would be hostile.\nSelf-terminating, since the disabled list removes the override from the next\nresolution, and the reload fires once however many widgets race into it.\n\nThe record is written under the same key asma-mfw-esmloader uses, so a host\nreads either transport''s heal with one consumeOverrideSelfHeal() call. The keys\nand the local-base rule are duplicated rather than imported, as this package\nmust stay free of an asma-mfw-esmloader dependency (see esmTransport.ts); a\ntest pins the shared key literal so a rename on either side breaks rather than\nsilently losing the message.\n\nAdds the first tests this package has had: 13 passing, tsc clean, 7 mutants\nkilled — treating any 4xx/5xx as gone, dropping the localhost exemption,\ndropping the one-shot reload guard, overwriting the disabled list, healing on a\nnetwork failure, leaving no record for the host, and probing widgets.json\ninstead of the entry.","tree":{"sha":"58d5eb94ba3cad68494ba0118346eb0077ec2dcd","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Carasent-ASMA/asma-qiankun-react-loader/git/trees/58d5eb94ba3cad68494ba0118346eb0077ec2dcd"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Carasent-ASMA/asma-qiankun-react-loader/git/commits/46e43b8b64425c3227e868b8d30882dd1531cc54","verification":{"payload":"tree 58d5eb94ba3cad68494ba0118346eb0077ec2dcd\nparent 69d8abee49a5417a3aab433de78e02c755bc6952\nauthor Nicolaev Eduard <118059335+nikeedw@users.noreply.github.com> 1786910064 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1786910064 +0300\n\nASMA-7866: self-heal a dead override on the qiankun path (#7)\n\nfeat(loader-queue): ASMA-7866 self-heal a dead override on the qiankun path\n\nWidgets that still mount through qiankun never reach EsmWidgetHost, so the\nself-heal shipped in asma-mfw-esmloader#5 does not cover them. When a pinned\n`pr<N>` preview is deleted on merge (ASMA-7863) those widgets fail on every\nload with no way for the tester to recover, since nothing brings the version\nback and the override outlives it.\n\nThe transport gate''s existing widgets.json probe cannot answer this. The CDN is\nthe object store itself and answers 403 for ANY key it does not hold — verified\nagainst the dev origin, which returns 403 AccessDenied for every path under a\nprefix that does not exist — and a healthy published qiankun version has no\nwidgets.json either. The two cases are identical on that path. The entry\ndocument is the discriminator: only a live version serves it, and it is also\nprecisely what qiankun is about to fetch.\n\nHealing requires proof of absence, never unreachability: 404/403 only. A 5xx, a\ntimeout or a network failure leaves the override alone, and a localhost\noverride is exempt outright because a dev server that is not running is\nrecoverable by starting it — silently discarding that setting would be hostile.\nSelf-terminating, since the disabled list removes the override from the next\nresolution, and the reload fires once however many widgets race into it.\n\nThe record is written under the same key asma-mfw-esmloader uses, so a host\nreads either transport''s heal with one consumeOverrideSelfHeal() call. The keys\nand the local-base rule are duplicated rather than imported, as this package\nmust stay free of an asma-mfw-esmloader dependency (see esmTransport.ts); a\ntest pins the shared key literal so a rename on either side breaks rather than\nsilently losing the message.\n\nAdds the first tests this package has had: 13 passing, tsc clean, 7 mutants\nkilled — treating any 4xx/5xx as gone, dropping the localhost exemption,\ndropping the one-shot reload guard, overwriting the disabled list, healing on a\nnetwork failure, leaving no record for the host, and probing widgets.json\ninstead of the entry.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqghVwCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA43oQABl7r7Zw5XG/HVoh8G8ei6J7\nyW+tq0C3UPpYhn82uqzvj6+8HaqaqkyXYRCjvaFu+Xj7rMRgO/a89brHfO9hA48N\no4VhlQYN/hwPG5OL2ZYyukiy/22xRvl/8D/t+BnzWwn017sMNzcvT/Q8w1rewtuQ\nA1rWMTIZEf7kZ7HOcaQKrOjBp5EPP0kJOneZVkli9RHsDZXFTFAtJNL/8lJ+MiyF\nMb8lPurMDjankbp28nukqI/noq0QKVVCnXhS4OYwkNX1WxprCal9h8tVS8hADppF\nftPeqcD7sbdJQ0WYubwoubJqS3YRSvYzEqXoRci9AGSUd1Av+8w4Inuc8+AWyREA\nF7LcKWy071hJQgSasjL+ZnVe4/UIZOE/J1sYt9w6rs1se0GVjjZXLhMxSHnuG/WJ\njVbbgpe5i7CBzGdMilmuTvAhX6KR07k9FXttz/GaAoETwGvnLT6PbF+bgO2Sxwyt\nSfKtJYoIZD5IYiHqB2+OLRzqcLWnFavuh8csn8HMFzp2nP9tVtJrcEXcIigHfK7n\nvS1QgbYbRN2xIjBr6fwidOVWeEsWWxx0xwhrvV+RJaFiRI7o+AfltsQ7PI1r72YT\nZqmJTs/u5+/4c/bDkZQZ5nub+YbzqY69dSHEV/DdML