s://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/hexplus/sibujs/commit/9e141afc2e67452dc24fc03f9f81c7081d277644","node_id":"C_kwDORx-O9toAKDllMTQxYWZjMmU2NzQ1MmRjMjRmYzAzZjlmODFjNzA4MWQyNzc2NDQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/hexplus/sibujs/commit/eaf68f37cf41368bdf817724e6997dea28a4571d","sha":"eaf68f37cf41368bdf817724e6997dea28a4571d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/hexplus/sibujs/commits/eaf68f37cf41368bdf817724e6997dea28a4571d"}],"sha":"9e141afc2e67452dc24fc03f9f81c7081d277644","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/hexplus/sibujs/commits/9e141afc2e67452dc24fc03f9f81c7081d277644"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3751819?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hexplus/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hexplus/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hexplus/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hexplus/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/hexplus","id":3751819,"login":"hexplus","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM3NTE4MTk=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hexplus/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hexplus/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hexplus/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hexplus/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hexplus/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/hexplus","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/hexplus/sibujs/commits/eaf68f37cf41368bdf817724e6997dea28a4571d/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-25T16:08:28Z","email":"jframonge@gmail.com","name":"Jose Ramírez"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-25T16:08:28Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Improvements (#45)\n\n* fix(lifecycle): dispose DOM subtrees removed via native DOM APIs\n\neach(), Suspense, and ErrorBoundary each removed SibuJS-owned DOM through a\npath that bypassed disposal, leaving orphaned subtrees subscribed and still\nupdating off-screen.\n\n- each(): the anchor now tears down its whole logical range. Rows and the\n  each:end sentinel are siblings of the anchor, so an ancestor dispose() walk\n  never reached them — swapping an each() out of a conditional left every row\n  visible on screen and still reactive.\n- Suspense/lazy(): commits route through replaceChildrenSafely(), disposing\n  the outgoing fallback rather than orphaning it via native replaceChildren().\n- ErrorBoundary: a disposed boundary now refuses (and disposes) late async\n  results instead of committing them into a detached container.\n\nAdds replaceChildrenSafely() to the disposal module, 78 regression tests, and\narchitecture docs for the DOM ownership model. Corrects a README claim that\ncontradicted each()''s documented LIS diffing.\n\n* fix(dispose): preserve incoming nodes nested inside outgoing subtrees","tree":{"sha":"0826fb0704f53dd886a180b7e9f5ed1d21ddec44","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/hexplus/sibujs/git/trees/0826fb0704f53dd886a180b7e9f5ed1d21ddec44"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/hexplus/sibujs/git/commits/eaf68f37cf41368bdf817724e6997dea28a4571d","verification":{"payload":"tree 0826fb0704f53dd886a180b7e9f5ed1d21ddec44\nparent 80df1f2273ffbd29c9d028920a595fe207093d63\nauthor Jose Ramírez <jframonge@gmail.com> 1787674108 -0600\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1787674108 -0600\n\nImprovements (#45)\n\n* fix(lifecycle): dispose DOM subtrees removed via native DOM APIs\n\neach(), Suspense, and ErrorBoundary each removed SibuJS-owned DOM through a\npath that bypassed disposal, leaving orphaned subtrees subscribed and still\nupdating off-screen.\n\n- each(): the anchor now tears down its whole logical range. Rows and the\n  each:end sentinel are siblings of the anchor, so an ancestor dispose() walk\n  never reached them — swapping an each() out of a conditional left every row\n  visible on screen and still reactive.\n- Suspense/lazy(): commits route through replaceChildrenSafely(), disposing\n  the outgoing fallback rather than orphaning it via native replaceChildren().\n- ErrorBoundary: a disposed boundary now refuses (and disposes) late async\n  results instead of committing them into a detached container.\n\nAdds replaceChildrenSafely() to the disposal module, 78 regression tests, and\narchitecture docs for the DOM ownership model. Corrects a README claim that\ncontradicted each()''s documented LIS diffing.\n\n* fix(dispose): preserve incoming nodes nested inside outgoing subtrees","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqjb38CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAry4QAKVKen+4Xyk2MDFTBclu62qR\nQKKcliKoHwVlpLKmadxjVEiVD9DUBnyHFm13xnkhWFpHUHVK5H18M5AR2BK66z9z\nKfVCfI61NY7MqPJ2awmTFvrjqLzSj1U/PuEbq1Mu/iNjdXqPFlr8Lx/tic1wd8nX\ntH//j7YzmyE5QhcsDipT+v3711wJZRpeDkvaAbAzLJa6FcTLKdZ4SrorZvDp7hoi\nI65FG8pOgpcMIJZCHxLjf/Fr8u85wxqtCF2nHrLn+B6e6AGo7x/Dks2nrqCh6vZT\nbWcJ9GIBL0e/IrtSknuQKxhneT6IdQ+DUO3mWjmyrJK4ovh3/CUq4+Zpb/yyOzmC\nig5uB5PGpw6ppdldEeKl2nMv9UxglVy9a90jVmK3J3E1Um8vXzCzk83xWOswEXsS\ntSy2LpTAgBYWB9H1LrnXI9EzHLT/egT7af83qL5Hm4wGvZGyKG3npHVq4typtSYR\nXMTlEubVHnDvpGFmhC6cbfS9RHIzzn+0PiFi9UXmOzUTBzQ6/9lTowZvhWWubroY\nv0IH3jQPUll16AScVgfdb9IS/oM3tcbsrauQ1u3kVRvO/YpjgOaiQyMgeCdB3xCV\nADn2EqLgQ+Qz6yp7f7vTPK4NHMu7WTohVSDaSGJHJvU1/SFnH6ZTo/kOk/JP26fq\nDo10dOAJLtQOaZz0JdZW\n=tl0L\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-25T16:08:28Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.c